1
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:29,569
Man : THEY CALLED THEM " THE HAUNTED SHORES , "

2
00:01:29,669 --> 00:01:32,970
THESE STRETCHES OF DEVONSHIRE AND CORNWALL AND IRELAND ,

3
00:01:33,406 --> 00:01:35,441
WHICH REAR UP AGAINST THE WESTWARD OCEAN .

4
00:01:35,541 --> 00:01:38,709
MISTS GATHER HERE , AND SEA FOG , AND EERIE STORIES .

5
00:01:40,980 --> 00:01:43,248
THAT 'S NOT BECAUSE THERE ARE MORE GHOSTS HERE

6
00:01:43,348 --> 00:01:44,950
THAN IN OTHER PLACES , MIND YOU ,

7
00:01:45,050 --> 00:01:48,652
IT 'S JUST THAT PEOPLE WHO LIVE HEREABOUTS ARE STRANGELY AWARE OF THEM .

8
00:01:49,521 --> 00:01:52,522
YOU SEE , DAY AND NIGHT , YEAR IN , YEAR OUT ,

9
00:01:52,658 --> 00:01:55,561
THEY LISTEN TO THE POUND AND STIR OF THE WAVES .

10
00:01:55,661 --> 00:01:58,728
THERE 'S LIFE AND DEATH IN THAT RESTLESS SOUND ,

11
00:01:59,465 --> 00:02:01,233
AND ETERNITY TOO .

12
00:02:01,333 --> 00:02:03,402
IF YOU LISTEN TO IT LONG ENOUGH ,

13
00:02:03,502 --> 00:02:05,437
ALL YOUR SENSES ARE SHARPENED .

14
00:02:05,537 --> 00:02:07,406
YOU COME BY STRANGE INSTINCTS .

15
00:02:07,506 --> 00:02:10,406
YOU GET TO RECOGNIZE A PECULIAR COLD ,

16
00:02:10,508 --> 00:02:11,877
WHICH IS THE FIRST WARNING .

17
00:02:11,977 --> 00:02:15,244
THE COLD WHICH IS NO MERE MATTER OF DEGREES FAHRENHEIT ,

18
00:02:15,679 --> 00:02:20,149
BUT A DRAINING OF WARMTH IN THE VITAL CENTERS OF THE LIVING .

19
00:02:20,384 --> 00:02:22,954
LOCAL PEOPLE TELL ME THEY WOULD HAVE FELT IT ,

20
00:02:23,054 --> 00:02:25,423
EVEN OUTSIDE THAT LOCKED DOOR .

21
00:02:25,523 --> 00:02:26,191
WE DIDN 'T .

22
00:02:26,291 --> 00:02:28,893
THEY CAN 'T UNDERSTAND WHY WE DIDN 'T KNOW WHAT IT MEANT

23
00:02:28,993 --> 00:02:30,995
WHEN OUR DOG WOULDN 'T GO UP THOSE STAIRS .

24
00:02:31,095 --> 00:02:34,129
ANIMALS SEE THE BLASTED THINGS , IT APPEARS .

25
00:02:35,265 --> 00:02:38,567
MY SISTER PAMELA AND I KNEW NOTHING ABOUT SUCH MATTERS- -

26
00:02:39,369 --> 00:02:40,605
NOT THEN , WE DIDN 'T .

27
00:02:40,705 --> 00:02:42,773
WE HAD THE DISADVANTAGE OF BEING LONDONERS ,

28
00:02:42,873 --> 00:02:44,975
JUST DOWN FOR A FORTNIGHT 'S REST .

29
00:02:45,075 --> 00:02:47,909
THAT 10TH DAY OF MAY , 1937 ,

30
00:02:48,112 --> 00:02:50,879
WAS THE END OF OUR HOLIDAY .

31
00:02:54,318 --> 00:02:56,684
( barking )

32
00:03:01,924 --> 00:03:04,293
WE SEEM TO BE IN SOMEBODY 'S GARDEN .

33
00:03:04,393 --> 00:03:06,796
WHAT WAS SOMEBODY 'S GARDEN .

34
00:03:06,896 --> 00:03:08,632
WHAT A MARVELOUS OLD HOUSE .

35
00:03:08,732 --> 00:03:11,333
BETTER GET OUT BEFORE WE 'RE HAD UP FOR TRESPASSING .

36
00:03:11,433 --> 00:03:13,335
WHERE ON EARTH DID WE LEAVE THE CAR ?

37
00:03:13,435 --> 00:03:16,103
THAT DIRECTION , I THINK .

38
00:03:25,781 --> 00:03:28,349
LOOK , A SQUIRREL .

39
00:03:28,450 --> 00:03:31,752
- Man : GRAB BOBBY ! - TOO LATE ! BOBBY , COME BACK HERE !

40
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:33,455
( barks )

41
00:03:33,555 --> 00:03:35,323
Pam : YOU BAD DOG !

42
00:03:35,423 --> 00:03:37,691
BOBBY !

43
00:03:43,598 --> 00:03:45,533
RICK , HE 'S GOT THE POOR LITTLE SQUIRREL TRAPPED .

44
00:03:45,633 --> 00:03:47,435
- HE 'LL KILL IT . - MY DEAR SWEET SISTER ,

45
00:03:47,535 --> 00:03:50,603
IT 'S MORE LIKELY HE 'S HAVING HIS WAY WITH OUR BOBBY .

46
00:03:52,407 --> 00:03:54,774
( barking )

47
00:03:56,076 --> 00:03:59,278
Rick : FINE WAY TO SPEND A HOLIDAY- - CHASING A DOG !

48
00:04:05,219 --> 00:04:07,586
( barking )

49
00:04:09,023 --> 00:04:12,090
- Pam : WHERE IS HE ? - Rick : UNDER HERE , I THINK .

50
00:04:14,061 --> 00:04:15,095
OWW !

51
00:04:15,195 --> 00:04:16,430
I THOUGHT YOU HAD HIM .

52
00:04:16,530 --> 00:04:19,333
HAD ME . THERE HE GOES ! HANG ON TO BOBBY !

53
00:04:19,433 --> 00:04:21,733
I CAN 'T !

54
00:04:24,271 --> 00:04:26,571
( barks )

55
00:04:29,309 --> 00:04:31,545
Rick : WELL PLAYED , SIR .

56
00:04:31,645 --> 00:04:33,313
( barks )

57
00:04:33,413 --> 00:04:36,948
- DO YOU SUPPOSE HE CAN GET OUT ? - CERTAINLY . HE 'S ON THE ROOF BY NOW .

58
00:04:39,285 --> 00:04:40,854
THAT 'S A SMART DOG .

59
00:04:40,954 --> 00:04:42,721
HE 'LL BE BACK ANY MINUTE .

60
00:04:42,821 --> 00:04:44,357
RICK , HAVE YOU NOTICED ANYTHING ?

61
00:04:44,457 --> 00:04:47,093
ONLY THAT I 'M IN NO SHAPE TO JOIN THE HUNTING SET .

62
00:04:47,193 --> 00:04:48,828
NO , I MEAN THIS HOUSE .

63
00:04:48,928 --> 00:04:51,729
IT 'S THE LOVELIEST THING I EVER SAW .

64
00:04:53,266 --> 00:04:54,767
LOOK AT THAT STAIRCASE .

65
00:04:54,867 --> 00:04:57,302
OH , BOY , WHAT BANISTERS FOR SLIDING .

66
00:04:57,402 --> 00:04:59,104
- OH , RICK . - WHAT IS IT ?

67
00:04:59,204 --> 00:05:02,439
YOUR SAYING THAT , AND THE HOUSE- - IT TOOK ME BACK .

68
00:05:03,175 --> 00:05:06,276
- YEAH , IT 'S QUITE A BIT LIKE- - - THE ROSE BOWL THERE ,

69
00:05:06,545 --> 00:05:08,246
THE GRANDFATHER CLOCK THERE ,

70
00:05:08,346 --> 00:05:10,382
AND MOTHER IN HER BEST GRAY MOIRE

71
00:05:10,482 --> 00:05:11,817
SWEEPING DOWN THE STAIRS .

72
00:05:11,917 --> 00:05:14,052
YOU 'LL BE HOWLING IN A MINUTE . COME ON OUT .

73
00:05:14,152 --> 00:05:16,155
NOT ON YOUR LIFE . I 'M GOING TO SEE THE REST OF THIS .

74
00:05:16,255 --> 00:05:18,657
COME ON , RICK , LET 'S PRETEND WE 'RE BUYING IT .

75
00:05:18,757 --> 00:05:21,125
I 'LL TOSS YOU FOR THE BEDROOM WITH THE BEST VIEW .

76
00:05:21,225 --> 00:05:23,993
THEY 'VE ALL GOT BEST VIEWS .

77
00:05:25,497 --> 00:05:26,531
HOW LOVELY .

78
00:05:26,631 --> 00:05:28,600
WHY DOES IT MAKE ME FEEL LIKE I 'M ON A BOAT ?

79
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:31,102
IT 'S THE LIGHT ON THE CEILING . THAT 'S THE SEA .

80
00:05:31,202 --> 00:05:32,770
IT 'S NICE TO WAKE UP AND SEE THAT .

81
00:05:32,870 --> 00:05:35,106
OH , HOW I DO HATE LIVING IN A LONDON FLAT .

82
00:05:35,206 --> 00:05:37,541
I SUPPOSE IF YOU 'RE BROUGHT UP IN AN OLD HOUSE ,

83
00:05:37,641 --> 00:05:39,477
YOU ALWAYS HANKER FOR ONE .

84
00:05:39,577 --> 00:05:42,211
IT 'S STUCK . YOU TRY IT .

85
00:05:44,181 --> 00:05:47,216
IT 'S LOCKED . FAMILY SKELETONS , PROBABLY .

86
00:05:47,418 --> 00:05:49,119
OH , WHAT A BORE .

87
00:05:49,219 --> 00:05:51,820
RICK , THE BATHROOM .

88
00:05:53,957 --> 00:05:56,359
OPEN FIRE WHILE YOU BATHE .

89
00:05:56,459 --> 00:05:58,061
WHAT LUXURY .

90
00:05:58,161 --> 00:05:59,062
( chuckles )

91
00:05:59,162 --> 00:06:01,498
YOU KNOW , THIS IS A SATURDAY-NIGHT-ONLY BATHROOM .

92
00:06:01,598 --> 00:06:03,533
YOU BOIL YOURSELF AS RED AS A LOBSTER

93
00:06:03,633 --> 00:06:05,769
THEN HURRY TO BED TO AVOID A CHILL .

94
00:06:05,869 --> 00:06:07,670
- RICK . - WHAT ?

95
00:06:07,770 --> 00:06:09,506
I 'VE HAD ONE OF MY " FEELINGS . "

96
00:06:09,606 --> 00:06:11,107
WE 'RE REALLY GOING TO BUY THIS HOUSE .

97
00:06:11,207 --> 00:06:14,575
OH , YES ? DID YOUR FEELING TELL YOU WHAT YOU 'RE GOING TO BUY IT WITH ?

98
00:06:14,677 --> 00:06:17,112
WELL , IF WE BOTH PUT IN EVERYTHING WE HAVE ,

99
00:06:17,212 --> 00:06:18,515
MAYBE WE CAN GET IT .

100
00:06:18,615 --> 00:06:20,082
IT 'S TERRIBLY OUT OF THE WAY ,

101
00:06:20,182 --> 00:06:22,117
AND IT HASN 'T BEEN LIVED IN FOR YEARS .

102
00:06:22,217 --> 00:06:23,486
WHAT WOULD WE DO WITH IT ?

103
00:06:23,586 --> 00:06:24,220
WE CAN 'T DRIVE NEARLY 300 MILES

104
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:25,821
JUST FOR WEEKENDS .

105
00:06:25,921 --> 00:06:29,089
WE 'LL LIVE HERE ALL THE TIME AND YOU 'LL WORK AT YOUR MUSIC .

106
00:06:29,591 --> 00:06:32,592
MY POOR , LUNATIC SISTER , I HAPPEN TO HAVE A JOB .

107
00:06:32,795 --> 00:06:34,797
AND WHAT A JOB- - GOING TO CONCERTS ,

108
00:06:34,897 --> 00:06:37,233
AND TELLING YOUR READERS HOW BAD THE MUSIC WAS .

109
00:06:37,333 --> 00:06:38,734
IT 'S NOT GOOD ENOUGH , RICK .

110
00:06:38,834 --> 00:06:39,401
CHUCK IT . DOWN HERE , YOU 'D

111
00:06:39,501 --> 00:06:41,203
WRITE YOUR OWN MUSIC ,

112
00:06:41,303 --> 00:06:44,571
AS YOU ALWAYS SHOULD HAVE DONE , AND AS YOU 'VE ALWAYS WANTED TO .

113
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:47,974
RICK , IT ISN 'T AS IF YOU WERE EVEN A GOOD MUSIC CRITIC .

114
00:06:48,644 --> 00:06:50,379
THANK YOU , VERY MUCH .

115
00:06:50,479 --> 00:06:51,980
ANYWAY , I GET PAID HARD CASH .

116
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:55,014
BUT DOESN 'T THE IDEA ATTRACT YOU AT ALL ?

117
00:06:55,183 --> 00:06:56,184
ATTRACT ME ?

118
00:06:56,284 --> 00:06:58,687
YOU COME OUT OF HERE , YOU 'RE DANGEROUS .

119
00:06:58,787 --> 00:07:01,821
DON 'T YOU KNOW HOW RARE HOUSES LIKE THIS ARE ?

120
00:07:02,423 --> 00:07:04,025
I LIKE THE BANISTERS .

121
00:07:04,125 --> 00:07:05,894
HOW LIZZIE WOULD LOVE THAT KITCHEN .

122
00:07:05,994 --> 00:07:07,795
THAT LITTLE BEACH MUST BELONG TO IT .

123
00:07:07,895 --> 00:07:09,797
IT 'S IN GOOD CONDITION TOO , NOT A SIGN OF DAMP .

124
00:07:09,897 --> 00:07:13,167
- WE 'LL GET OUR FURNITURE OUT OF STORAGE . - NOW BE CALM , PAMELA .

125
00:07:13,267 --> 00:07:15,236
A CHANGE LIKE THIS WOULD HAVE TO BE DISCUSSED .

126
00:07:15,336 --> 00:07:18,571
OH , NONSENSE . IMPORTANT DECISIONS HAVE TO BE MADE QUICKLY .

127
00:07:19,039 --> 00:07:19,940
WELL ...

128
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:21,742
MY PAPER HAS ASKED ME TO DO A SERIES- -

129
00:07:21,842 --> 00:07:24,044
" LIVES OF THE GREAT MUSICIANS- - " READING TIME , TWO MINUTES .

130
00:07:24,144 --> 00:07:27,579
- THERE YOU ARE , THAT WILL FEED US . - UNTIL I RUN OUT OF MUSICIANS .

131
00:07:27,981 --> 00:07:29,883
HOW DO WE KNOW THIS PLACE IS FOR SALE ?

132
00:07:29,983 --> 00:07:32,252
RICK , LIFE ISN 'T AS CRUEL AS THAT .

133
00:07:32,352 --> 00:07:34,819
IT 'S GOT TO BE .

134
00:07:42,061 --> 00:07:44,163
NOW REMEMBER , PAM , NO SIGNS OF KEENNESS .

135
00:07:44,263 --> 00:07:47,164
WE 'RE JUST MILDLY INTERESTED . MILDLY .

136
00:07:47,266 --> 00:07:49,500
SHH .

137
00:07:49,702 --> 00:07:50,470
GOOD AFTERNOON .

138
00:07:50,570 --> 00:07:53,573
Rick : WE 'D LIKE TO SEE COMMANDER BEECH IF WE MAY .

139
00:07:53,673 --> 00:07:55,541
HE 'S NOT IN AT THE MOMENT .

140
00:07:55,641 --> 00:07:57,643
COULD WE WAIT FOR HIM ?

141
00:07:57,743 --> 00:08:00,177
WON 'T YOU COME IN ?

142
00:08:08,587 --> 00:08:10,289
THERE 'S A FIRE IN THE STUDY .

143
00:08:10,389 --> 00:08:13,390
I THINK I CAN CATCH MY GRANDFATHER BY TELEPHONE .

144
00:08:16,762 --> 00:08:18,597
WHO SHALL I SAY WANTS TO SEE HIM ?

145
00:08:18,697 --> 00:08:20,533
HE WOULDN 'T KNOW OUR NAME . IT 'S FITZGERALD .

146
00:08:20,633 --> 00:08:23,800
MY SISTER PAMELA FITZGERALD AND I 'M RODERICK FITZGERALD .

147
00:08:24,202 --> 00:08:26,970
HOW DO YOU DO ? I 'M STELLA MEREDITH .

148
00:08:27,072 --> 00:08:28,774
WON 'T YOU SIT DOWN ?

149
00:08:28,874 --> 00:08:30,308
THANK YOU .

150
00:08:30,408 --> 00:08:32,143
NOT IN THAT CHAIR !

151
00:08:32,243 --> 00:08:34,312
IT 'S GOT A LUMPY SEAT .

152
00:08:34,412 --> 00:08:35,547
OH .

153
00:08:35,647 --> 00:08:38,347
- DO YOU MIND ? - OH , NO .

154
00:08:40,250 --> 00:08:43,152
- OH , DEAR . WILL THIS DO ? - THANK YOU .

155
00:08:43,588 --> 00:08:45,490
WHAT AN AWFULLY UNSMOKING HOUSE .

156
00:08:45,590 --> 00:08:48,659
GRANDFATHER HAD A CIGAR BLOWN STRAIGHT DOWN HIS THROAT ONCE

157
00:08:48,759 --> 00:08:51,994
WHEN HE WAS ON THE FOREDECK . HE LOST HIS TASTE FOR TOBACCO .

158
00:08:54,098 --> 00:08:55,299
CAN I HELP IN ANY WAY ?

159
00:08:55,399 --> 00:08:58,502
WE WANTED TO TALK TO THE COMMANDER ABOUT A HOUSE HE OWNS

160
00:08:58,602 --> 00:09:00,571
ON TOP OF THE CLIFF .

161
00:09:00,671 --> 00:09:01,939
- WINDWARD ? - YES .

162
00:09:02,039 --> 00:09:05,042
YOU SEE , WE 'VE FALLEN HEAD OVER HEELS IN LOVE WITH- -

163
00:09:05,142 --> 00:09:07,876
I MEAN , IT MIGHT JUST DO FOR US .

164
00:09:08,077 --> 00:09:08,579
REALLY ?

165
00:09:08,679 --> 00:09:11,815
Rick : WE UNDERSTAND FROM MRS. BROWN AT THE INN IT 'S FOR SALE .

166
00:09:11,915 --> 00:09:13,116
MRS. BROWN IS MISTAKEN .

167
00:09:13,216 --> 00:09:15,985
I 'M SORRY YOU 'VE BEEN PUT TO THE TROUBLE OF COMING HERE .

168
00:09:16,085 --> 00:09:19,022
PERHAPS IF WE COULD SPEAK TO YOUR GRANDFATHER ABOUT IT ?

169
00:09:19,122 --> 00:09:20,691
IT WOULDN 'T BE THE SLIGHTEST USE .

170
00:09:20,791 --> 00:09:23,693
I 'M SORRY , BUT THERE 'S REALLY NO POINT IN YOUR WAITING .

171
00:09:23,793 --> 00:09:26,527
Man : STELLA , ARE YOU THERE ?

172
00:09:27,663 --> 00:09:29,565
YES , GRANDFATHER .

173
00:09:29,665 --> 00:09:31,965
IN HERE .

174
00:09:37,473 --> 00:09:38,741
WELL , WHAT IS IT ?

175
00:09:38,841 --> 00:09:41,677
SOME PEOPLE WHO CAME HERE BY MISTAKE , GRANDFATHER .

176
00:09:41,777 --> 00:09:42,911
THEY 'RE JUST LEAVING .

177
00:09:43,011 --> 00:09:45,715
WE HEARD THE WINDWARD HOUSE IS FOR SALE .

178
00:09:45,815 --> 00:09:47,182
YES , IT IS .

179
00:09:47,282 --> 00:09:49,852
WON 'T YOU SIT DOWN ? I 'LL BE WITH YOU IN A MOMENT .

180
00:09:49,952 --> 00:09:52,820
Pam : THANK YOU , VERY MUCH .

181
00:09:56,691 --> 00:09:57,859
GRANDFATHER , PLEASE .

182
00:09:57,959 --> 00:10:01,194
I THOUGHT I MADE MYSELF QUITE CLEAR ON THIS POINT , STELLA .

183
00:10:01,463 --> 00:10:02,964
YES , GRANDFATHER ...

184
00:10:03,064 --> 00:10:04,432
I DON 'T UNDERSTAND YOU .

185
00:10:04,532 --> 00:10:07,001
A HOUSE YOU HAVEN 'T LIVED IN SINCE YOU WERE A CHILD .

186
00:10:07,101 --> 00:10:09,671
A PIECE OF PROPERTY WE CAN 'T AFFORD TO MAINTAIN .

187
00:10:09,771 --> 00:10:12,472
BUT IT WAS MY MOTHER 'S HOUSE ...

188
00:10:12,574 --> 00:10:14,676
I CAN 'T PUT IT INTO WORDS , IT 'S- -

189
00:10:14,776 --> 00:10:16,077
NONSENSE .

190
00:10:16,177 --> 00:10:18,778
GRANDFATHER , PLEASE .

191
00:10:37,197 --> 00:10:40,100
I DON 'T BELIEVE MANY REPAIRS WILL BE NECESSARY .

192
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:41,368
THE ROOF IS SOUND ,

193
00:10:41,468 --> 00:10:44,803
THE WALLS HAVE WITHSTOOD THE ATLANTIC GALES FOR TWO CENTURIES .

194
00:10:45,205 --> 00:10:46,439
- THANK YOU . - THANK YOU .

195
00:10:46,539 --> 00:10:47,073
THERE WAS A CONSIDERABLE SUM

196
00:10:47,173 --> 00:10:49,941
SPENT ON THE HOUSE 20 YEARS AGO ,

197
00:10:50,110 --> 00:10:52,512
WHEN I GAVE IT TO MY DAUGHTER .

198
00:10:52,612 --> 00:10:54,414
Rick : I UNDERSTAND .

199
00:10:54,514 --> 00:10:55,782
WELL , I 'M SORRY ,

200
00:10:55,882 --> 00:10:58,618
BUT I 'M AFRAID # 1200 IS OUR ABSOLUTE LIMIT .

201
00:10:58,718 --> 00:11:01,552
- IS THAT A DEFINITE OFFER ? - YES .

202
00:11:01,687 --> 00:11:04,324
AND YOU WOULD PAY THE ENTIRE SUM IMMEDIATELY ?

203
00:11:04,424 --> 00:11:06,992
Rick : YOU MEAN , YOU 'D SELL FOR THAT ?

204
00:11:07,092 --> 00:11:09,295
YES .

205
00:11:09,395 --> 00:11:12,663
I SUPPOSE YOU OUGHT TO HAVE THE PROPERTY SURVEYED BEFORE- -

206
00:11:12,999 --> 00:11:13,800
OH , RICK .

207
00:11:13,900 --> 00:11:15,634
THERE 'S NO NEED TO GET SUSPICIOUS .

208
00:11:15,734 --> 00:11:18,003
THE HOUSE IS WORTH FAR MORE THAN THAT ,

209
00:11:18,103 --> 00:11:20,406
BUT I HAVE A VERY YOUNG GRANDDAUGHTER ,

210
00:11:20,506 --> 00:11:22,374
AND # 1200 IN THE BANK FOR HER

211
00:11:22,474 --> 00:11:24,176
WOULD EASE MY MIND CONSIDERABLY .

212
00:11:24,276 --> 00:11:26,845
Pam : WE UNDERSTAND PERFECTLY .

213
00:11:26,945 --> 00:11:30,046
AND YOU WOULD NOT BE NERVOUS IN SUCH A LONELY HOUSE ?

214
00:11:30,148 --> 00:11:31,350
NO , INDEED .

215
00:11:31,450 --> 00:11:33,151
OR OF THE WIND AT NIGHTS ?

216
00:11:33,251 --> 00:11:35,086
IT PLAYS ODD TRICKS IN OLD HOUSES .

217
00:11:35,186 --> 00:11:37,589
ARE YOU TRYING TO TELL US THE HOUSE IS HAUNTED ?

218
00:11:37,689 --> 00:11:40,623
NO , MISS FITZGERALD , NO HOUSE IS HAUNTED .

219
00:11:40,992 --> 00:11:44,260
BUT I HAD SOME TENANTS FIVE YEARS AGO WHO COMPLAINED OF ...

220
00:11:45,063 --> 00:11:45,797
DISTURBANCES .

221
00:11:45,897 --> 00:11:49,398
WHAT WAS THE TROUBLE- - LADIES CARRYING THEIR HEADS UNDER THEIR ARMS ?

222
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:52,270
I DECLINED TO DISCUSS IT AND CANCELLED THE LEASE .

223
00:11:52,370 --> 00:11:55,104
BUT I COULDN 'T CANCEL A SALE .

224
00:11:55,306 --> 00:11:56,441
WE WOULDN 'T WANT YOU TO .

225
00:11:56,541 --> 00:11:59,677
OF COURSE , ONE DOES FEEL THAT A STORY LIKE THAT SHOULD BRING THE PRICE DOWN .

226
00:11:59,777 --> 00:12:03,211
I 'VE ALREADY MADE A VERY CONSIDERABLE REDUCTION , MR. FITZGERALD .

227
00:12:03,681 --> 00:12:06,584
PERHAPS WE BOTH NEED TIME TO THINK THE MATTER OVER .

228
00:12:06,684 --> 00:12:08,753
BUT OUR OFFER 'S DEFINITE . ISN 'T IT , RICK ?

229
00:12:08,853 --> 00:12:11,954
- OH , YES , YES . - VERY WELL , THEN . I ACCEPT IT .

230
00:12:12,957 --> 00:12:16,391
Beech : TITLE DEEDS AND CHECKS WILL BE EXCHANGED BY OUR SOLICITORS .

231
00:12:16,927 --> 00:12:19,263
IN THE MEANTIME , I HAVE YOUR WORD

232
00:12:19,363 --> 00:12:21,829
AND YOU HAVE MINE .

233
00:12:23,300 --> 00:12:26,434
IT 'S WONDERFULLY SIMPLE TO BUY A HOUSE , ISN 'T IT ?

234
00:12:29,339 --> 00:12:31,341
- ( barking ) - PAM , WHERE ARE YOU ?

235
00:12:31,441 --> 00:12:34,208
HERE I AM . LOOK , OUR OWN ROSES .

236
00:12:39,515 --> 00:12:42,449
RICK , IT 'S ALL OURS . ISN 'T IT WONDERFUL ?

237
00:12:42,852 --> 00:12:44,954
HMM . YOU KNOW , IT 'S BIGGER THAN I THOUGHT .

238
00:12:45,054 --> 00:12:47,356
I CAN 'T WAIT TO SEE WHAT 'S IN THAT BLUEBEARD ROOM .

239
00:12:47,456 --> 00:12:49,458
PROBABLY THE HOUSEMAID 'S CUPBOARD- -

240
00:12:49,558 --> 00:12:52,061
SLOPS , MOPS , DRIPPING TAPS .

241
00:12:52,161 --> 00:12:54,730
I WONDER HOW SOON WE CAN GET CLEANERS AND PAINTERS IN ?

242
00:12:54,830 --> 00:12:57,599
YOU 'LL GO BACK TO LONDON , OF COURSE , WHILE I STAY HERE .

243
00:12:57,699 --> 00:12:59,568
WHAT , ROLLED UP IN A BLANKET LIKE A SQUAW ?

244
00:12:59,668 --> 00:13:02,736
AT THE INN , IDIOT , UNTIL YOU SHIP ME THE FURNITURE .

245
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:08,310
DID THE OLD BOY TELL YOU WHY IT WAS LOCKED ?

246
00:13:08,410 --> 00:13:11,177
I NEVER THOUGHT TO ASK HIM .

247
00:13:16,484 --> 00:13:18,653
WELL , NOW WE KNOW .

248
00:13:18,753 --> 00:13:21,423
IT 'S THE ONE UGLY ROOM IN THE HOUSE .

249
00:13:21,523 --> 00:13:23,090
OH , IT 'S NOT SO BAD .

250
00:13:23,190 --> 00:13:25,626
BUT THAT WINDOW , IT 'S LIKE A CUCUMBER FRAME .

251
00:13:25,726 --> 00:13:28,396
THEY PUT THAT IN LATER TO MAKE A PAINTER 'S STUDIO .

252
00:13:28,496 --> 00:13:31,131
EVEN THE VIEW DOESN 'T CHEER IT UP .

253
00:13:31,231 --> 00:13:32,733
WHAT WILL WE DO WITH IT ?

254
00:13:32,833 --> 00:13:35,169
WHAT ? MY WORKROOM , OF COURSE . IT 'S IDEAL .

255
00:13:35,269 --> 00:13:37,271
PUT THE PIANO OVER THERE WITH SHELVES FOR MUSIC ,

256
00:13:37,371 --> 00:13:40,772
PLENTY OF SPACE TO WALK UP AND DOWN , MANUSCRIPTS ALL OVER THE FLOOR ,

257
00:13:40,875 --> 00:13:42,809
HOT PINCERS TO TEAR THE FLESH FROM PEOPLE

258
00:13:42,909 --> 00:13:44,744
WHO KEEP TELLING ME LUNCHEON IS READY ,

259
00:13:44,844 --> 00:13:47,114
STACKS OF CHECKS FROM MY PUBLISHERS AND- -

260
00:13:47,214 --> 00:13:49,948
DO YOU THINK THIS ROOM IS DAMP ?

261
00:13:50,350 --> 00:13:51,818
IT NEEDS AIRING .

262
00:13:51,918 --> 00:13:53,987
IT 'S FUNNY IT SHOULD STRIKE SO COLD

263
00:13:54,087 --> 00:13:56,189
IN HERE AFTER SUCH A WARM DAY .

264
00:13:56,289 --> 00:13:58,525
- OH , LAW . - WHAT , RICK ?

265
00:13:58,625 --> 00:14:01,560
I SUDDENLY FELT COMPLETELY FLATTENED .

266
00:14:01,995 --> 00:14:05,463
DO YOU SUPPOSE I 'LL EVER BE ABLE TO WRITE ANY MUSIC HERE OR ANYWHERE ?

267
00:14:05,932 --> 00:14:08,001
WHAT ON EARTH ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT ?

268
00:14:08,101 --> 00:14:11,502
YOU DON 'T SUPPOSE WE 'VE MADE THE MOST HOWLING MISTAKE , DO YOU ?

269
00:14:12,205 --> 00:14:13,506
OH , RICK , HAVE WE ?

270
00:14:13,606 --> 00:14:16,675
WHY DID THE COMMANDER SUDDENLY COME DOWN ON HIS PRICE LIKE THAT ?

271
00:14:16,775 --> 00:14:19,479
THE " DISTURBANCES . " RUMORS LIKE THAT ARE DYNAMITE

272
00:14:19,579 --> 00:14:20,846
IF YOU 'RE SELLING A PLACE .

273
00:14:20,946 --> 00:14:24,317
PAMELA , YOU 'RE NOT GOING TO GET SCARED OF THIS GHOST BUSINESS , ARE YOU ?

274
00:14:24,417 --> 00:14:27,651
OF COURSE NOT . I DON 'T BELIEVE IN THEM REALLY ,

275
00:14:27,753 --> 00:14:30,887
AND I 'D BE INTERESTED , NOT SCARED . WOULDN 'T YOU ?

276
00:14:31,356 --> 00:14:34,059
ME ? NO , DISTURBANCES WOULDN 'T DISTURB ME ,

277
00:14:34,159 --> 00:14:35,895
NOT FOR A SINGLE SECOND .

278
00:14:35,995 --> 00:14:38,428
( dog howling )

279
00:14:38,597 --> 00:14:39,631
WHY , IT 'S BOBBY .

280
00:14:39,731 --> 00:14:42,167
OF COURSE , IT 'S BOBBY . DON 'T GO GETTING IMAGINATIVE .

281
00:14:42,267 --> 00:14:45,602
- ( dog whining ) - IT IS A FILTHY ROOM , ISN 'T IT ?

282
00:14:46,605 --> 00:14:48,039
( dog barks )

283
00:14:48,139 --> 00:14:49,408
Pam : WE 'RE HERE , BOBBY .

284
00:14:49,508 --> 00:14:52,076
Rick : HE 'S TRYING TO TELL US ABOUT THE SQUIRREL , I EXPECT .

285
00:14:52,176 --> 00:14:55,013
WHAT 'S THE MATTER ? DIDN 'T HE KEEP HIS DATE WITH YOU , BOBBY ?

286
00:14:55,113 --> 00:14:58,147
Pam : WHY DON 'T YOU COME UP , STUPID ?

287
00:14:59,216 --> 00:15:01,753
RICK , LOOK AT THAT LAMB OF A WINDOW !

288
00:15:01,853 --> 00:15:04,820
NEVER THOUGHT BOBBY WAS A KILLER AT HEART .

289
00:15:06,991 --> 00:15:08,659
WHO 'S THAT STANDING OUT THERE ?

290
00:15:08,759 --> 00:15:11,760
LOOKS LIKE THE OLD BOY 'S GRANDDAUGHTER .

291
00:15:16,333 --> 00:15:18,101
OH , DON 'T WASTE A WAVE ON THAT ONE .

292
00:15:18,201 --> 00:15:20,438
BECAUSE SHE DIDN 'T WANT US TO BUY THE HOUSE ?

293
00:15:20,538 --> 00:15:22,773
OH , RICK , I THINK SHE 'D BEEN CRYING .

294
00:15:22,873 --> 00:15:24,542
- HAD SHE ? - DON 'T YOU SEE ?

295
00:15:24,642 --> 00:15:27,609
SHE ADORED THE HOUSE , AND WE 'VE CAST HER OUT .

296
00:15:28,178 --> 00:15:29,046
ISN 'T IT AWFUL ?

297
00:15:29,146 --> 00:15:31,181
STOP MAKING UP STORIES . SHE DIDN 'T LIVE HERE .

298
00:15:31,281 --> 00:15:34,717
SHE JUST DOESN 'T WANT US TO . SHE 'S AN ILL-MANNERED LITTLE DOG-IN-THE-MANGER .

299
00:15:34,817 --> 00:15:36,920
- ( dog barking ) - ALL RIGHT , BOBBY , ALL RIGHT .

300
00:15:37,020 --> 00:15:40,023
WE 'LL TAKE YOU BACK TO THE INN AND LET YOU ORDER YOUR DINNER .

301
00:15:40,123 --> 00:15:43,023
- HAVE YOU FORGOTTEN SOMETHING ? - UH-HUH .

302
00:15:47,196 --> 00:15:48,197
NO .

303
00:15:48,297 --> 00:15:50,933
ON SECOND THOUGHT , MY LANDING GEAR

304
00:15:51,033 --> 00:15:53,734
ISN 'T WHAT IT USED TO BE .

305
00:16:23,164 --> 00:16:25,564
( bell rings )

306
00:16:27,035 --> 00:16:28,603
- MORNING , SIR . - MORNING .

307
00:16:28,703 --> 00:16:31,537
- 20 TURRETS , PLEASE . - YES , SIR .

308
00:16:33,374 --> 00:16:35,209
- ISN 'T THIS WINDWARD HOUSE ? - YES , SIR .

309
00:16:35,309 --> 00:16:38,677
A FINE HOUSE TOO . GLAD TO HEAR THERE 'LL BE FOLK IN IT AGAIN .

310
00:16:39,012 --> 00:16:42,047
- YOU HAVE A DOZEN OF THESE ? - LIKELY , I HAVE .

311
00:16:43,718 --> 00:16:46,354
OH , MAYBE YOU 'RE THE NEW OWNER .

312
00:16:46,454 --> 00:16:48,355
YES , MY SISTER AND I BOUGHT THE PLACE YESTERDAY .

313
00:16:48,455 --> 00:16:51,690
WELL , WELL . I HOPE YOU 'LL BRING IT BACK TO ITSELF AGAIN .

314
00:16:51,892 --> 00:16:55,026
THE LAST LOT THAT LIVED THERE WEREN 'T NO GOOD .

315
00:16:55,229 --> 00:16:56,764
WENT AWAY OWING MONEY .

316
00:16:56,864 --> 00:17:00,232
GOT OUT OF THEIR LEASE STARTING UGLY STORIES ABOUT THE PLACE .

317
00:17:00,900 --> 00:17:02,869
SO THAT 'S HOW THE RUMORS STARTED .

318
00:17:02,969 --> 00:17:04,171
THAT 'S WHAT I DO SAY .

319
00:17:04,271 --> 00:17:06,473
HERE YOU ARE , SIR . NINE SEEMS TO BE ALL I HAVE .

320
00:17:06,573 --> 00:17:10,141
- THAT 'S ALL RIGHT . - OF COURSE , THERE ARE OTHERS WHO SAY DIFFERENT .

321
00:17:10,577 --> 00:17:12,812
- THERE ARE ? - THAT 'S ONLY NATURAL ,

322
00:17:12,912 --> 00:17:15,946
AFTER THE WAY THE LADY OF WINDWARD HOUSE DIED .

323
00:17:16,415 --> 00:17:17,884
GOD REST HER SOUL .

324
00:17:17,984 --> 00:17:19,486
YOU MEAN THE COMMANDER 'S DAUGHTER ?

325
00:17:19,586 --> 00:17:22,887
ONLY CHILD . IT CAME NEAR BREAKING THE GENTLEMAN 'S HEART .

326
00:17:23,256 --> 00:17:24,991
HE 'S NEVER BEEN THE SAME SINCE .

327
00:17:25,091 --> 00:17:27,626
- HOW DID SHE DIE ? - FELL OFF THE CLIFF .

328
00:17:27,726 --> 00:17:30,229
- ACCIDENT ? - THAT 'S WHAT I 'D HAVE SAID .

329
00:17:30,329 --> 00:17:32,298
GOOD MORNING , MR. HARDY .

330
00:17:32,398 --> 00:17:34,467
A COPY OF AMATEUR GARDENING , PLEASE .

331
00:17:34,567 --> 00:17:37,669
YES , MRS. COATESWORTHY . THE BEST OF LUCK TO YOU , SIR .

332
00:17:37,769 --> 00:17:41,237
IF YOU HAVE A FAVORITE TOBACCO , I 'LL BE GLAD TO STOCK IT FOR YOU .

333
00:17:41,773 --> 00:17:43,008
THANK YOU . GOODBYE .

334
00:17:43,108 --> 00:17:46,042
THE GENT THAT JUST BOUGHT WINDWARD HOUSE .

335
00:17:46,178 --> 00:17:48,579
YOU DON 'T SAY ?

336
00:17:52,384 --> 00:17:54,352
- MR. FITZGERALD ? - YES ?

337
00:17:54,452 --> 00:17:55,686
OH , IT 'S YOU .

338
00:17:55,786 --> 00:17:57,322
MAY I SPEAK TO YOU FOR A MOMENT ?

339
00:17:57,422 --> 00:17:59,324
LOOK HERE , YOUNG LADY , IF YOU WANT TO TALK ME OUT

340
00:17:59,424 --> 00:18:02,227
OF WINDWARD HOUSE , YOU MIGHT JUST AS WELL SAVE YOUR BREATH .

341
00:18:02,327 --> 00:18:05,395
IT ISN 'T THAT . IT 'S ABOUT ME , YESTERDAY AFTERNOON .

342
00:18:05,597 --> 00:18:07,299
MY BEHAVIOR WAS INEXCUSABLE .

343
00:18:07,399 --> 00:18:09,767
COME NOW , IT WASN 'T AS BAD AS ALL THAT .

344
00:18:09,867 --> 00:18:11,002
THANK YOU , VERY MUCH .

345
00:18:11,102 --> 00:18:13,438
YOUR GRANDFATHER MADE YOU APOLOGIZE , DIDN 'T HE ?

346
00:18:13,538 --> 00:18:15,973
OH , NO , IT WAS MY MOTHER .

347
00:18:16,073 --> 00:18:17,041
YOUR MOTH- -

348
00:18:17,141 --> 00:18:19,409
BUT I UNDERSTOOD THAT- - I BEG YOUR PARDON ?

349
00:18:19,509 --> 00:18:22,443
I KEPT LOOKING AT HER LAST NIGHT , THINKING HOW I 'D LET HER DOWN .

350
00:18:23,444 --> 00:18:24,945
BUT ISN 'T YOUR MOTHER DEAD ?

351
00:18:25,045 --> 00:18:27,818
YES , BUT I KNOW ALL ABOUT HER- - FROM GRANDFATHER , OF COURSE .

352
00:18:27,918 --> 00:18:29,686
I WAS ONLY THREE WHEN SHE DIED .

353
00:18:29,786 --> 00:18:31,455
BUT I THOUGHT YOU SAID YOU LOOKED AT HER .

354
00:18:31,555 --> 00:18:34,691
HER PORTRAIT HANGS IN MY ROOM . MY FATHER PAINTED IT .

355
00:18:34,791 --> 00:18:36,493
OH , THEN IT WAS HIS STUDIO .

356
00:18:36,593 --> 00:18:39,361
YES , AND SHE WAS SO BEAUTIFUL .

357
00:18:39,763 --> 00:18:42,363
LET 'S GO FOR A WALK .

358
00:18:44,367 --> 00:18:46,903
GRANDFATHER WILL NEVER GET OVER HER DEATH .

359
00:18:47,003 --> 00:18:49,105
HE 'S HATED WINDWARD EVER SINCE .

360
00:18:49,205 --> 00:18:50,406
THAT 'S UNDERSTANDABLE .

361
00:18:50,506 --> 00:18:53,576
BUT IT ISN 'T FAIR TO HATE A HOUSE BECAUSE SOMEONE 'S DIED THERE .

362
00:18:53,676 --> 00:18:56,445
I LOVE WINDWARD BECAUSE SHE LIVED THERE

363
00:18:56,545 --> 00:18:58,381
FOR THREE YEARS AND THOSE WERE MY YEARS .

364
00:18:58,481 --> 00:19:01,484
AND THAT 'S WHY YOU DON 'T WANT ANYONE ELSE TO LIVE IN IT ?

365
00:19:01,584 --> 00:19:03,719
THAT 'S FOOLISH , ISN 'T IT ?

366
00:19:03,819 --> 00:19:05,488
NO , JUST ONE THING IS FOOLISH .

367
00:19:05,588 --> 00:19:07,423
YOU 'RE LIVING SOMEBODY ELSE 'S LIFE .

368
00:19:07,523 --> 00:19:09,392
HOW OLD ARE YOU , STELLA MEREDITH ?

369
00:19:09,492 --> 00:19:12,526
- 20 . - YOU 'RE 20 , AND YOU 'RE PRETTY .

370
00:19:12,995 --> 00:19:14,930
YOU SHOULDN 'T WASTE A SINGLE SECOND

371
00:19:15,030 --> 00:19:16,832
LOOKING BACK ON THREE LITTLE YEARS .

372
00:19:16,932 --> 00:19:18,667
- YOU SHOULD BE HAVING FUN . - I AM .

373
00:19:18,767 --> 00:19:21,336
OH , NONSENSE . WHAT ARE YOU DOING TODAY , FOR INSTANCE ?

374
00:19:21,436 --> 00:19:24,471
- OH , JUST THINGS . - FACTS , DETAILS , COME ON .

375
00:19:25,040 --> 00:19:26,941
OH , DEAR .

376
00:19:27,041 --> 00:19:28,843
I 'VE GOT TO MATCH SOME WOOL .

377
00:19:28,943 --> 00:19:31,180
THEN I HAVE TO STOP AT THE LENDING LIBRARY

378
00:19:31,280 --> 00:19:32,914
AND GET A COPY OF BLEAK HOUSE .

379
00:19:33,014 --> 00:19:34,749
GRANDFATHER AND I ARE READING DICKENS .

380
00:19:34,849 --> 00:19:38,317
YOU 'RE NOT GOING TO DO ANY OF THOSE THINGS . I HAVE A BETTER IDEA .

381
00:19:47,761 --> 00:19:50,431
ISN 'T THIS BETTER THAN READING TO GRANDFATHER ?

382
00:19:50,531 --> 00:19:52,833
OH , IT 'S WONDERFUL .

383
00:19:52,933 --> 00:19:54,635
EVER GET SEASICK ?

384
00:19:54,735 --> 00:19:55,703
( chuckles )

385
00:19:55,803 --> 00:19:58,172
FORTUNATELY , I HAVE A STOMACH LIKE GIBRALTAR .

386
00:19:58,272 --> 00:20:00,939
NOT EXTERNALLY , OF COURSE .

387
00:20:02,710 --> 00:20:03,977
Stella : ARE YOU ASLEEP ?

388
00:20:04,077 --> 00:20:06,714
NO , JUST WONDERING IF OUR NATIONAL CONFIDENCE

389
00:20:06,814 --> 00:20:09,581
IN GIBRALTAR ISN 'T MISPLACED .

390
00:20:17,324 --> 00:20:19,226
SHOULDN 'T YOU GET OUT OF THE SUN ?

391
00:20:19,326 --> 00:20:21,993
NO , I 'D- - I 'D RATHER- -

392
00:20:22,262 --> 00:20:24,364
REMAIN HERE .

393
00:20:24,464 --> 00:20:27,398
OH , PLEASE- - THE TILLER- - PLEASE !

394
00:20:27,834 --> 00:20:30,368
OH ! ( groans )

395
00:20:33,673 --> 00:20:34,974
SMELLS GOOD .

396
00:20:35,074 --> 00:20:37,510
THAT 'S MIMOSA . IT WAS MY MO- -

397
00:20:37,610 --> 00:20:40,711
OH , I FORGOT , I 'M NOT SUPPOSED TO TALK ABOUT THAT .

398
00:20:41,580 --> 00:20:44,281
- WHY ? - OUT OF THE PAST .

399
00:20:44,416 --> 00:20:45,517
OH , GO AHEAD .

400
00:20:45,617 --> 00:20:47,586
IT WAS MY MOTHER 'S FAVORITE PERFUME .

401
00:20:47,686 --> 00:20:49,989
MY FATHER SENT ME A BOTTLE BEFORE HE DIED .

402
00:20:50,089 --> 00:20:52,822
I 'VE MADE IT LAST A LONG TIME .

403
00:20:54,593 --> 00:20:55,560
MIMOSA .

404
00:20:55,660 --> 00:20:57,729
- EVER SEE IT GROWING ? - NO , I HAVEN 'T .

405
00:20:57,829 --> 00:21:00,365
LIKE A MILLION LITTLE YELLOW BELLS , LIKE- -

406
00:21:00,465 --> 00:21:03,199
( groans ) LIKE SLEIGH BELLS .

407
00:21:10,141 --> 00:21:13,109
IT 'S SMOOTH AGAIN . ARE YOU FEELING BETTER ?

408
00:21:13,278 --> 00:21:14,445
OH , YES .

409
00:21:14,545 --> 00:21:16,147
I WAS ABOUT TO RESUME COMMAND .

410
00:21:16,247 --> 00:21:19,315
BRING HER ABOUT SHARPLY . HEAD STRAIGHT FOR THE JETTY .

411
00:21:19,450 --> 00:21:21,885
AVAST THE BOOM . SCUTTLE THE FUNNELS .

412
00:21:21,985 --> 00:21:24,455
- OH ! - OH ! ( laughs )

413
00:21:24,555 --> 00:21:26,988
LADY , PLEASE .

414
00:21:32,563 --> 00:21:35,299
Boatman : I THOUGHT YOU 'D GONE OFF FOR LONDON , MR. FITZGERALD .

415
00:21:35,399 --> 00:21:38,533
- JUST LEAVING NOW , BEN . - THAT 'LL BE HALF A CROWN .

416
00:21:41,738 --> 00:21:42,472
- YOU DOING UP YOUR HAIR AGAIN ?

417
00:21:42,572 --> 00:21:44,474
- Stella : YES .

418
00:21:44,574 --> 00:21:47,208
NO , NO , NO . COME ON .

419
00:21:48,878 --> 00:21:52,147
IT 'S WONDERFUL LIKE THIS . ALL LOOSE AND FREE AND WINDBLOWN .

420
00:21:52,249 --> 00:21:54,284
WHAT AM I DOING ? TALKING HIGH POETRY

421
00:21:54,384 --> 00:21:55,752
OR SELLING HAIRSTYLE ADVERTISING ?

422
00:21:55,852 --> 00:21:58,087
- YOU LAUGH AT EVERYTHING , DON 'T YOU ? - TOO MUCH ?

423
00:21:58,187 --> 00:22:01,288
OH , NO . I 'VE NEVER KNOWN ANYONE WHO LAUGHED MUCH .

424
00:22:03,660 --> 00:22:05,595
SEE A LOT OF PAMELA WHILE I 'M AWAY , WILL YOU ?

425
00:22:05,695 --> 00:22:08,097
- HOW LONG WILL YOU BE GONE ? - OH , ABOUT THREE WEEKS .

426
00:22:08,197 --> 00:22:10,800
PERHAPS SHE 'LL LET ME HELP HER WITH CURTAINS AND THINGS .

427
00:22:10,900 --> 00:22:14,101
GET HER TO TALK ABOUT ME- - IN A RESPECTFUL WAY , OF COURSE .

428
00:22:14,403 --> 00:22:17,537
NONE OF THOSE ANECDOTES WHERE I 'M THE FAMILY HALFWIT .

429
00:22:20,609 --> 00:22:22,245
I HOPE YOU HAVE A NICE TRIP .

430
00:22:22,345 --> 00:22:24,913
- I 'LL TAKE YOU HOME FIRST . - YOU 'RE SO LATE STARTING .

431
00:22:25,013 --> 00:22:26,982
- MIGHT AS WELL . - I 'D RATHER BREAK IT GENTLY

432
00:22:27,082 --> 00:22:30,218
TO GRANDFATHER ABOUT OUR SAIL . IF YOU DON 'T MIND .

433
00:22:30,318 --> 00:22:33,086
ALL RIGHT , GENTLY BUT FIRMLY , MIND .

434
00:22:33,188 --> 00:22:35,290
- GOODBYE . - GOODBYE .

435
00:22:35,390 --> 00:22:38,124
- OH , MR. FITZGERALD ! - YES ?

436
00:22:38,226 --> 00:22:39,561
I ALMOST FORGOT TO SAY IT .

437
00:22:39,661 --> 00:22:43,098
I 'M AWFULLY HAPPY YOU AND YOUR SISTER ARE GOING TO LIVE AT WINDWARD .

438
00:22:43,198 --> 00:22:45,998
WHY , THANK YOU , STELLA MEREDITH .

439
00:23:07,721 --> 00:23:09,156
WELL , HERE WE ARE .

440
00:23:09,256 --> 00:23:11,792
WHAT A GRAND HOUSE , MASTER RICK .

441
00:23:11,892 --> 00:23:13,160
'TIS A MANSION , SO ' TIS .

442
00:23:13,260 --> 00:23:13,660
ARE YOU WORTHY OF IT ,

443
00:23:13,760 --> 00:23:16,463
LIZZIE FLYNN ? THAT 'S WHAT I KEEP ASKING MYSELF .

444
00:23:16,563 --> 00:23:19,233
( laughs ) 'TIS ON TOP OF THE WORLD .

445
00:23:19,333 --> 00:23:21,034
- RICK ! - HELLO , PAM .

446
00:23:21,134 --> 00:23:23,801
- LIZZIE ! - BABY , DARLING .

447
00:23:25,005 --> 00:23:27,474
YOU DEVIL FOR BEING LATE . I WANTED YOU TO SEE

448
00:23:27,574 --> 00:23:29,543
EVERYTHING WHILE IT WAS STILL DAYLIGHT .

449
00:23:29,643 --> 00:23:31,912
MASTER RICK AND HIS FRIENDS AND THEIR COCKTAILS .

450
00:23:32,012 --> 00:23:34,547
- WE GOT LIZZIE DRUNK . - GET ON WITH YOU , MASTER RICK .

451
00:23:34,647 --> 00:23:37,183
BOBBY ! OH , BOBBY ! WHERE 'S OUR BOBBY ?

452
00:23:37,283 --> 00:23:38,684
- ( whistles ) - DON 'T , RICK .

453
00:23:38,784 --> 00:23:42,319
- SOMETHING HAPPEN TO HIM ? - NOTHING TRAGIC . HE JUST WANDERED AWAY .

454
00:23:43,122 --> 00:23:45,191
I SUPPOSE I HAVEN 'T ENOUGH DOG APPEAL .

455
00:23:45,291 --> 00:23:46,525
NO , SERIOUSLY , PAM .

456
00:23:46,625 --> 00:23:49,662
HE LOATHED THE COUNTRY . YOU KNOW , NO NICE DUST BINS ,

457
00:23:49,762 --> 00:23:52,332
NO SPORTING INTEREST IN FINDING A TREE .

458
00:23:52,432 --> 00:23:55,432
HMM- - NEVER HEARD OF A TERRIER WALKING OUT .

459
00:23:59,637 --> 00:24:02,107
AH , MISS PAMELA , I 'M DREAMING ON ME FEET .

460
00:24:02,207 --> 00:24:05,475
Rick : PAM , IT 'S PERFECT . YOU 'RE PRACTICALLY STRAIGHT .

461
00:24:05,945 --> 00:24:08,678
THERE 'S SOUP IN THE KITCHEN .

462
00:24:08,947 --> 00:24:11,383
LOOK AT WHISKEY NOW . HE KNOWS WHERE THE FOOD IS .

463
00:24:11,483 --> 00:24:13,751
- HOW DID THE FURNITURE FIT IN ? - OH , BEAUTIFULLY .

464
00:24:13,851 --> 00:24:16,554
I SAW THE GRANDFATHER CLOCK . IT WAVED BOTH HANDS AT ME .

465
00:24:16,654 --> 00:24:18,857
IF THE SOUP 'S BURNED , LIZZIE WILL SPANK ME .

466
00:24:18,957 --> 00:24:20,359
GET ON WITH YOU , MISS .

467
00:24:20,459 --> 00:24:23,194
THE SAINTS BE PRAISED . THERE 'S ME OLD ROCKER .

468
00:24:23,294 --> 00:24:26,495
IT 'S BEEN 10 YEARS SINCE YOU NESTLED YOUR BUSTLE IN THAT .

469
00:24:26,998 --> 00:24:29,331
( laughs )

470
00:24:30,501 --> 00:24:33,402
- YOU 'VE DONE WONDERS , PAM . - THANKS .

471
00:24:36,373 --> 00:24:39,241
WHAT DOES STELLA THINK OF THE CHANGES ?

472
00:24:39,343 --> 00:24:41,078
- YOU MEAN STELLA MEREDITH ? - MM-HMM .

473
00:24:41,178 --> 00:24:42,946
- I HAVEN 'T SET EYES ON HER . - YOU HAVEN 'T ?

474
00:24:43,046 --> 00:24:45,649
I DID WRITE AND ASK HER TO TEA . GOT A REPLY FROM THE COMMANDER ,

475
00:24:45,749 --> 00:24:49,017
SAYING SHE WASN 'T STRONG ENOUGH TO ACCEPT INVITATIONS .

476
00:24:49,219 --> 00:24:51,655
- NOT STRONG ENOUGH ? - I EXPECT IT 'S US .

477
00:24:51,755 --> 00:24:53,123
WE JUST AREN 'T NICE TO KNOW .

478
00:24:53,223 --> 00:24:56,126
BUT THAT 'S NOT STELLA . SHE WAS CRAZY TO MAKE FRIENDS WITH YOU .

479
00:24:56,226 --> 00:24:58,594
- SHE TOLD ME . - BUT WHERE DID YOU SEE HER ?

480
00:24:58,694 --> 00:25:01,695
HMM ? OH , UH , JUST BEFORE I LEFT FOR LONDON .

481
00:25:02,299 --> 00:25:05,033
WHY , YOU COLOSSAL BLUFF !

482
00:25:05,135 --> 00:25:08,005
YOU WERE JUST AS SORRY FOR THAT CHILD AS I WAS .

483
00:25:08,105 --> 00:25:09,939
STOP PUSHING HER INTO THE NURSERY .

484
00:25:10,039 --> 00:25:12,074
SHE 'S 20 , SHE SAID SO HERSELF .

485
00:25:12,174 --> 00:25:14,575
YOU LIKE HER .

486
00:25:17,113 --> 00:25:19,580
I CAN 'T HELP IT .

487
00:25:19,915 --> 00:25:24,020
THERE 'S KIND OF A SLEEPING BEAUTY MAGIC ABOUT THE KID .

488
00:25:24,120 --> 00:25:27,354
I 'D THOUGHT I 'D DONE SOMETHING TOWARDS BREAKING THE SPELL .

489
00:25:28,090 --> 00:25:29,658
SEEMS NOT .

490
00:25:29,758 --> 00:25:32,526
" PRINCE CHARMLESS , " THAT 'S ME .

491
00:25:32,628 --> 00:25:34,629
THAT 'LL DO FOR TONIGHT , MR. RODERICK .

492
00:25:34,729 --> 00:25:37,666
IT 'S TIME FOR MISS PAMELA TO GO TO BED .

493
00:25:37,766 --> 00:25:38,734
SHE LOOKS TIRED OUT .

494
00:25:38,834 --> 00:25:41,470
YOU 'RE AN OLD TYRANT , LIZZIE FLYNN .

495
00:25:41,570 --> 00:25:44,203
BUT YOU 'RE PERFECTLY RIGHT .

496
00:25:47,075 --> 00:25:49,742
PUT THE LIGHTS OUT , RICK .

497
00:25:51,245 --> 00:25:52,013
NOW , LET 'S SEE .

498
00:25:52,113 --> 00:25:55,214
I THINK I TURN IT DOWN AND BLOW DOWN THE CHIMNEY .

499
00:25:57,618 --> 00:26:00,354
I HAVEN 'T DONE THAT SINCE I WAS A KID .

500
00:26:00,454 --> 00:26:01,957
COME ON , WHISKEY .

501
00:26:02,057 --> 00:26:03,324
- ( cat meows ) - OH .

502
00:26:03,424 --> 00:26:05,193
ARE YOU HAVING HIM IN YOUR ROOM ?

503
00:26:05,293 --> 00:26:07,161
HE 'S USED TO IT , THE CREATURE .

504
00:26:07,261 --> 00:26:09,695
GET ALONG UP NOW .

505
00:26:10,064 --> 00:26:12,467
Lizzie : HAVEN 'T I CARRIED YOU ENOUGH THIS DAY ?

506
00:26:12,567 --> 00:26:15,534
- GET ON UP , NOW . - I 'LL GIVE HIM A START .

507
00:26:17,971 --> 00:26:19,873
WHAT IN THE NAME OF ALL THE SAINTS ?

508
00:26:19,973 --> 00:26:22,342
OH , WELL , HE 'S NOT USED TO TRAVELING ,

509
00:26:22,442 --> 00:26:24,078
AND STRANGE HOUSES .

510
00:26:24,178 --> 00:26:25,678
HE 'LL FIND ME IF HE WANTS ME .

511
00:26:25,778 --> 00:26:28,181
I 'VE NOT SLEPT WITH THE SOUND OF THE SEA

512
00:26:28,281 --> 00:26:29,849
IN ME EARS SINCE I LEFT IRELAND .

513
00:26:29,949 --> 00:26:31,851
WOULD YOU LIKE TO GO BACK THERE ?

514
00:26:31,951 --> 00:26:33,886
I 'D SOONER SEE MYSELF DEAD .

515
00:26:33,986 --> 00:26:36,654
Rick : AW , GO ON WITH YOU !

516
00:26:38,825 --> 00:26:40,860
WHY , WHATEVER AILS THESE CANDLES ?

517
00:26:40,960 --> 00:26:43,029
IT SEEMS TO BE A RATHER DRAFTY STAIRCASE .

518
00:26:43,129 --> 00:26:46,330
RICK , I 'VE HAD A SWIM EVERY DAY FROM OUR OWN BEACH ,

519
00:26:46,600 --> 00:26:48,034
AND I 'VE STARTED TO MAKE A GARDEN .

520
00:26:48,134 --> 00:26:50,503
YOU LEARN THE ODDEST THINGS WHEN YOU- - WHEN YOU GARDEN .

521
00:26:50,603 --> 00:26:53,339
DID YOU KNOW THERE WAS AN UPSIDE-DOWN TO SEEDS ?

522
00:26:53,439 --> 00:26:54,540
NO . GOOD NIGHT .

523
00:26:54,640 --> 00:26:57,409
- GOOD NIGHT , RICK . - GOOD NIGHT , MASTER RICK .

524
00:26:57,509 --> 00:26:59,943
GOOD NIGHT , LIZ .

525
00:27:03,349 --> 00:27:06,183
- ( knocking on door ) - COME IN !

526
00:27:11,823 --> 00:27:13,125
I THOUGHT YOU WERE ASLEEP .

527
00:27:13,225 --> 00:27:16,226
IT TURNS COLD IN THE NIGHT HERE SOMETIMES .

528
00:27:18,496 --> 00:27:20,864
OH , THANKS .

529
00:27:21,967 --> 00:27:24,968
THERE 'S SOMETHING I WANT TO TALK TO YOU ABOUT .

530
00:27:25,303 --> 00:27:26,771
DO YOU HAVE ANY NICE CAST-IRON

531
00:27:26,871 --> 00:27:28,606
I CAN SWAP FOR THIS MATTRESS ?

532
00:27:28,706 --> 00:27:30,441
WE 'LL GIVE YOU ANOTHER TOMORROW .

533
00:27:30,541 --> 00:27:33,309
NOTHING WILL KEEP ME AWAKE TONIGHT .

534
00:27:33,745 --> 00:27:36,646
WHAT PRICE OUR HOUSE ? PRETTY GOOD , HMM ?

535
00:27:36,914 --> 00:27:38,483
YOU 'RE REALLY PLEASED WITH IT ?

536
00:27:38,583 --> 00:27:40,351
I WAS NEVER SO HAPPY IN MY LIFE .

537
00:27:40,451 --> 00:27:42,987
YOU STARTED TO SAY SOMETHING . WHAT ?

538
00:27:43,087 --> 00:27:44,789
WELL , IT WAS JUST- - JUST THAT I WAS

539
00:27:44,889 --> 00:27:46,658
THE ONE WHO GOT YOU TO BUY THE HOUSE- -

540
00:27:46,758 --> 00:27:49,894
AND I DIDN 'T APPEAR VERY APPRECIATIVE . IS THAT IT ?

541
00:27:49,994 --> 00:27:51,461
IT 'LL WAIT TILL TOMORROW .

542
00:27:51,561 --> 00:27:54,296
BLESS YOU , RICK . SLEEP WELL .

543
00:27:54,931 --> 00:27:56,500
YOU , TOO .

544
00:27:56,600 --> 00:27:59,268
THESE ARE PRETTY GOOD APPLES .

545
00:28:01,505 --> 00:28:04,672
Announcer : That concludes our broadcast for today .

546
00:28:04,874 --> 00:28:07,709
Good night , everyone . Good night .

547
00:28:39,642 --> 00:28:42,142
( woman sobbing )

548
00:28:46,882 --> 00:28:49,316
PAM , IS THAT YOU ?

549
00:28:57,959 --> 00:29:00,493
( sobbing continues )

550
00:29:22,616 --> 00:29:25,184
( sobbing continues )

551
00:29:57,149 --> 00:29:59,617
( moaning , sighs )

552
00:30:05,658 --> 00:30:07,259
- RICK . - PAMELA !

553
00:30:07,359 --> 00:30:10,160
WE DON 'T WANT TO WAKE LIZZIE .

554
00:30:10,295 --> 00:30:11,731
BUT , ISN 'T IT LIZZIE ?

555
00:30:11,831 --> 00:30:14,066
NO , IT ISN 'T LIZZIE .

556
00:30:14,166 --> 00:30:16,335
IT 'S COMING FROM DOWNSTAIRS .

557
00:30:16,435 --> 00:30:19,302
IT COMES FROM EVERYWHERE , AND NOWHERE .

558
00:30:19,671 --> 00:30:21,206
NOW , TAKE HOLD OF YOURSELF , PAM .

559
00:30:21,306 --> 00:30:23,642
I 'M GOING DOWN AND SEARCH THE PLACE .

560
00:30:23,742 --> 00:30:25,210
I 'VE SEARCHED .

561
00:30:25,310 --> 00:30:26,911
THERE 'S NEVER ANYTHING THERE .

562
00:30:27,011 --> 00:30:29,948
NEVER ? DO YOU MEAN YOU 'VE HEARD IT BEFORE ?

563
00:30:30,048 --> 00:30:32,651
YES . IT 'S TRUE , ISN 'T IT ?

564
00:30:32,751 --> 00:30:34,485
THE SOUND , I MEAN . YOU 'RE HEARING IT , TOO ?

565
00:30:34,585 --> 00:30:36,888
- OF COURSE I 'M HEARING IT . - YOU SEE , I WASN 'T SURE .

566
00:30:36,988 --> 00:30:39,924
- PAM ! - I THOUGHT I MIGHT BE GOING CRAZY .

567
00:30:40,024 --> 00:30:41,760
WAS THAT WHY YOU DIDN 'T TELL ME ?

568
00:30:41,860 --> 00:30:44,526
YES , THAT- - IT 'S YOUR HOME .

569
00:30:45,029 --> 00:30:47,198
IT 'S ALL WE 'VE GOT TO LIVE IN .

570
00:30:47,298 --> 00:30:49,800
( woman 's voice wails )

571
00:30:49,900 --> 00:30:52,270
IT SOUNDS SO HEARTBROKEN .

572
00:30:52,370 --> 00:30:53,571
NOW DON 'T GET RATTLED .

573
00:30:53,671 --> 00:30:55,105
THERE 'S A LOGICAL EXPLANATION FOR THIS .

574
00:30:55,205 --> 00:30:58,241
- SUCH AS ? - YOU CAN 'T EXPECT ME TO GIVE IT TO YOU OFFHAND ?

575
00:30:58,341 --> 00:31:01,443
BUT IT STANDS TO REASON . DOES IT COME EVERY NIGHT ?

576
00:31:03,413 --> 00:31:06,050
NO ... BUT JUST WHEN YOU BEGIN

577
00:31:06,150 --> 00:31:08,651
TO THINK YOU 'VE DREAMT IT , IT COMES AGAIN .

578
00:31:08,751 --> 00:31:11,386
BE CALM , PAM , BE CALM .

579
00:31:11,621 --> 00:31:14,422
I 'M ALL RIGHT . IT 'LL STOP SOON NOW .

580
00:31:16,526 --> 00:31:18,161
HOW DO YOU KNOW ?

581
00:31:18,261 --> 00:31:20,828
IT DIES AWAY AT DAWN .

582
00:31:21,764 --> 00:31:23,099
LISTEN .

583
00:31:23,199 --> 00:31:25,566
( silence )

584
00:31:28,171 --> 00:31:30,972
Pam : THAT 'S THE DAWN BREEZE .

585
00:31:31,941 --> 00:31:33,776
WELL , THAT 'S ALL FOR TONIGHT .

586
00:31:33,876 --> 00:31:35,477
THAT 'S A PITY , REALLY .

587
00:31:35,577 --> 00:31:37,446
HARDLY GIVES ONE TIME TO LOOK INTO IT .

588
00:31:37,546 --> 00:31:40,647
- NOW LISTEN , DEAR- - - LOOK , LET 'S TALK TOMORROW .

589
00:31:40,782 --> 00:31:42,818
I 'LL DIE IF I DON 'T GET SOME SLEEP .

590
00:31:42,918 --> 00:31:45,787
PAM , LEAVE YOUR DOOR OPEN IN CASE YOU 'RE NERVOUS .

591
00:31:45,887 --> 00:31:46,855
ALL RIGHT , RICK .

592
00:31:46,955 --> 00:31:49,158
REMEMBER , YOU HAVEN 'T A THING TO WORRY ABOUT .

593
00:31:49,258 --> 00:31:51,293
THIS BUSINESS CAN BE SCIENTIFICALLY EXPLAINED .

594
00:31:51,393 --> 00:31:54,162
PROBABLY A LOOSE WIRE HIDDEN AROUND THE HOUSE SOMEWHERE ,

595
00:31:54,262 --> 00:31:56,064
ACTING AS AN AERIAL , PICKING UP THE SOUND

596
00:31:56,164 --> 00:31:57,866
OF SOME WOMAN IN THE VILLAGE CRYING .

597
00:31:57,966 --> 00:32:01,302
Pam : WAS SHE CRYING WHEN THE LAST TENANTS WERE FRIGHTENED OUT ?

598
00:32:01,402 --> 00:32:04,204
WELL , MAYBE SHE HAD A SAD LIFE .

599
00:32:05,606 --> 00:32:07,976
ANYWAY , I 'M HERE NOW ,

600
00:32:08,076 --> 00:32:10,178
AND I 'M NOT THE LEAST RATTLED .

601
00:32:10,278 --> 00:32:13,179
NOT THE LEAST LITTLE BIT IN THE WORLD .

602
00:32:16,150 --> 00:32:18,884
IT 'S JUST SILLY TO BE UPSET .

603
00:32:25,860 --> 00:32:28,260
( mild slam )

604
00:32:33,133 --> 00:32:37,371
LAST NIGHT I HEARD A PERFECTLY APPALLING SOUND OF CRYING .

605
00:32:37,471 --> 00:32:40,705
MR. FITZGERALD , WINDWARD HOUSE BELONGS TO YOU NOW .

606
00:32:41,341 --> 00:32:43,210
WHY DO YOU BRING THIS MATTER TO ME ?

607
00:32:43,310 --> 00:32:44,578
BECAUSE WE WANT INFORMATION .

608
00:32:44,678 --> 00:32:46,380
I , FOR PRACTICAL REASONS , AND MY SISTER

609
00:32:46,480 --> 00:32:47,914
BECAUSE SHE BELIEVES IT 'S A GHOST .

610
00:32:48,014 --> 00:32:50,049
SHE 'D LIKE TO KNOW WHAT THE GHOST WANTS .

611
00:32:50,149 --> 00:32:52,686
- WHAT UTTER BOSH . - BOSH , I AGREE .

612
00:32:52,786 --> 00:32:55,221
BUT WHEN DID THE NOISES START ?

613
00:32:55,321 --> 00:32:57,390
YOU INHERITED THE HOUSE , I BELIEVE ?

614
00:32:57,490 --> 00:32:58,357
FROM MY GRANDMOTHER .

615
00:32:58,457 --> 00:33:00,259
AND THERE WERE NO DISTURBANCES IN HER TIME ?

616
00:33:00,359 --> 00:33:02,128
NONE . AND IF THERE ARE ANY NOISES NOW ,

617
00:33:02,228 --> 00:33:03,897
THEY 'RE FROM PERFECTLY NATURAL CAUSES .

618
00:33:03,997 --> 00:33:05,798
AN ECHO FROM A SUBTERRANEAN CAVE , PERHAPS .

619
00:33:05,898 --> 00:33:07,934
THAT WOULD HAVE BEEN HEARD IN YOUR GRANDMOTHER 'S DAY .

620
00:33:08,034 --> 00:33:10,503
EROSION MAY HAVE CHANGED THE STRUCTURE OF THE CLIFFS .

621
00:33:10,603 --> 00:33:12,738
Rick : WELL , IT 'S NOT A BAD SUGGESTION .

622
00:33:12,838 --> 00:33:14,240
MAY I COME IN , GRANDFATHER ?

623
00:33:14,340 --> 00:33:15,741
NO , YOU RUN ALONG TO CHURCH .

624
00:33:15,841 --> 00:33:17,243
I 'LL JOIN YOU IN JUST A FEW MINUTES .

625
00:33:17,343 --> 00:33:18,777
BUT I WANT TO SEE MR. FITZGERALD .

626
00:33:18,877 --> 00:33:20,579
I 'M AWFULLY GLAD YOU 'RE BETTER .

627
00:33:20,679 --> 00:33:22,147
BETTER ?

628
00:33:22,247 --> 00:33:23,683
BUT I HAVEN 'T BEEN ILL .

629
00:33:23,783 --> 00:33:26,518
STELLA MERELY SUFFERS WITH A GENERAL DELICACY .

630
00:33:26,618 --> 00:33:28,654
SHE DOESN 'T ACCEPT INVITATIONS .

631
00:33:28,754 --> 00:33:29,254
NEVER ?

632
00:33:29,354 --> 00:33:30,889
PERHAPS I 'D BETTER FRANKLY STATE

633
00:33:30,989 --> 00:33:32,891
SHE 'S NOT STRONG ENOUGH TO MAKE NEW FRIENDS .

634
00:33:32,991 --> 00:33:34,726
- GRANDFATHER ? ! - RUN ALONG , MY DEAR .

635
00:33:34,826 --> 00:33:37,627
WE 'RE DISCUSSING SOMETHING PRIVATE .

636
00:33:40,599 --> 00:33:42,434
IS THERE ANYTHING ELSE ?

637
00:33:42,534 --> 00:33:43,768
NO , JUST ONE MORE QUESTION .

638
00:33:43,868 --> 00:33:46,438
WAS STELLA 'S MOTHER EVER TROUBLED AT WINDWARD HOUSE ?

639
00:33:46,538 --> 00:33:48,640
- WHAT DO YOU MEAN ? - DID SHE HEAR THE CRYING ?

640
00:33:48,740 --> 00:33:51,907
MY DAUGHTER WAS NOT ONE TO CIRCULATE RIDICULOUS RUMORS .

641
00:33:52,176 --> 00:33:54,012
IF SHE 'D HEARD THIS , SHE 'D HAVE MENTIONED IT ,

642
00:33:54,112 --> 00:33:55,780
- AND SHE NEVER DID ? - CERTAINLY NOT .

643
00:33:55,880 --> 00:33:57,815
THEN THE TROUBLE MUST HAVE BEGUN SINCE HER DEATH .

644
00:33:57,915 --> 00:34:01,483
- DO YOU MEAN TO IMPLY- - - OH , NO , I 'M MERELY TRYING TO SET THE DATE .

645
00:34:01,652 --> 00:34:03,554
I DIDN 'T MEAN THAT YOUR DAUGHTER HAUNTS- -

646
00:34:03,654 --> 00:34:05,256
HOW DARE YOU SUGGEST SUCH A THING ?

647
00:34:05,356 --> 00:34:08,526
REALLY , I 'M MOST DESPERATELY SORRY . PLEASE FORGIVE ME .

648
00:34:08,626 --> 00:34:10,327
VERY WELL . I ACCEPT YOUR APOLOGY .

649
00:34:10,427 --> 00:34:12,263
BUT PLEASE UNDERSTAND ONE THING .

650
00:34:12,363 --> 00:34:14,064
YOUR PURCHASE OF THE PROPERTY

651
00:34:14,164 --> 00:34:17,165
DOESN 'T ESTABLISH A SOCIAL BOND BETWEEN US .

652
00:34:17,801 --> 00:34:19,302
WHAT 'S THE MATTER WITH US ?

653
00:34:19,402 --> 00:34:21,437
WHY DON 'T YOU ALLOW STELLA TO SEE US ?

654
00:34:21,537 --> 00:34:22,939
BECAUSE I DON 'T WANT TO .

655
00:34:23,039 --> 00:34:24,440
AND I MUST ASK YOU FOR YOUR WORD

656
00:34:24,540 --> 00:34:26,209
NOT TO SEND HER ANY MORE INVITATIONS .

657
00:34:26,309 --> 00:34:27,677
I 'LL GIVE YOU NO SUCH UNDERTAKING .

658
00:34:27,777 --> 00:34:29,980
VERY WELL , I KNOW HOW TO DEAL WITH THE MATTER .

659
00:34:30,080 --> 00:34:32,981
STELLA IS NOT GOING INSIDE THAT HOUSE .

660
00:34:33,650 --> 00:34:34,884
GREAT SCOTT ,

661
00:34:34,984 --> 00:34:37,751
YOU BELIEVE THE PLACE IS HAUNTED .

662
00:34:47,730 --> 00:34:50,764
I HOPED YOU 'D COME ALONG . I WANTED TO TALK TO YOU .

663
00:34:51,834 --> 00:34:54,303
QUICK , DRIVE AROUND THE NEXT CORNER .

664
00:34:54,403 --> 00:34:56,703
GET IN .

665
00:34:59,441 --> 00:35:00,076
YOU HAD FOUR FRECKLES ON THE BOAT .

666
00:35:00,176 --> 00:35:04,046
THEY 'VE GONE . I COULDN 'T GO TO SEE YOUR SISTER .

667
00:35:04,146 --> 00:35:06,681
GRANDFATHER 'S BEEN ILL .

668
00:35:06,781 --> 00:35:09,148
TURN HERE .

669
00:35:14,523 --> 00:35:16,892
NOW , WHAT IS THIS ABOUT YOU NOT SEEING PAMELA ?

670
00:35:16,992 --> 00:35:19,260
AT THE MERE MENTION OF ME COMING TO WINDWARD ,

671
00:35:19,360 --> 00:35:20,829
GRANDFATHER ALMOST HAD AN ATTACK .

672
00:35:20,929 --> 00:35:22,797
YOU FEEL YOUR MOTHER NEVER WOULD HAVE LEFT HIM ?

673
00:35:22,897 --> 00:35:24,833
- NEVER . - YET SHE DID WHEN SHE MARRIED ,

674
00:35:24,933 --> 00:35:27,768
- HE SEEMED TO SURVIVE VERY NICELY . - HE WAS YOUNGER THEN .

675
00:35:27,868 --> 00:35:31,137
SO YOU 'RE GOING TO TURN INTO ONE OF THESE DIM LITTLE LADIES

676
00:35:31,439 --> 00:35:33,608
WHO FILL HOT-WATER BOTTLES FOR ELDERLY RELATIVES ?

677
00:35:33,708 --> 00:35:36,709
- GOODBYE , STELLA MEREDITH . - I 'M NOT NOW .

678
00:35:36,977 --> 00:35:38,279
YOU 'RE HERE NOW .

679
00:35:38,379 --> 00:35:41,647
THAT 'S PRACTICALLY THE NICEST SENTENCE THAT EVER WAS SPOKEN .

680
00:35:41,782 --> 00:35:45,183
WOULD YOU AND YOUR SISTER BE IN IF I CAME TO WINDWARD TONIGHT ?

681
00:35:45,620 --> 00:35:47,521
YES . SUPPER 'S AT 8 : 00 ,

682
00:35:47,621 --> 00:35:49,690
BUT PLEASE COME AS EARLY AS YOU CAN .

683
00:35:49,790 --> 00:35:50,824
( footsteps )

684
00:35:50,924 --> 00:35:53,892
BOB DOWN . HE 'S PASSING THE END OF THE LANE .

685
00:35:57,164 --> 00:35:58,598
HE 'S GONE .

686
00:35:58,698 --> 00:36:00,400
HOW WILL I EVER GET TO CHURCH ?

687
00:36:00,500 --> 00:36:03,601
SIT ON THE FLOOR OF THE CAR . I 'LL DRIVE YOU PAST HIM .

688
00:36:08,174 --> 00:36:10,577
DRIVE TO THE SIDE GATE , PLEASE .

689
00:36:10,677 --> 00:36:12,943
YES .

690
00:36:24,490 --> 00:36:26,258
LIKE A LIFT , COMMANDER ?

691
00:36:26,358 --> 00:36:28,759
NO , THANK YOU .

692
00:36:32,498 --> 00:36:35,332
- WHAT A MOMENT . - WERE YOU SCARED ?

693
00:36:35,668 --> 00:36:38,368
YES , BUT IT WAS WONDERFUL .

694
00:36:50,515 --> 00:36:53,482
WELL , GOODBYE . SAY A LITTLE PRAYER FOR ME .

695
00:36:54,219 --> 00:36:57,486
HOW AM I EVER GOING TO FEEL MEEK ENOUGH FOR CHURCH ?

696
00:37:00,292 --> 00:37:01,659
OH , STELLA !

697
00:37:01,759 --> 00:37:04,295
HERE 'S YOUR PRAYER BOOK AND PURSE .

698
00:37:04,395 --> 00:37:07,029
- GOODBYE . - GOODBYE .

699
00:37:08,132 --> 00:37:10,666
( congregation singing )

700
00:37:29,820 --> 00:37:31,888
THANK YOU , MRS. CARLTON , COLONEL .

701
00:37:31,988 --> 00:37:34,956
- Colonel : UNTIL NEXT SUNDAY . - Beech : YES .

702
00:37:35,091 --> 00:37:37,494
- GOODBYE . - GOODBYE .

703
00:37:37,594 --> 00:37:40,194
YOU SEEM VERY SILENT .

704
00:37:40,596 --> 00:37:43,166
WHAT HAVE YOU AGAINST THE FITZGERALDS ?

705
00:37:43,266 --> 00:37:45,967
WELL , THEY 'RE HARDLY OUR SORT .

706
00:37:46,769 --> 00:37:49,739
I 'VE DECIDED TO MAKE FRIENDS WITH THEM .

707
00:37:49,839 --> 00:37:52,539
YOU 'LL DO NO SUCH THING .

708
00:37:54,310 --> 00:37:56,011
WHY DO YOU SAY THAT , GRANDFATHER ?

709
00:37:56,111 --> 00:37:57,880
I DO NOT CONSIDER IT SUITABLE FOR YOU

710
00:37:57,980 --> 00:38:00,250
- TO VISIT WINDWARD HOUSE . - NOT SUITABLE ?

711
00:38:00,350 --> 00:38:01,817
I CAN 'T DISCUSS THE MATTER .

712
00:38:01,917 --> 00:38:04,654
THEN THAT 'S ALL THE REASON I 'M GOING TO GET FROM YOU ?

713
00:38:04,754 --> 00:38:06,288
IT WILL HAVE TO SUFFICE , YES .

714
00:38:06,388 --> 00:38:08,658
NO , GRANDFATHER , I 'M 20 AND I 'M- -

715
00:38:08,758 --> 00:38:11,825
IT 'S TIME I STOPPED LIVING SOMEBODY ELSE 'S LIFE .

716
00:38:12,727 --> 00:38:15,497
I SHALL GO TO WINDWARD WHENEVER I PLEASE .

717
00:38:15,597 --> 00:38:16,865
DID YOU HEAR WHAT I SAID ?

718
00:38:16,965 --> 00:38:19,766
IT ISN 'T ANY GOOD . I 'M ON STRIKE .

719
00:38:20,435 --> 00:38:21,536
GO TO YOUR ROOM .

720
00:38:21,636 --> 00:38:24,837
NO USE TRYING TO LOCK ME IN . THERE ISN 'T ANY KEY .

721
00:38:25,807 --> 00:38:28,441
DON 'T BE IMPERTINENT .

722
00:38:30,211 --> 00:38:33,047
- HELLO , ANNIE . - DINNER WILL BE LATE , MISS .

723
00:38:33,147 --> 00:38:35,416
I 'M HAVING EVER SUCH TROUBLE WITH THE LAMB .

724
00:38:35,516 --> 00:38:38,350
YOU 'D BETTER TELL THE COMMANDER .

725
00:38:41,522 --> 00:38:44,790
YES , IT 'S VERY URGENT . WILL YOU TRY TO HURRY THE CALL ?

726
00:38:45,893 --> 00:38:47,228
- ( knocking ) - THANK YOU .

727
00:38:47,328 --> 00:38:48,930
I 'M TELEPHONING . CLOSE THAT DOOR .

728
00:38:49,030 --> 00:38:51,365
IT 'S JUST THAT DINNER WILL BE LATE .

729
00:38:51,465 --> 00:38:52,866
IT 'S THE LAMB BEING AWKWARD .

730
00:38:52,966 --> 00:38:56,302
I WON 'T BE HERE FOR DINNER . TAKE SOME TO STELLA ON A TRAY .

731
00:38:57,838 --> 00:39:00,539
AND CLOSE THAT DOOR !

732
00:39:01,007 --> 00:39:03,374
( ringing )

733
00:39:04,044 --> 00:39:06,812
MAY I SPEAK TO MISS HOLLOWAY ?

734
00:39:10,984 --> 00:39:13,220
IT 'S A TRUNK CALL , MISS HOLLOWAY .

735
00:39:13,320 --> 00:39:14,955
A COMMANDER BEECH .

736
00:39:15,055 --> 00:39:17,388
THANK YOU .

737
00:39:20,193 --> 00:39:21,094
YES , COMMANDER BEECH .

738
00:39:21,194 --> 00:39:24,295
I WANT TO CONSULT YOU ABOUT STELLA , MISS HOLLOWAY .

739
00:39:24,797 --> 00:39:26,766
IT 'S A MATTER OF THE UTMOST URGENCY .

740
00:39:26,866 --> 00:39:29,001
I CAN BE WITH YOU LATE THIS AFTERNOON .

741
00:39:29,101 --> 00:39:30,737
I CAN 'T SEE YOU UNTIL THIS EVENING ,

742
00:39:30,837 --> 00:39:33,205
BUT I SHALL BE GLAD TO PUT YOU UP FOR THE NIGHT .

743
00:39:33,305 --> 00:39:35,808
ISN 'T IT A LITTLE LATE TO CONSULT ME ABOUT STELLA ?

744
00:39:35,908 --> 00:39:38,777
YES , YES , I KNOW THAT , BUT I BEG YOU TO HELP ME .

745
00:39:39,078 --> 00:39:42,614
YOU 'RE THE ONLY HUMAN BEING IN THE WORLD TO WHOM I CAN TURN .

746
00:39:42,714 --> 00:39:45,217
THE ONLY PERSON WHO WOULDN 'T THINK ME DEMENTED

747
00:39:45,317 --> 00:39:48,485
BECAUSE I BELIEVE A HOUSE CAN BE FILLED WITH MALIGNITY- -

748
00:39:49,355 --> 00:39:52,289
MALIGNITY DIRECTED AGAINST A CERTAIN CHILD .

749
00:39:54,659 --> 00:39:56,194
THE DINING ROOM ISN 'T FINISHED YET .

750
00:39:56,294 --> 00:39:59,364
HOW GLAD THIS HOUSE MUST BE TO BE LIVED IN AGAIN .

751
00:39:59,464 --> 00:40:00,666
I MUST DASH BACK TO LIZZIE .

752
00:40:00,766 --> 00:40:04,133
WE 'RE FIGHTING OVER HOW MUCH SHERRY YOU PUT IN A TIPSY PUDDING .

753
00:40:04,235 --> 00:40:05,637
SHE WANTS TO MAKE IT DEAD DRUNK .

754
00:40:05,737 --> 00:40:08,807
- DO YOU LIKE TIPSY PUDDING ? - I THINK I LIKE EVERYTHING TO EAT .

755
00:40:08,907 --> 00:40:11,276
SHOW HER THE REST OF THE HOUSE , RICK , BEFORE IT 'S DARK .

756
00:40:11,376 --> 00:40:14,610
YOU 'VE REALLY NEVER BEEN HERE SINCE YOU WERE THREE ?

757
00:40:14,712 --> 00:40:15,380
NOT INSIDE .

758
00:40:15,480 --> 00:40:18,847
BUT I WALKED HERE ONCE WHEN I WAS 10 AND PEERED IN AT THE WINDOWS .

759
00:40:18,949 --> 00:40:20,351
THERE WAS A STUPENDOUS ROW .

760
00:40:20,451 --> 00:40:23,688
AND THE NEXT WEEK I GOT PACKED OFF TO A SCHOOL IN BRUSSELS .

761
00:40:23,788 --> 00:40:25,656
DID YOUR GRANDFATHER GIVE YOU ANY REASONS ?

762
00:40:25,756 --> 00:40:28,192
REASONS ? IF I 'D EVER BEEN REASONED WITH ,

763
00:40:28,292 --> 00:40:31,159
I MIGHT HAVE BEEN A BETTER CHILD .

764
00:40:31,628 --> 00:40:33,798
MY OLD NURSERY 'S THROUGH THERE , ISN 'T IT ?

765
00:40:33,898 --> 00:40:36,899
I SHOULD THINK SO , IT HAD NURSERY WALLPAPER .

766
00:40:38,468 --> 00:40:41,269
HOW PRETTY YOUR SISTER 'S MADE IT .

767
00:40:46,843 --> 00:40:48,678
WHAT IS IT ?

768
00:40:48,778 --> 00:40:51,415
SOMETHING I 'VE FORGOTTEN .

769
00:40:51,515 --> 00:40:53,182
WHEN I WAS LITTLE ,

770
00:40:53,282 --> 00:40:56,183
I USED TO HAVE A DREAM ABOUT THIS ROOM .

771
00:40:56,719 --> 00:40:58,421
YOU DID ?

772
00:40:58,521 --> 00:40:59,823
I 'D BE LYING HERE ,

773
00:40:59,923 --> 00:41:02,957
AND IT WOULD BE DARK AND COLD AND FRIGHTENING .

774
00:41:03,960 --> 00:41:06,861
AND THEN ... A LITTLE FLAME WOULD COME- -

775
00:41:07,330 --> 00:41:10,130
JUST A TINY POINT OF LIGHT SO BIG- -

776
00:41:10,799 --> 00:41:13,135
AND YET SUDDENLY ...

777
00:41:13,235 --> 00:41:15,604
EVERYTHING WOULD BE WARM

778
00:41:15,704 --> 00:41:18,274
AND LIGHT AND PEACEFUL .

779
00:41:18,374 --> 00:41:19,641
AND THEN ...

780
00:41:19,741 --> 00:41:23,043
SOMEONE WOULD COME AND PUT THE FLAME OUT AND I 'D BE TERRIFIED .

781
00:41:23,311 --> 00:41:26,248
PERHAPS YOUR MOTHER USED TO BRING YOU A NIGHT-LIGHT .

782
00:41:26,348 --> 00:41:28,982
BUT WHO 'D TAKE IT OUT ?

783
00:41:30,685 --> 00:41:33,519
MAY I SEE THE STUDIO BEFORE IT 'S DARK ?

784
00:41:37,125 --> 00:41:40,293
IT 'S RATHER MESSY IN HERE . I WAS THINKING OF SKIPPING THIS .

785
00:41:41,696 --> 00:41:44,830
THIS IS WHERE MY FATHER PAINTED MY MOTHER 'S PICTURE .

786
00:41:46,166 --> 00:41:48,934
STRANGE TO THINK OF THEM HERE .

787
00:41:50,972 --> 00:41:54,106
MY FATHER WOULD HAVE HIS EASEL TO THE LIGHT , WOULDN 'T HE ?

788
00:41:55,442 --> 00:41:58,711
AND PERHAPS MY MOTHER WOULD SIT THERE IN A SOFT , WHITE DRESS .

789
00:41:59,847 --> 00:42:02,149
BUT SOMETIMES , OF COURSE , HE 'D PAINT THE OTHER ONE .

790
00:42:02,249 --> 00:42:05,384
- THE OTHER ONE ? - HE HAD A MODEL- - A FOREIGN GIRL .

791
00:42:05,952 --> 00:42:09,021
I 'VE NEVER BEEN ABLE TO FIND OUT MUCH ABOUT HER .

792
00:42:09,523 --> 00:42:12,426
PEOPLE GET AWFULLY HUSH-HUSH WHEN I ASK THEM .

793
00:42:12,526 --> 00:42:14,761
BETWEEN YOU AND ME AND THE GRAND PIANO ,

794
00:42:14,861 --> 00:42:17,731
I SUSPECT FATHER WAS A BIT OF A BAD HAT .

795
00:42:17,831 --> 00:42:19,466
ARTISTIC TEMPERAMENT ?

796
00:42:19,566 --> 00:42:21,167
VERY ARTISTIC , I 'M AFRAID .

797
00:42:21,267 --> 00:42:24,435
SOMETIMES , YOU KNOW , IT 'S QUITE A COMFORT TO ME .

798
00:42:25,538 --> 00:42:26,740
IN WHAT WAY ?

799
00:42:26,840 --> 00:42:28,942
IF FATHER HAD BEEN AS GOOD AS MOTHER ,

800
00:42:29,042 --> 00:42:31,377
THINK HOW GOOD I 'D HAVE BEEN .

801
00:42:31,477 --> 00:42:34,545
IT 'S GETTING ALMOST TOO DARK TO SEE YOU PROPERLY .

802
00:42:44,624 --> 00:42:47,292
WON 'T YOU PLAY SOMETHING ?

803
00:42:47,392 --> 00:42:50,226
IT 'S ABOUT TIME YOU ASKED ME THAT .

804
00:42:57,069 --> 00:42:59,803
( playing classical melody )

805
00:43:32,636 --> 00:43:34,505
( music stops )

806
00:43:34,605 --> 00:43:36,707
PLEASE GO ON .

807
00:43:36,807 --> 00:43:38,409
JUST A SECOND .

808
00:43:38,509 --> 00:43:40,677
- YOU MADE THAT UP ? - YES .

809
00:43:40,777 --> 00:43:43,680
- BUT YOU MUST BE BRILLIANT ! - OH , DAZZLING !

810
00:43:43,780 --> 00:43:45,949
PEOPLE HAVE TO WEAR SUNGLASSES .

811
00:43:46,049 --> 00:43:47,317
WHAT 'S IT CALLED ?

812
00:43:47,417 --> 00:43:50,451
IT 'S A SERENADE . " TO STELLA BY STARLIGHT . "

813
00:43:50,620 --> 00:43:53,390
- YOU MEAN , THIS STELLA ? - MM-HMM .

814
00:43:53,490 --> 00:43:56,657
IT 'S THE MOST EXCITING THING THAT 'S EVER HAPPENED TO ME .

815
00:43:56,759 --> 00:43:59,427
- IS IT ? - PLEASE GO ON .

816
00:44:04,567 --> 00:44:07,001
( music resumes )

817
00:44:08,571 --> 00:44:11,307
YOU SEE , THIS IS THE ONLY WAY I CAN PAINT YOU .

818
00:44:11,407 --> 00:44:14,208
SOME BLACK KEYS AND SOME WHITE ,

819
00:44:14,409 --> 00:44:17,079
AND FINGERS THAT ARE MUCH TOO CLUMSY ,

820
00:44:17,179 --> 00:44:19,913
BUT YOU 'RE IN IT , SOMEHOW .

821
00:44:27,123 --> 00:44:29,656
( melancholy tone )

822
00:44:36,465 --> 00:44:39,432
IT 'S GONE AWFULLY SAD . WHY HAVE YOU CHANGED IT ?

823
00:44:40,702 --> 00:44:43,369
IT JUST CAME OUT THAT WAY .

824
00:44:55,316 --> 00:44:56,584
WHAT 'S THE MATTER ?

825
00:44:56,684 --> 00:44:59,287
WHAT IS IT , STELLA ? YOU 'RE TREMBLING !

826
00:44:59,387 --> 00:45:00,621
OH , I WAS WICKED .

827
00:45:00,721 --> 00:45:02,923
HOW COULD I EVER HAVE LAUGHED IN HER HOUSE ?

828
00:45:03,023 --> 00:45:05,726
BUT IT 'S MY HOUSE NOW- - PAM 'S AND MINE .

829
00:45:05,826 --> 00:45:08,761
BUT SHE WAS SO YOUNG AND SHE DIED SO CRUELLY .

830
00:45:12,499 --> 00:45:14,833
STELLA !

831
00:45:15,670 --> 00:45:17,969
STELLA !

832
00:45:18,738 --> 00:45:19,940
RICK , WHAT IS IT ?

833
00:45:20,040 --> 00:45:22,974
I DON 'T KNOW . IT 'S THAT BLASTED ROOM !

834
00:45:23,943 --> 00:45:26,344
STELLA , STOP !

835
00:45:30,850 --> 00:45:33,150
STELLA !

836
00:45:34,253 --> 00:45:37,289
- FOR HEAVEN 'S SAKE , STELLA . - WHAT 'S THE MATTER , RICK ?

837
00:45:37,389 --> 00:45:39,158
YOU WERE GOING OVER THE EDGE .

838
00:45:39,258 --> 00:45:41,094
- WAS I ? - IF I HADN 'T CAUGHT YOU .

839
00:45:41,194 --> 00:45:43,763
I HADN 'T ANY SENSE OF DANGER AT ALL .

840
00:45:43,863 --> 00:45:45,598
LOOK .

841
00:45:45,698 --> 00:45:48,567
Stella : I THINK THIS IS WHERE MY MOTHER FELL .

842
00:45:48,667 --> 00:45:51,168
BY THE DEAD TREE .

843
00:45:51,503 --> 00:45:53,106
ARE YOU ALL RIGHT ?

844
00:45:53,206 --> 00:45:54,773
QUITE , THANKS- -

845
00:45:54,873 --> 00:45:56,308
EXCEPT DYING OF HUNGER .

846
00:45:56,408 --> 00:45:59,278
Pam : THEN YOU MUST COME AND GET SOME FOOD .

847
00:45:59,378 --> 00:46:00,112
DO YOU KNOW THIS IS OUR VERY FIRST PARTY

848
00:46:00,212 --> 00:46:01,947
IN THIS HOUSE ?

849
00:46:02,047 --> 00:46:04,182
- IS IT ? - SHALL WE SING HER THE SONG ?

850
00:46:04,282 --> 00:46:06,585
HIS INTRODUCTION TO MUSIC .

851
00:46:06,685 --> 00:46:07,285
LA !

852
00:46:07,385 --> 00:46:11,054
Pamela , Rick : WEE CHICKABIRDIE , TRA LA LA , LAID AN EGG ON THE VUNDYSULL

853
00:46:11,556 --> 00:46:13,091
THE VUNDYSULL BEGAN TO CRACK

854
00:46:13,191 --> 00:46:16,327
WEE CHICKABIRDIE , LA , LA , LA , WEE CHICKABIRDIE- -

855
00:46:16,427 --> 00:46:18,995
( woman screams within )

856
00:46:19,897 --> 00:46:21,633
STAY HERE .

857
00:46:21,733 --> 00:46:24,200
( screaming )

858
00:46:24,802 --> 00:46:27,105
LIZZIE , WHERE ARE YOU ? WHAT 'S THE MATTER ?

859
00:46:27,205 --> 00:46:30,172
Lizzie : MR. RODERICK ! MR. RODERICK !

860
00:46:35,780 --> 00:46:38,082
WHAT IS IT , LIZZIE ? ARE YOU HURT ?

861
00:46:38,182 --> 00:46:40,417
THE STUDIO DOOR .

862
00:46:40,517 --> 00:46:43,185
THERE 'S SOMETHING THERE .

863
00:46:43,754 --> 00:46:46,190
LOOK , LIZZIE , THERE 'S NOTHING THERE .

864
00:46:46,290 --> 00:46:47,524
THERE WAS !

865
00:46:47,624 --> 00:46:50,027
I SAW IT WITH ME OWN TWO EYES .

866
00:46:50,127 --> 00:46:51,028
WHAT ?

867
00:46:51,128 --> 00:46:54,028
IT WAS LIKE A MIST- - A CRAWLING MIST .

868
00:46:54,298 --> 00:46:57,201
YOU IMAGINED IT , JUST BECAUSE YOU HEARD THE HOUSE WAS HAUNTED .

869
00:46:57,301 --> 00:46:59,369
I HEARD NOTHING OF THE SORT , MR. RODERICK .

870
00:46:59,469 --> 00:47:02,371
HOLY SAINTS , ARE YOU TELLIN ' ME IT IS ?

871
00:47:02,839 --> 00:47:05,141
Pam : FOR HEAVENS SAKE , RICK , WHAT IS IT ?

872
00:47:05,241 --> 00:47:07,844
OH , LIZZIE 'S DREAMED UP A GHOST FOR HERSELF .

873
00:47:07,944 --> 00:47:10,146
COME ALONG , LIZZIE .

874
00:47:10,246 --> 00:47:11,547
OH , DARLING LIZZIE .

875
00:47:11,647 --> 00:47:13,683
I HAD JUST COME UPSTAIRS TO TURN DOWN THE BEDS ,

876
00:47:13,783 --> 00:47:16,752
AND THERE IT STOOD BY THE STUDIO DOOR , LOOKING DOWN AT ME .

877
00:47:16,852 --> 00:47:20,188
- A WOMAN , IT WAS . - FOUR STEPS BACK , IT WAS JUST A MIST .

878
00:47:20,856 --> 00:47:24,225
Lizzie : ' TWAS A WOMAN , I SWEAR IT . THE GHOST OF A WOMAN !

879
00:47:25,027 --> 00:47:28,061
Pam : COME SIT DOWN . YOU 'LL BE ALL RIGHT .

880
00:47:35,871 --> 00:47:37,873
HAVE SOME SHERRY , LIZZIE .

881
00:47:37,973 --> 00:47:38,774
JUST A DROP .

882
00:47:38,874 --> 00:47:41,676
I 'LL NOT SLEEP IN THIS HOUSE ANOTHER NIGHT , MR. RODERICK .

883
00:47:41,776 --> 00:47:44,679
- COME NOW , LIZZIE . - I WILL NOT ! I 'D SOONER DIE .

884
00:47:44,779 --> 00:47:46,615
SHE CAN GO TO THE JESSUP FARM .

885
00:47:46,715 --> 00:47:49,449
WHAT 'S HAPPENED TO STELLA ?

886
00:47:50,952 --> 00:47:53,920
Pam : SHE WAS WITH ME WHEN I CAME IN .

887
00:47:55,390 --> 00:47:57,690
STELLA ?

888
00:48:00,428 --> 00:48:03,062
STELLA , WHERE ARE YOU ?

889
00:48:05,266 --> 00:48:08,033
STELLA , ARE YOU IN THE HOUSE ?

890
00:48:12,139 --> 00:48:14,406
STELLA !

891
00:48:17,043 --> 00:48:19,511
PAMELA ! PAMELA !

892
00:48:23,751 --> 00:48:26,284
STELLA , DARLING .

893
00:48:27,387 --> 00:48:30,088
YES , RICK , WHAT 'S HAPPENED ?

894
00:48:30,991 --> 00:48:32,760
- WHAT IS IT ? - SHE 'S IN A DEAD FAINT .

895
00:48:32,860 --> 00:48:35,894
- THIS ROOM IS LIKE AN ICEBOX . - COLDER .

896
00:48:37,697 --> 00:48:38,932
WE 'LL HAVE TO GET A DOCTOR .

897
00:48:39,032 --> 00:48:42,100
THERE 'S ONE AT THE FIRST HOUSE IN THE VILLAGE .

898
00:48:43,270 --> 00:48:44,504
THAT 'S THE GIRL .

899
00:48:44,604 --> 00:48:47,073
WELL , WHAT KIND OF BOGEY DID YOU SEE ?

900
00:48:47,173 --> 00:48:49,409
I DIDN 'T SEE ANYTHING .

901
00:48:49,509 --> 00:48:52,377
FAINTED OUT OF SHEER CUSSEDNESS , HUH ?

902
00:48:52,812 --> 00:48:55,679
I CAN ONLY REMEMBER THE COLD COMING .

903
00:48:55,948 --> 00:48:58,348
HELLO , STELLA .

904
00:48:59,619 --> 00:49:00,953
HELLO .

905
00:49:01,053 --> 00:49:03,921
Doctor : YOU SUDDENLY FELT COLD ?

906
00:49:05,424 --> 00:49:07,193
IT WASN 'T JUST THAT .

907
00:49:07,293 --> 00:49:09,228
THE ROOM WENT COLD AND I WAS FRIGHTENED .

908
00:49:09,328 --> 00:49:11,463
YES . WELL , YOU JUST FORGET ABOUT IT FOR A BIT .

909
00:49:11,563 --> 00:49:14,133
MISS FITZGERALD HAS GOT SOME SOUP FOR YOU .

910
00:49:14,233 --> 00:49:17,100
SEE IF YOU CAN GET HER TO TAKE SOME .

911
00:49:27,961 --> 00:49:30,816
SHE 'LL DO ALL RIGHT . BUT IT 'S QUITE A NASTY CASE OF SHOCK .

912
00:49:30,916 --> 00:49:32,317
THAT 'S ALL ? YOU 'RE QUITE SURE ?

913
00:49:32,417 --> 00:49:35,351
- SIT DOWN . - YOU SEE , I BROUGHT HER HERE .

914
00:49:37,088 --> 00:49:38,656
TAKE THAT NEAT .

915
00:49:38,756 --> 00:49:41,059
CAN 'T SHE STAY THE NIGHT HERE ?

916
00:49:41,159 --> 00:49:43,794
OH , YES . BUT SUPPOSE THAT SPOOK STARTS HOWLING .

917
00:49:43,894 --> 00:49:47,196
- OH , YOUR SPOOK . - IT 'S JUST AN ECHO FROM A CAVE PROBABLY ,

918
00:49:47,365 --> 00:49:48,766
BUT IT SOUNDS LIKE A SPOOK .

919
00:49:48,866 --> 00:49:50,568
I 'D RATHER RISK IT THAN MOVE HER TONIGHT .

920
00:49:50,668 --> 00:49:53,270
THERE WAS SOME RATHER QUEER BUSINESS EARLIER THIS EVENING .

921
00:49:53,370 --> 00:49:55,840
THE CLIFF IS SO CLOSE AND SHE WALKED RIGHT TO THE EDGE ,

922
00:49:55,940 --> 00:49:59,140
- AND IF I HADN 'T CAUGHT HER- - - WE 'LL KEEP A CLOSE WATCH .

923
00:50:00,544 --> 00:50:01,779
WELL , DID SHE TAKE HER SOUP ?

924
00:50:01,879 --> 00:50:04,181
EIGHT SPOONFULS , AND THEN DRIFTED OFF TO SLEEP .

925
00:50:04,281 --> 00:50:06,416
SPLENDID . SHE 'LL SLEEP FOR HOURS NOW .

926
00:50:06,516 --> 00:50:07,784
WE 'LL KEEP ON WATCH HERE .

927
00:50:07,884 --> 00:50:10,954
YOU BETTER GO TO BED , MISS FITZGERALD . YOU 'RE LOOKING ALL IN .

928
00:50:11,054 --> 00:50:12,489
I 'D RATHER WATCH WITH YOU .

929
00:50:12,589 --> 00:50:14,958
- WOULD YOU LIKE SOME COFFEE ? - OH , THANKS .

930
00:50:15,058 --> 00:50:18,125
OH , PAM , WHO DO YOU THINK 'S MOVED IN WITH DR. SCOTT ?

931
00:50:18,928 --> 00:50:20,597
- OUR BOBBY . - NO !

932
00:50:20,697 --> 00:50:22,799
I FOUND THE POOR DOG IN THE STREET ONE DAY .

933
00:50:22,899 --> 00:50:24,834
HE WAS IN A PITIABLE STATE OF NERVES .

934
00:50:24,934 --> 00:50:26,435
- HOW IS HE NOW ? - FINE .

935
00:50:26,535 --> 00:50:28,371
BOBBY WAS THE VERY FIRST TO SEE THE GHOST .

936
00:50:28,471 --> 00:50:31,806
- PAMELA BELIEVES IT . - STOP HIDING YOUR HEAD IN THE SAND .

937
00:50:32,541 --> 00:50:34,243
YOU HEARD THE SOUNDS LAST NIGHT .

938
00:50:34,343 --> 00:50:36,612
LIZZIE 'S BEEN HALF FRIGHTENED OUT OF HER WITS

939
00:50:36,712 --> 00:50:38,680
AND STELLA 'S BEEN IN DEADLY DANGER TWICE .

940
00:50:38,780 --> 00:50:41,450
EVERYONE IN THE VILLAGE KNOWS THE HOUSE IS STRANGE .

941
00:50:41,550 --> 00:50:43,386
I EXPECTED SUPPORT FROM YOU .

942
00:50:43,486 --> 00:50:46,955
YOU MUST TELL US EVERYTHING YOU KNOW ABOUT THE PLACE AFTER I 'VE MADE THE COFFEE .

943
00:50:47,055 --> 00:50:49,392
UNFORTUNATELY , I 'M A NEWCOMER TO BIDDLECOMBE .

944
00:50:49,492 --> 00:50:51,693
YOU SEE , I 'VE ONLY LIVED HERE 12 YEARS .

945
00:50:51,793 --> 00:50:54,427
- ( chuckles ) - OH !

946
00:50:54,630 --> 00:50:57,565
IT 'S NOT ANCIENT HISTORY TO US . PLEASE GO ON .

947
00:50:57,665 --> 00:51:00,068
THE MODEL 'S NAME WAS CARMEL . SHE WAS SPANISH- -

948
00:51:00,168 --> 00:51:02,270
A SPANISH GYPSY , AND A THOROUGH BAD LOT .

949
00:51:02,370 --> 00:51:04,006
SO WAS MEREDITH , FROM WHAT I CAN GATHER .

950
00:51:04,106 --> 00:51:07,675
- DIDN 'T MRS. MEREDITH SUSPECT ? - SHE MUST HAVE , THE THING WAS AN OPEN SCANDAL .

951
00:51:07,775 --> 00:51:10,078
THE GIRL AND HE 'D HAVE BEEN STONED OUT OF THE VILLAGE

952
00:51:10,178 --> 00:51:13,248
IF IT HADN 'T BEEN FOR MARY MEREDITH . SHE WAS VERY MUCH ADMIRED .

953
00:51:13,348 --> 00:51:15,182
I SUPPOSE SHE JUST ACCEPTED THE SITUATION .

954
00:51:15,282 --> 00:51:17,184
AND SHE 'S STILL SOBBING HER HEART OUT ABOUT IT .

955
00:51:17,284 --> 00:51:19,987
- WHERE 'S CARMEL NOW ? - DEAD . SHE DIED IN THIS VERY HOUSE ,

956
00:51:20,087 --> 00:51:23,157
A WEEK AFTER MARY FELL FROM THE CLIFF TRYING TO SAVE HER FROM SUICIDE .

957
00:51:23,257 --> 00:51:26,825
- IRONIC , WASN 'T IT ? - IS IT KNOWN WHY THE GIRL TRIED TO KILL HERSELF ?

958
00:51:27,261 --> 00:51:28,930
MEREDITH 'S SAID TO HAVE TIRED OF HER .

959
00:51:29,030 --> 00:51:32,033
THINK OF IT- - THOSE TWO WOMEN STRUGGLING ON THE CLIFF .

960
00:51:32,133 --> 00:51:35,134
I WONDER IF MARY 'S DEATH COULD HAVE BEEN MURDER ?

961
00:51:35,569 --> 00:51:37,004
IT 'S BEEN HINTED AT , ALL RIGHT .

962
00:51:37,104 --> 00:51:39,406
THE WHOLE STORY WAS DUG UP AND EMBROIDERED

963
00:51:39,506 --> 00:51:40,874
WHEN STELLA 'S FATHER DIED .

964
00:51:40,974 --> 00:51:43,109
- WHEN WAS THAT ? - THREE YEARS AGO , ABROAD .

965
00:51:43,209 --> 00:51:44,978
HE NEVER CAME BACK TO WINDWARD .

966
00:51:45,078 --> 00:51:46,880
ALL OF THEM DEAD WITH THEIR SECRETS .

967
00:51:46,980 --> 00:51:49,883
ONE OF THEM 'S NOT QUITE DEAD ENOUGH FOR ME .

968
00:51:49,983 --> 00:51:52,118
DON 'T SAY THAT ABOUT THE POOR SOUL .

969
00:51:52,218 --> 00:51:54,520
I TELL YOU , RICK , IF A SPIRIT COMES BACK ,

970
00:51:54,620 --> 00:51:56,222
IT 'S FOR SOME PARTICULAR PURPOSE .

971
00:51:56,322 --> 00:51:58,191
THAT 'S MY SISTER 'S SPECIAL CROTCHET .

972
00:51:58,291 --> 00:51:59,725
WE 'VE GOT TO FIND OUT WHAT IT IS .

973
00:51:59,825 --> 00:52:02,926
I WISH I KNEW SOME MORE , BUT I 'M AFRAID I DON 'T .

974
00:52:03,196 --> 00:52:06,064
WHAT TIME IS YOUR WAILING LADY DUE ?

975
00:52:06,666 --> 00:52:07,300
ABOUT DAWN .

976
00:52:07,400 --> 00:52:10,668
WELL , WE OUGHT TO KNOW EACH OTHER PRETTY WELL BY THEN .

977
00:52:13,338 --> 00:52:15,074
21 HAND .

978
00:52:15,174 --> 00:52:16,075
I 'M OUT .

979
00:52:16,175 --> 00:52:19,142
- IS IT MY DEAL ? - IT WAS TWO HOURS AGO .

980
00:52:19,311 --> 00:52:20,913
( yawns )

981
00:52:21,013 --> 00:52:21,647
5 : 30 .

982
00:52:21,747 --> 00:52:24,881
YES , MOANING MARTHA SEEMS TO HAVE MISSED HER CUE .

983
00:52:27,086 --> 00:52:29,955
RICK , HAVE YOU BROUGHT SOME MORE FLOWERS IN ?

984
00:52:30,055 --> 00:52:31,256
NO . WHY ?

985
00:52:31,356 --> 00:52:34,326
DON 'T YOU NOTICE THE SCENT ? IT 'S OVERPOWERING .

986
00:52:34,426 --> 00:52:37,660
Dr. Scott : EXTRAORDINARY . HELIOTROPE , ISN 'T IT ?

987
00:52:40,098 --> 00:52:42,033
NO .

988
00:52:42,133 --> 00:52:44,567
NO , IT 'S MIMOSA .

989
00:52:45,870 --> 00:52:47,171
THERE 'S A LIGHT !

990
00:52:47,271 --> 00:52:49,107
WHERE DID THAT COME FROM ?

991
00:52:49,207 --> 00:52:51,807
IT 'S LIKE A NIGHT-LIGHT .

992
00:52:59,450 --> 00:53:01,816
SHE 'S GONE !

993
00:53:02,886 --> 00:53:04,955
RICK , THE WINDOW !

994
00:53:05,055 --> 00:53:08,156
- Stella : WHAT IS IT ? - Pam : WHERE ARE YOU , STELLA ?

995
00:53:18,401 --> 00:53:21,069
DON 'T BE AFRAID , STELLA .

996
00:53:22,072 --> 00:53:23,306
AFRAID ?

997
00:53:23,406 --> 00:53:25,142
WELL , WE WERE A LITTLE .

998
00:53:25,242 --> 00:53:28,209
I WANTED TO SEE THE DAWN- - WITH HER .

999
00:53:29,112 --> 00:53:30,613
HER ?

1000
00:53:30,713 --> 00:53:33,216
DON 'T YOU KNOW WHO IT IS IN YOUR HOUSE ?

1001
00:53:33,316 --> 00:53:36,150
- IT 'S MY MOTHER . - YOU SAW HER ?

1002
00:53:37,387 --> 00:53:38,555
I DIDN 'T SEE HER ,

1003
00:53:38,655 --> 00:53:41,589
BUT WHEN I WOKE , SHE WAS HERE IN THE ROOM .

1004
00:53:41,957 --> 00:53:44,060
IT WAS FULL OF HER SCENT .

1005
00:53:44,160 --> 00:53:47,027
I COULD FEEL HER PRESENCE EVERYWHERE .

1006
00:53:48,530 --> 00:53:51,298
AND THERE WAS SOMETHING ELSE ...

1007
00:53:51,500 --> 00:53:54,467
SOMETHING I 'VE NEVER KNOWN IN MY WHOLE LIFE .

1008
00:53:54,736 --> 00:53:56,305
Rick : WHAT ?

1009
00:53:56,405 --> 00:53:57,906
THE KNOWLEDGE THAT ...

1010
00:53:58,006 --> 00:53:59,508
SOMEONE LOVED ME VERY DEARLY .

1011
00:53:59,608 --> 00:54:02,709
NOW , COME ON , YOUNG STELLA , I 'LL TAKE YOU HOME .

1012
00:54:03,512 --> 00:54:04,813
BUT I DON 'T WANT TO GO .

1013
00:54:04,913 --> 00:54:07,649
SORRY , BUT I 'VE GOT TO GET SOME SLEEP , YOU KNOW .

1014
00:54:07,749 --> 00:54:09,751
BUT I CAN COME BACK ?

1015
00:54:09,851 --> 00:54:10,284
NO .

1016
00:54:10,384 --> 00:54:13,720
WHAT DO YOU MEAN ? YOU COULDN 'T WANT TO KEEP ME AWAY FROM HER .

1017
00:54:13,855 --> 00:54:16,692
STELLA , REMEMBER HOW ILL YOU WERE LAST NIGHT ?

1018
00:54:16,792 --> 00:54:18,693
BUT THAT WAS NOTHING TO DO WITH HER .

1019
00:54:18,793 --> 00:54:21,496
I WAS JUST FRIGHTENED AFTER WHAT LIZZIE SAID .

1020
00:54:21,596 --> 00:54:24,199
I TELL YOU , MY MOTHER WOULD NEVER HURT ME .

1021
00:54:24,299 --> 00:54:27,133
I SHAN 'T BE AFRAID AGAIN , PLEASE .

1022
00:54:30,070 --> 00:54:31,272
I 'M SORRY .

1023
00:54:31,372 --> 00:54:33,274
IT 'S JUST THAT MY KNEES ARE WOBBLY .

1024
00:54:33,374 --> 00:54:36,475
COME ALONG . DR. SCOTT WILL DRIVE YOU HOME .

1025
00:54:45,953 --> 00:54:48,486
( car motor starts )

1026
00:54:51,091 --> 00:54:53,393
I WONDER WHAT I 'VE DONE TO HER , PAMELA ,

1027
00:54:53,493 --> 00:54:55,029
BRINGING HER HERE .

1028
00:54:55,129 --> 00:54:56,630
DON 'T BLAME YOURSELF .

1029
00:54:56,730 --> 00:54:58,532
BUT THAT LOOK IN HER EYES- -

1030
00:54:58,632 --> 00:55:01,066
THAT TERRIBLE HAPPINESS .

1031
00:55:01,785 --> 00:55:02,802
OH !

1032
00:55:02,902 --> 00:55:06,303
WAIT A MINUTE , RICK . PERHAPS SHE 'S NEARER RIGHT THAN WE ARE .

1033
00:55:06,506 --> 00:55:09,041
- SHE 'S WHAT ? - PERHAPS SHE 'S RIGHT IN BEING HAPPY .

1034
00:55:09,141 --> 00:55:12,376
SUPPOSING MARY MEREDITH 'S SPIRIT HAD BEEN SEARCHING FOR STELLA ,

1035
00:55:12,846 --> 00:55:16,013
AND NOW THAT IT 'S FOUND HER , IT 'S FOUND PEACE .

1036
00:55:18,084 --> 00:55:20,619
SUPPOSE WE HAVEN 'T A GHOST ANYMORE .

1037
00:55:20,719 --> 00:55:22,488
WHERE ARE YOU GOING ?

1038
00:55:22,588 --> 00:55:23,555
TO THE STUDIO .

1039
00:55:23,655 --> 00:55:26,259
HOW HAS IT ALWAYS SHOWN ITSELF IN THE PAST ?

1040
00:55:26,359 --> 00:55:27,926
SOBBING SOUNDS DOWNSTAIRS

1041
00:55:28,026 --> 00:55:29,928
AND COLD AND DEPRESSION IN THE STUDIO .

1042
00:55:30,028 --> 00:55:31,997
THERE WASN 'T ANY SOBBING TONIGHT ,

1043
00:55:32,097 --> 00:55:33,465
ONLY WARMTH AND FRAGRANCE .

1044
00:55:33,565 --> 00:55:35,801
- BUT WHY THE STUDIO ? - I 'LL KNOW IN THERE .

1045
00:55:35,901 --> 00:55:38,935
I 'LL KNOW WHETHER IT 'S A DECENT HUMAN ROOM .

1046
00:55:39,604 --> 00:55:41,971
WON 'T YOU ?

1047
00:55:44,910 --> 00:55:47,445
IT MAY NOT BE QUITE SO COLD , REALLY .

1048
00:55:47,545 --> 00:55:49,981
STOP IT , PAM . IT 'S CLAMMY AND ROTTEN .

1049
00:55:50,081 --> 00:55:52,817
WHATEVER IT IS , IT 'S IN HERE WITH US .

1050
00:55:52,917 --> 00:55:54,919
LET 'S GET OUT .

1051
00:55:55,019 --> 00:55:57,553
( distant weeping )

1052
00:56:09,566 --> 00:56:11,135
( moaning )

1053
00:56:11,235 --> 00:56:13,503
MARY MEREDITH , PLEASE .

1054
00:56:13,603 --> 00:56:16,604
PLEASE ! WE 'RE SORRY YOU HAD TO SUFFER .

1055
00:56:17,741 --> 00:56:20,277
- ( weeping continues ) - ISN 'T THAT ENOUGH ?

1056
00:56:20,377 --> 00:56:22,146
WHAT MORE DO YOU WANT ?

1057
00:56:22,246 --> 00:56:24,315
YOU WERE RIGHT ABOUT ONE THING , PAM .

1058
00:56:24,415 --> 00:56:27,615
WE HAVEN 'T A GHOST ANYMORE- - WE 'VE GOT TWO OF THEM !

1059
00:56:32,088 --> 00:56:33,657
IS COMMANDER BEECH AT HOME ?

1060
00:56:33,757 --> 00:56:35,726
HE WON 'T BE BACK UNTIL THIS EVENING , SIR .

1061
00:56:35,826 --> 00:56:37,526
IT 'S STELLA THAT I REALLY WANT TO SEE .

1062
00:56:37,626 --> 00:56:40,962
- WON 'T YOU COME IN , SIR ? I 'LL TELL HER . - THANK YOU .

1063
00:56:45,168 --> 00:56:48,135
MISS STELLA 'S IN HER ROOM , SIR . I 'LL- -

1064
00:56:51,106 --> 00:56:52,508
- RICK . - STELLA .

1065
00:56:52,608 --> 00:56:55,511
- I KNEW YOU COULDN 'T MEAN IT . - MEAN WHAT ?

1066
00:56:55,611 --> 00:56:58,280
HAVEN 'T YOU COME TO TAKE ME TO WINDWARD ?

1067
00:56:58,380 --> 00:56:59,682
NO , STELLA .

1068
00:56:59,782 --> 00:57:02,616
YOU MUSTN 'T GO THERE AGAIN , EVER .

1069
00:57:03,853 --> 00:57:05,187
LISTEN , DARLING ,

1070
00:57:05,287 --> 00:57:06,889
I 'VE THOUGHT THIS THING OUT ,

1071
00:57:06,989 --> 00:57:08,590
AND YOU MUST GO AWAY FROM HERE .

1072
00:57:08,690 --> 00:57:11,026
- GO AWAY ? - YES , FOREVER .

1073
00:57:11,126 --> 00:57:12,027
YOU WOULDN 'T CARE ?

1074
00:57:12,127 --> 00:57:14,396
NOT IN THE LEAST , BECAUSE I 'LL BE COMING WITH YOU .

1075
00:57:14,496 --> 00:57:17,266
IT WON 'T BE LUXURY- - JUST THE SMALLEST LONDON FLAT- -

1076
00:57:17,366 --> 00:57:20,269
BUT IT WILL BE OURS . AND NO UNSEEN , UNINVITED GUESTS .

1077
00:57:20,369 --> 00:57:23,571
- AND WINDWARD ? - WE 'LL TEAR IT DOWN AND FORGET IT .

1078
00:57:23,671 --> 00:57:24,539
AND MY MOTHER ?

1079
00:57:24,639 --> 00:57:27,041
BUT STELLA , YOU 'RE TALKING OF A DREAM AND A MEMORY .

1080
00:57:27,141 --> 00:57:30,242
I 'M TALKING ABOUT MY MOTHER . SHE 'S BEEN WAITING FOR ME .

1081
00:57:30,478 --> 00:57:33,178
IN SOME QUEER SORT OF WAY ,

1082
00:57:33,381 --> 00:57:34,248
I ALWAYS KNEW IT .

1083
00:57:34,348 --> 00:57:37,817
BUT WHAT ABOUT ME ? I WAS UNDER THE IMPRESSION THAT YOU CARED FOR ME .

1084
00:57:38,052 --> 00:57:39,720
THIS HASN 'T ANYTHING TO DO WITH YOU .

1085
00:57:39,820 --> 00:57:43,288
YOU TALK ABOUT DESTROYING THAT HOUSE- - YOU 'D BE TEARING ME APART .

1086
00:57:44,658 --> 00:57:45,826
STOP IT , STELLA .

1087
00:57:45,926 --> 00:57:47,594
DO YOU CARE FOR ME , OR DON 'T YOU ?

1088
00:57:47,694 --> 00:57:50,697
I CAN 'T THINK ABOUT YOU , NOT WHILE SHE 'S OUT THERE .

1089
00:57:50,797 --> 00:57:52,266
TAKE ME THERE , RICK .

1090
00:57:52,366 --> 00:57:54,601
BUT THIS IS HORRIBLE , UNHEALTHY STUFF .

1091
00:57:54,701 --> 00:57:56,236
PUT IT OUT OF YOUR MIND , STELLA .

1092
00:57:56,336 --> 00:57:58,906
TURN YOUR BACK ON THE PAST AND RUN , RUN HARD !

1093
00:57:59,006 --> 00:58:00,607
I 'LL GO THERE SOMEHOW .

1094
00:58:00,707 --> 00:58:02,810
YOU WON 'T , I PROMISE YOU .

1095
00:58:02,910 --> 00:58:04,978
I HATE YOU FOR THAT .

1096
00:58:05,078 --> 00:58:07,378
STELLA !

1097
00:58:09,749 --> 00:58:12,650
YOU SHAN 'T MAKE ME FORGET HER ! YOU SHAN 'T !

1098
00:58:17,156 --> 00:58:18,458
OH !

1099
00:58:18,558 --> 00:58:20,760
THAT 'S ENOUGH , BOBBY , THAT 'S ENOUGH !

1100
00:58:20,860 --> 00:58:22,462
YOU 'LL GET LIPSTICK POISONING .

1101
00:58:22,562 --> 00:58:24,597
HE 'S GOT A PASSION FOR HARD-BOILED EGGS .

1102
00:58:24,697 --> 00:58:26,265
- DID YOU KNOW ? - AND TURNIP TOPS .

1103
00:58:26,365 --> 00:58:29,134
I DON 'T THINK HE HAS ANY IDEA HE 'S A DOG . NOT REALLY .

1104
00:58:29,234 --> 00:58:31,804
OF COURSE , HE THINKS HE HAS A RATHER ODD FIGURE FOR A MAN .

1105
00:58:31,904 --> 00:58:35,238
I DIDN 'T QUESTION HIM VERY CLOSELY ABOUT WHERE HE BELONGED .

1106
00:58:35,574 --> 00:58:37,609
YOU SEE , I WAS AFRAID I MIGHT FIND OUT .

1107
00:58:37,709 --> 00:58:39,644
- I 'M SORRY NOW . - YOU 'RE SORRY ?

1108
00:58:39,744 --> 00:58:41,546
YES . I SHOULD HAVE MET YOU SOONER .

1109
00:58:41,646 --> 00:58:43,915
Rick : ARE YOU THERE , SCOTT ?

1110
00:58:44,015 --> 00:58:46,251
IN HERE .

1111
00:58:46,351 --> 00:58:47,619
Pam : DID YOU SEE STELLA ?

1112
00:58:47,719 --> 00:58:49,955
YES , I DID . SCOTT , YOU 'VE GOT TO DO SOMETHING ABOUT THAT GIRL .

1113
00:58:50,055 --> 00:58:52,591
- SHE 'S ON THE EDGE OF A NERVOUS COLLAPSE . - YOU 'RE TELLING ME ?

1114
00:58:52,691 --> 00:58:55,326
THIS IS HARDLY A CASE FOR A COUNTRY DOCTOR , YOU KNOW .

1115
00:58:55,426 --> 00:58:57,028
Pam : WHEN DOES THE COMMANDER GET BACK ?

1116
00:58:57,128 --> 00:58:59,464
LAST TRAIN TONIGHT . HEAVEN HELP YOUNG STELLA THEN .

1117
00:58:59,564 --> 00:59:01,499
CAN 'T YOU CONVINCE HER THAT HER MOTHER

1118
00:59:01,599 --> 00:59:03,468
WOULDN 'T WANT HER TO GO NEAR THAT BLASTED HOUSE ?

1119
00:59:03,568 --> 00:59:05,669
NOT I. SHE 'S BEEN LISTENING FOR A VOICE

1120
00:59:05,769 --> 00:59:07,738
THAT 'S BEEN STILL FOR 17 YEARS .

1121
00:59:07,838 --> 00:59:09,173
I CAN GIVE HER A SEDATIVE .

1122
00:59:09,273 --> 00:59:12,143
WHY DON 'T WE TRY TO GET A MESSAGE FROM MARY MEREDITH ?

1123
00:59:12,243 --> 00:59:14,312
- DO WHAT ? - WE COULD HOLD A SEANCE .

1124
00:59:14,412 --> 00:59:15,480
YOU 'RE NOT SERIOUS !

1125
00:59:15,580 --> 00:59:18,483
THAT 'S HOW THE DEAD ARE SUPPOSED TO COMMUNICATE WITH THE LIVING .

1126
00:59:18,583 --> 00:59:20,751
Rick : ACCORDING TO THE IDIOT FRINGE .

1127
00:59:20,851 --> 00:59:22,219
YOU HAVE NO RIGHT TO SAY THAT .

1128
00:59:22,319 --> 00:59:24,688
MANY INTELLIGENT PEOPLE BELIEVE IN SPIRITUALISM .

1129
00:59:24,788 --> 00:59:26,289
HAVE YOU EVER BEEN TO A SEANCE ?

1130
00:59:26,389 --> 00:59:29,159
- I HAVE . - SHADED LIGHTS , THE ALPHABET LAID OUT ON A TABLE ,

1131
00:59:29,259 --> 00:59:32,695
AN UPSIDE-DOWN WINE GLASS , MESSAGES FROM SOMEBODY 'S UNCLE OSWALD ,

1132
00:59:32,795 --> 00:59:34,564
HOW TO FIND A MISLAID TOOTHBRUSH- - OH !

1133
00:59:34,664 --> 00:59:37,732
OH , STOP SCOFFING , RICK . NOT ALL SEANCES ARE FAKED .

1134
00:59:39,936 --> 00:59:41,304
ALL RIGHT , WE 'LL HAVE A SEANCE .

1135
00:59:41,404 --> 00:59:45,008
IT SHOULDN 'T BE DIFFICULT TO MOVE A WINE GLASS AROUND AND SAY IT 'S MARY MEREDITH .

1136
00:59:45,108 --> 00:59:47,844
- WHAT DO YOU THINK , SCOTT ? - LEAVE ME OUT OF THIS .

1137
00:59:47,944 --> 00:59:49,245
I WON 'T LET YOU CHEAT STELLA .

1138
00:59:49,345 --> 00:59:51,414
BUT WHAT DO YOU EXPECT MARY MEREDITH TO TELL HER ?

1139
00:59:51,514 --> 00:59:54,216
ENTRUST YOUR LIFE TO A TALL , DARK MAN , EXCRUCIATINGLY HANDSOME ?

1140
00:59:54,316 --> 00:59:56,719
CRIKEY , NO ! I WANT TO SET STELLA 'S MIND AT REST .

1141
00:59:56,819 --> 00:59:59,355
- SHE 'S ABOUT TORN IN TWO . - WELL , I WILL SAY THIS- -

1142
00:59:59,455 --> 01:00:01,590
UNLESS THE CONFLICT INSIDE HER IS STOPPED ,

1143
01:00:01,690 --> 01:00:03,426
IT MAY EVEN AFFECT HER REASON .

1144
01:00:03,526 --> 01:00:05,694
WELL , HERE 'S A MESSAGE THAT MIGHT DO IT- -

1145
01:00:05,794 --> 01:00:07,363
STELLA , THIS IS YOUR MOTHER .

1146
01:00:07,463 --> 01:00:09,465
SINCE I 'VE FOUND YOU , I 'VE FOUND PEACE .

1147
01:00:09,565 --> 01:00:11,066
STAY AWAY FROM WINDWARD HOUSE .

1148
01:00:11,166 --> 01:00:13,602
- BUT STELLA WOULD HAVE TO BE AT THE SEANCE . - NATURALLY .

1149
01:00:13,702 --> 01:00:16,905
IT 'LL HAVE TO BE AT WINDWARD , AND IT 'S DANGEROUS FOR HER TO BE THERE .

1150
01:00:17,005 --> 01:00:20,339
- BUT WE 'D BE WITH HER ALL THE TIME . - IT MAY BE WORTH A TRY .

1151
01:00:30,552 --> 01:00:33,619
THE IMPORTANT THING IS THAT WE SHOULD ALL BELIEVE- -

1152
01:00:33,988 --> 01:00:35,590
ISN 'T IT , DR. SCOTT ?

1153
01:00:35,690 --> 01:00:38,059
SO I UNDERSTAND . WHAT NOW ?

1154
01:00:38,159 --> 01:00:41,026
EVERYBODY PUTS A FINGER ON THE GLASS .

1155
01:00:43,498 --> 01:00:46,566
PERHAPS YOU SHOULD ASK SOME QUESTIONS , STELLA .

1156
01:00:49,336 --> 01:00:51,804
IS ANYBODY HERE ?

1157
01:01:04,251 --> 01:01:06,984
Stella : ARE YOU MY MOTHER ?

1158
01:01:11,491 --> 01:01:14,792
YOU DON 'T WANT ME TO STAY AWAY FROM WINDWARD , DO YOU , MOTHER ?

1159
01:01:24,904 --> 01:01:26,572
I KNEW IT , MOTHER .

1160
01:01:26,672 --> 01:01:28,241
I WANT TO BE NEAR YOU , TOO .

1161
01:01:28,341 --> 01:01:31,308
IS THAT WHY YOU STAY HERE , JUST TO BE NEAR ME ?

1162
01:01:35,881 --> 01:01:37,517
BUT YOU 'RE HOLDING IT , RICK .

1163
01:01:37,617 --> 01:01:40,152
AND YOU , DR. SCOTT , HOLDING IT HARD .

1164
01:01:40,252 --> 01:01:42,886
TAKE YOUR FINGERS OFF .

1165
01:01:44,422 --> 01:01:46,659
IS THAT YOUR REASON , DARLING ,

1166
01:01:46,759 --> 01:01:49,259
JUST TO BE NEAR ME ?

1167
01:01:55,900 --> 01:01:58,301
BUT WHAT ELSE ?

1168
01:02:01,773 --> 01:02:03,608
I ...

1169
01:02:03,708 --> 01:02:05,941
G ...

1170
01:02:07,512 --> 01:02:08,946
U ...

1171
01:02:09,046 --> 01:02:10,382
A ...

1172
01:02:10,482 --> 01:02:11,383
" I GUARD . "

1173
01:02:11,483 --> 01:02:14,449
YOU MEAN , YOU GUARD ME , FROM SOME DANGER ?

1174
01:02:18,256 --> 01:02:20,589
BUT WHAT ?

1175
01:02:22,093 --> 01:02:23,961
C ...

1176
01:02:24,061 --> 01:02:26,262
A ...

1177
01:02:27,765 --> 01:02:30,099
R ... M ...

1178
01:02:30,967 --> 01:02:33,568
Rick , Pam : " CARMEL " !

1179
01:02:40,410 --> 01:02:42,844
( glass breaks )

1180
01:02:43,614 --> 01:02:45,315
- THAT 'S ENOUGH . - IT IS , INDEED .

1181
01:02:45,415 --> 01:02:48,183
LET 'S GO INTO THE OTHER ROOM .

1182
01:02:49,485 --> 01:02:50,754
STELLA , WHAT IS IT ? !

1183
01:02:50,854 --> 01:02:53,955
- ARE YOU ILL , STELLA ? - QUIET . LEAVE HER ALONE .

1184
01:02:54,424 --> 01:02:56,326
OIGNAN . OIGNAN !

1185
01:02:56,426 --> 01:02:58,528
- STOP HER , SCOTT . - SHH . SHE 'S IN A TRANCE .

1186
01:02:58,628 --> 01:03:01,831
I SAW THIS HAPPEN ONCE BEFORE AT A SEANCE . I THOUGHT IT WAS A FAKE .

1187
01:03:01,931 --> 01:03:04,867
- BUT THIS ISN 'T . - I KNOW , AND IT 'S DANGEROUS .

1188
01:03:04,967 --> 01:03:07,570
- MAY I ASK HER SOME QUESTIONS ? - NO , NO !

1189
01:03:07,670 --> 01:03:09,672
IT MAY BE BEST TO TRY AND REACH HER MIND .

1190
01:03:09,772 --> 01:03:12,673
NOW KEEP YOUR VOICE QUIET AND REASSURING .

1191
01:03:14,376 --> 01:03:17,279
ARE YOU MARY MEREDITH , STELLA 'S MOTHER ?

1192
01:03:17,379 --> 01:03:20,080
EYA NO 'E . EYA NO 'E .

1193
01:03:20,515 --> 01:03:21,617
NO LE CREAN NA !

1194
01:03:21,717 --> 01:03:24,419
NO LE PONGAN OIDOS QUE ESTA MINTIENDO .

1195
01:03:24,519 --> 01:03:26,555
DON 'T ASK HER ANYMORE !

1196
01:03:26,655 --> 01:03:27,922
( doorbell jingling )

1197
01:03:28,022 --> 01:03:31,225
Pam : THAT 'S THE DOORBELL . SHALL I ANSWER IT ?

1198
01:03:31,493 --> 01:03:32,761
LIZZIE 'S AT THE JESSUPS .

1199
01:03:32,861 --> 01:03:35,497
NO , DON 'T MOVE UNTIL SHE 'S OVER THE WORST OF THIS .

1200
01:03:35,597 --> 01:03:38,399
So ladrona ! Ladrona de mi cariño !

1201
01:03:38,499 --> 01:03:41,402
- THAT 'S SPANISH , ISN 'T IT , SCOTT ? - I DON 'T KNOW .

1202
01:03:41,502 --> 01:03:44,203
RICK , THE MIMOSA SCENT !

1203
01:03:45,573 --> 01:03:47,142
THE ROOM 'S FULL OF IT !

1204
01:03:47,242 --> 01:03:49,710
MARY MEREDITH 'S IN HERE , TOO !

1205
01:03:49,810 --> 01:03:51,312
( gasps )

1206
01:03:51,412 --> 01:03:53,281
( doorbell jingles )

1207
01:03:53,381 --> 01:03:54,715
THE COLD .

1208
01:03:54,815 --> 01:03:57,385
IT 'S NEVER BEEN COLD IN HERE .

1209
01:03:57,485 --> 01:04:00,151
CANDLES ! LOOK AT THE CANDLES !

1210
01:04:02,723 --> 01:04:04,925
( Stella sobbing )

1211
01:04:05,025 --> 01:04:06,494
( doorbell jingles )

1212
01:04:06,594 --> 01:04:09,561
- Pam : I 'D BETTER ANSWER IT . - ALL RIGHT .

1213
01:04:10,530 --> 01:04:12,432
STOP , PAMELA !

1214
01:04:12,532 --> 01:04:15,200
DON 'T GO NEAR THAT DOOR .

1215
01:04:26,513 --> 01:04:29,146
IT 'S COMING TOWARD US !

1216
01:04:31,551 --> 01:04:33,984
( glass breaks )

1217
01:04:37,657 --> 01:04:40,324
WHAT IN THUNDER IS THIS ? !

1218
01:04:40,727 --> 01:04:42,494
STELLA ! STELLA , IT 'S ALL RIGHT NOW .

1219
01:04:42,594 --> 01:04:44,297
- WE MUST GET HER OUT . - Scott : YES .

1220
01:04:44,397 --> 01:04:46,799
WHAT HAVE YOU BEEN DOING TO THE CHILD ?

1221
01:04:46,899 --> 01:04:49,800
WHAT 'S THE MEANING OF THIS , DR. SCOTT ?

1222
01:04:50,069 --> 01:04:51,937
I CAN 'T EXPLAIN NOW , COMMANDER .

1223
01:04:52,037 --> 01:04:53,306
THIS IS INCREDIBLE BEHAVIOR !

1224
01:04:53,406 --> 01:04:56,175
QUIETLY , STELLA , QUIETLY . THERE 'S NOTHING TO BE FRIGHTENED OF .

1225
01:04:56,275 --> 01:04:58,844
- CONTROL YOURSELF , CHILD ! - DON 'T SPEAK TO HER LIKE THAT !

1226
01:04:58,944 --> 01:05:01,313
YOU 'RE RESPONSIBLE FOR THIS- - YOU AND YOUR CRIMINAL MEDDLING .

1227
01:05:01,413 --> 01:05:04,915
I AM AND SO ARE YOU . WHY DIDN 'T YOU TELL US THE TRUTH ABOUT THE HOUSE ?

1228
01:05:05,150 --> 01:05:06,985
- I WARNED YOU . - ONLY OF IDLE GOSSIP !

1229
01:05:07,085 --> 01:05:08,654
PERHAPS YOU 'D LIKE YOUR MONEY BACK .

1230
01:05:08,754 --> 01:05:10,723
YOU SHALL HAVE IT- - THE ENTIRE PURCHASE PRICE .

1231
01:05:10,823 --> 01:05:12,791
NO , THANK YOU , COMMANDER . I KNOW THIS NOW- -

1232
01:05:12,891 --> 01:05:15,293
STELLA WILL NEVER BE WELL UNTIL THIS HOUSE IS CURED .

1233
01:05:15,393 --> 01:05:17,028
AND SOMEHOW , WE 'RE GOING TO CURE IT !

1234
01:05:17,128 --> 01:05:20,196
DR. SCOTT , HAVE THE GOODNESS TO DRIVE US HOME .

1235
01:05:22,667 --> 01:05:25,601
THERE . NOW YOU 'LL SLEEP ALL RIGHT .

1236
01:05:28,806 --> 01:05:30,708
I 'LL BE HERE EARLY IN THE MORNING .

1237
01:05:30,808 --> 01:05:33,410
STELLA IS NO LONGER YOUR PATIENT , NOR AM I.

1238
01:05:33,510 --> 01:05:35,246
BUT SOMEONE MUST LOOK AFTER HER .

1239
01:05:35,346 --> 01:05:38,146
THAT IS NOT YOUR CONCERN , DR. SCOTT .

1240
01:05:43,187 --> 01:05:46,190
I SHALL BE AT YOUR DISPOSAL AT ANY HOUR , REMEMBER .

1241
01:05:46,290 --> 01:05:48,656
THANK YOU .

1242
01:05:50,126 --> 01:05:52,894
EVERYTHING WILL BE ALL RIGHT .

1243
01:05:56,733 --> 01:05:59,534
WON 'T YOU COME IN , MISS HOLLOWAY ?

1244
01:06:02,305 --> 01:06:04,973
- IS SHE ASLEEP ? - NOT YET .

1245
01:06:13,649 --> 01:06:16,083
HELLO , STELLA .

1246
01:06:16,986 --> 01:06:18,521
MISS HOLLOWAY .

1247
01:06:18,621 --> 01:06:21,222
GO TO SLEEP , STELLA .

1248
01:06:28,497 --> 01:06:31,534
DR. SCOTT TELLS ME SHE WENT INTO A TRANCE TONIGHT- -

1249
01:06:31,634 --> 01:06:33,936
SPOKE SOME WORDS THEY THOUGHT WERE SPANISH .

1250
01:06:34,036 --> 01:06:35,738
HOW DID SHE HAPPEN TO BE AT WINDWARD ?

1251
01:06:35,838 --> 01:06:38,908
THE PEOPLE WHO BOUGHT THE PLACE ARE SEARCHING INTO ITS PAST .

1252
01:06:39,008 --> 01:06:40,409
ARE THEY INDEED !

1253
01:06:40,509 --> 01:06:42,110
CAN YOU MAKE THE CHILD WELL AGAIN ?

1254
01:06:42,210 --> 01:06:44,913
I HOPE SO . IT WON 'T BE A SHORT PROCESS .

1255
01:06:45,013 --> 01:06:46,981
SHE 'S FAR MORE ILL THAN YOU IMAGINE .

1256
01:06:47,081 --> 01:06:48,550
SHE WON 'T WANT TO GO WITH YOU .

1257
01:06:48,650 --> 01:06:50,585
SHE 'S NEVER OUTGROWN HER CHILDISH FEAR OF YOU .

1258
01:06:50,685 --> 01:06:53,521
I COULD HAVE CURED IT YEARS AGO IF YOU 'D LET ME HAVE HER ,

1259
01:06:53,621 --> 01:06:55,122
AS MARY WOULD HAVE WISHED ME TO .

1260
01:06:55,222 --> 01:06:58,791
HER PLACE WAS IN MARY 'S HOME . I 'VE TAUGHT HER TO BE LIKE MARY IN EVERY WAY .

1261
01:06:59,827 --> 01:07:01,462
HOW CAN YOU SAY SUCH A THING ? !

1262
01:07:01,562 --> 01:07:03,164
SHE 'S NOT SO BEAUTIFUL , OF COURSE .

1263
01:07:03,264 --> 01:07:04,999
Miss Holloway : MARY WAS A GODDESS !

1264
01:07:05,099 --> 01:07:08,300
HER SKIN WAS RADIANT , AND THAT BRIGHT , BRIGHT HAIR !

1265
01:07:09,736 --> 01:07:12,440
HOW THIS ROOM BRINGS HER BACK TO ME .

1266
01:07:12,540 --> 01:07:15,674
THE NIGHTS WE SAT TALKING IN FRONT OF THAT FIREPLACE ,

1267
01:07:15,842 --> 01:07:17,244
PLANNING OUR WHOLE LIVES .

1268
01:07:17,344 --> 01:07:20,113
IT WASN 'T FLIRTATIONS AND DRESSES WE TALKED ABOUT .

1269
01:07:20,213 --> 01:07:22,883
WE WERE NO SILLY , GIGGLING GIRLS .

1270
01:07:22,983 --> 01:07:25,684
WE INTENDED TO CONQUER LIFE .

1271
01:07:26,086 --> 01:07:27,354
YOU AT LEAST DID .

1272
01:07:27,454 --> 01:07:30,521
WILL YOU TRY TO TAKE MARY 'S PLACE WITH HER NOW ?

1273
01:07:31,224 --> 01:07:33,624
I 'LL DO MY BEST .

1274
01:07:34,194 --> 01:07:35,863
Miss Holloway : SHE 'S ASLEEP .

1275
01:07:35,963 --> 01:07:38,698
IF YOU 'LL CALL MY CHAUFFEUR , HE 'LL CARRY HER DOWNSTAIRS .

1276
01:07:38,798 --> 01:07:41,468
IT WILL BE BETTER FOR HER TO WAKE AT MY PLACE .

1277
01:07:41,568 --> 01:07:44,268
I 'M DEEPLY GRATEFUL TO YOU .

1278
01:07:48,908 --> 01:07:51,675
SO THEY 'RE SEARCHING INTO THE PAST ?

1279
01:07:55,314 --> 01:07:58,150
THEY SHAN 'T EVER FIND OUT , MY DARLING- -

1280
01:07:58,250 --> 01:08:00,683
I PROMISE YOU !

1281
01:08:03,222 --> 01:08:05,757
Rick : ELIZABETH FLYNN , WHERE ARE YOU ?

1282
01:08:05,857 --> 01:08:07,626
I 'M HERE , MR. RODERICK .

1283
01:08:07,726 --> 01:08:10,362
AND WILL YOU PLEASE COME HERE AT ONCE ?

1284
01:08:10,462 --> 01:08:13,399
DON 'T WE GET ANY BREAKFAST ? WHAT 'S THE MATTER ?

1285
01:08:13,499 --> 01:08:15,467
OH- - OH , THAT !

1286
01:08:15,567 --> 01:08:17,235
THAT HAPPENED LAST NIGHT .

1287
01:08:17,335 --> 01:08:19,270
I AM NOT TALKING ABOUT THAT .

1288
01:08:19,370 --> 01:08:21,105
I AM TALKING ABOUT THIS .

1289
01:08:21,205 --> 01:08:23,341
THE ANAGRAM LETTERS ? YES , YES .

1290
01:08:23,441 --> 01:08:24,910
ANAGRAMS , IS IT ?

1291
01:08:25,010 --> 01:08:27,178
DON 'T YOU TRY TO BLUFF ME , MR. RODERICK .

1292
01:08:27,278 --> 01:08:29,213
'TIS A HEATHEN DEVICE TO CALL DEVILS OUT OF HELL .

1293
01:08:29,313 --> 01:08:32,849
STOP LOOKING AT ME AS THOUGH YOU WERE GOING TO TAKE AWAY MY BICYCLE .

1294
01:08:32,951 --> 01:08:35,353
I WILL NOT STAY IN A HOUSE WHERE IT GOES ON ,

1295
01:08:35,453 --> 01:08:36,921
AND THAT IS AN ULTIMATO !

1296
01:08:37,021 --> 01:08:38,222
OH , COME NOW , LIZZIE .

1297
01:08:38,322 --> 01:08:40,724
FROM NOW ON WE 'RE THROUGH WITH ALL THIS RUBBISH .

1298
01:08:40,824 --> 01:08:43,361
- WE 'RE GOING AFTER THE FACTS . - Pam : WHAT FACTS ?

1299
01:08:43,461 --> 01:08:45,195
THE FACTS ABOUT THIS BLASTED HAUNTING .

1300
01:08:45,295 --> 01:08:47,532
RICK , WHY BURDEN LIZZIE WITH THIS ?

1301
01:08:47,632 --> 01:08:50,699
WHISHT NOW , MISS PAM . WHERE WILL WE START , MR. RICK ?

1302
01:08:51,068 --> 01:08:52,936
I DON 'T KNOW . EVERYBODY SEEMS TO BE DEAD .

1303
01:08:53,036 --> 01:08:55,205
- THE TRAINED NURSE ISN 'T . - WHAT TRAINED NURSE ?

1304
01:08:55,305 --> 01:08:59,007
SHE WAS HERE WHEN IT HAPPENED- - THE FRIEND OF THE POOR LADY THAT WENT OVER THE CLIFF .

1305
01:09:00,010 --> 01:09:01,411
WHERE DID YOU HEAR ALL THIS ?

1306
01:09:01,511 --> 01:09:04,148
NOW WHAT DO YOU SUPPOSE WE TALK OF AT THE JESSUPS ?

1307
01:09:04,248 --> 01:09:06,516
IT WAS THE TRAINED NURSE THAT SHOUTED DOWN

1308
01:09:06,616 --> 01:09:08,152
TO MR. JESSUP ON THE SHORE .

1309
01:09:08,252 --> 01:09:09,952
WAS JESSUP IN ON THE TRAGEDY ?

1310
01:09:10,052 --> 01:09:11,788
HE WAS AFTER SOME LOST SHEEP .

1311
01:09:11,888 --> 01:09:13,723
THE TIDE WAS OUT , SO HE WENT DOWN .

1312
01:09:13,823 --> 01:09:15,859
AND AS HE PASSED UNDER THE DEAD TREE ,

1313
01:09:15,959 --> 01:09:17,894
- HE HEARD A SCREAM . - MRS. MEREDITH ?

1314
01:09:17,994 --> 01:09:20,895
NO , ' TWAS THE SCREAM OF A TERRIFIED CHILD .

1315
01:09:21,130 --> 01:09:22,765
AND AS HE RAN TOWARDS IT ,

1316
01:09:22,865 --> 01:09:25,001
THE POOR LADY CAME CRASHING DOWN .

1317
01:09:25,101 --> 01:09:26,969
'TWAS THEN THAT THE NURSE CALLED .

1318
01:09:27,069 --> 01:09:28,671
LIZZIE FLYNN , YOU 'RE A GOLD MINE .

1319
01:09:28,771 --> 01:09:31,273
NOW IF WE COULD ONLY GET THE NAME OF THIS NURSE .

1320
01:09:31,373 --> 01:09:34,041
SURE , THAT 'S EASY . WAIT NOW .

1321
01:09:36,011 --> 01:09:37,979
- MR. JESSUP ! - YES , MRS. FLYNN ?

1322
01:09:38,079 --> 01:09:38,847
WHAT WAS THE NAME OF MRS. MEREDITH 'S

1323
01:09:38,947 --> 01:09:41,116
TRAINED NURSE- -

1324
01:09:41,216 --> 01:09:43,452
THE ONE THAT GOT SO FAMOUS AND GRAND ?

1325
01:09:43,552 --> 01:09:46,119
- MISS HOLLOWAY . - AH !

1326
01:09:46,689 --> 01:09:47,923
MISS HOLLOWAY .

1327
01:09:48,023 --> 01:09:50,092
SHE 'S A BIG , FINE PLACE OF HER OWN NOW- -

1328
01:09:50,192 --> 01:09:52,761
A HOSPITAL , LIKE . 'TIS ON BODMIN MOOR .

1329
01:09:52,861 --> 01:09:55,829
SHE CALLS IT " THE MARY MEREDITH RETREAT . "

1330
01:10:06,106 --> 01:10:09,008
- MR. AND MISS FITZGERALD ? - Rick : YES .

1331
01:10:09,176 --> 01:10:11,977
- WON 'T YOU COME IN ? - THANK YOU .

1332
01:10:17,785 --> 01:10:19,120
WAIT IN THERE , PLEASE .

1333
01:10:19,220 --> 01:10:22,120
I WILL ANNOUNCE YOU TO MISS HOLLOWAY .

1334
01:10:39,740 --> 01:10:42,674
THE PLACE IS QUITE STUNNING , ISN 'T IT ?

1335
01:10:43,544 --> 01:10:45,646
WHY ARE YOU WHISPERING ?

1336
01:10:45,746 --> 01:10:48,112
WHY ARE YOU ?

1337
01:11:07,367 --> 01:11:09,001
OOH !

1338
01:11:09,101 --> 01:11:10,803
A GENTLEMAN !

1339
01:11:10,903 --> 01:11:12,404
HOW VERY UNUSUAL .

1340
01:11:12,504 --> 01:11:15,340
- GOOD AFTERNOON . - OH , DEAR ME ...

1341
01:11:15,440 --> 01:11:18,075
YES . GOOD AFTERNOON .

1342
01:11:18,243 --> 01:11:20,676
GOOD AFTERNOON .

1343
01:11:22,281 --> 01:11:25,348
ARE YOU BY ANY CHANCE WAITING TO SEE MISS HOLLOWAY ?

1344
01:11:25,450 --> 01:11:28,184
YES , WE HAVE AN APPOINTMENT .

1345
01:11:28,820 --> 01:11:30,655
WHAT LUCKY PEOPLE .

1346
01:11:30,755 --> 01:11:32,524
AND WHAT LUCK FOR ME , TOO ,

1347
01:11:32,624 --> 01:11:34,859
BECAUSE I 'M SURE YOU WON 'T MIND- -

1348
01:11:34,959 --> 01:11:38,127
- BUT PERHAPS YOU WILL . - IS THERE SOMETHING WE CAN DO ?

1349
01:11:38,329 --> 01:11:40,898
OH , IF YOU 'D BE SO VERY KIND .

1350
01:11:40,998 --> 01:11:42,033
YOU SEE ,

1351
01:11:42,133 --> 01:11:44,703
THIS ISN 'T MY DAY FOR AN INTERVIEW ,

1352
01:11:44,803 --> 01:11:47,569
AND I WANT HER TO HAVE THESE .

1353
01:11:48,806 --> 01:11:51,042
WHAT ARE THEY- - BIRD 'S EGGS ?

1354
01:11:51,142 --> 01:11:52,376
OOH !

1355
01:11:52,476 --> 01:11:54,212
BUT THAT 'S VERY FUNNY ,

1356
01:11:54,312 --> 01:11:57,079
BECAUSE YOU SEE , I 'M MISS BIRD .

1357
01:12:03,219 --> 01:12:05,921
THEY 'RE JUST LITTLE STONES ,

1358
01:12:06,022 --> 01:12:08,391
BECAUSE SHE LIKES SIMPLE THINGS ,

1359
01:12:08,491 --> 01:12:11,192
AND SHE HAS SO MANY FLOWERS .

1360
01:12:11,494 --> 01:12:14,362
THERE ISN 'T MUCH ELSE ONE CAN FIND .

1361
01:12:14,697 --> 01:12:17,100
WELL , I 'LL GIVE THEM TO HER .

1362
01:12:17,200 --> 01:12:18,701
THANK YOU .

1363
01:12:18,801 --> 01:12:20,136
AND NOW , I ...

1364
01:12:20,236 --> 01:12:23,204
THINK I 'LL JUST GO OUT FOR A LITTLE WALK .

1365
01:12:26,242 --> 01:12:29,143
GO BACK TO YOUR WORK AT ONCE , MISS BIRD !

1366
01:12:33,516 --> 01:12:35,618
DON 'T FORGET !

1367
01:12:35,718 --> 01:12:38,752
Woman : WILL YOU COME THIS WAY , PLEASE ?

1368
01:12:40,322 --> 01:12:43,256
- SHALL I TAKE THEM ? - NO , I 'LL DELIVER THEM .

1369
01:12:43,659 --> 01:12:46,026
AS YOU WISH .

1370
01:12:49,365 --> 01:12:52,299
- ( knocking ) - Miss Holloway : COME IN .

1371
01:12:55,837 --> 01:12:57,906
- HOW DO YOU DO ? - HOW DO YOU DO ?

1372
01:12:58,006 --> 01:12:59,107
THIS IS SO KIND OF YOU .

1373
01:12:59,207 --> 01:13:02,277
I WAS ASKED TO GIVE YOU THESE BY A MISS BIRD , I BELIEVE .

1374
01:13:02,377 --> 01:13:04,479
POOR MISS BIRD . OUR SADDEST CASE .

1375
01:13:04,579 --> 01:13:06,782
THEY 'RE REALLY VERY FINE STONES , AREN 'T THEY ?

1376
01:13:06,882 --> 01:13:08,750
I MUST REMEMBER TO THANK HER FOR THEM .

1377
01:13:08,850 --> 01:13:11,352
SHE COMES TO ME ONCE A WEEK FOR A LITTLE CHAT .

1378
01:13:11,452 --> 01:13:13,054
- WON 'T YOU SIT DOWN ? - THANK YOU .

1379
01:13:13,154 --> 01:13:16,788
MISS HOLLOWAY , FORGIVE OUR IGNORANCE , BUT WE KNOW SO VERY LITTLE OF YOUR WORK .

1380
01:13:17,192 --> 01:13:18,826
IS IT WITH MENTAL PATIENTS ?

1381
01:13:18,926 --> 01:13:21,927
NOT PATIENTS , MISS FITZGERALD , JUST GUESTS .

1382
01:13:22,163 --> 01:13:23,831
IN A WAY THIS IS LIKE A HOTEL- -

1383
01:13:23,931 --> 01:13:27,266
WHERE THERE ARE BEAUTIFUL THINGS TO LOOK AT , MUSIC TO HEAR ,

1384
01:13:27,502 --> 01:13:29,036
AND A LITTLE SYMPATHY .

1385
01:13:29,136 --> 01:13:31,904
BUT DON 'T LET 'S TALK ABOUT ME .

1386
01:13:32,406 --> 01:13:35,774
YOU TOLD ME ON THE TELEPHONE ABOUT DISTURBANCES AT WINDWARD .

1387
01:13:36,443 --> 01:13:37,812
HOW CAN I HELP YOU ?

1388
01:13:37,912 --> 01:13:39,647
WE THOUGHT , PERHAPS , YOU COULD TELL US

1389
01:13:39,747 --> 01:13:41,949
WHAT MARY AND CARMEL WERE REALLY LIKE .

1390
01:13:42,049 --> 01:13:45,050
THEY WERE EXTRAORDINARY WOMEN , BOTH OF THEM .

1391
01:13:45,953 --> 01:13:49,087
MARY MEREDITH WAS THE FINEST HUMAN BEING I EVEN KNEW .

1392
01:13:49,223 --> 01:13:51,724
- Rick : IS THAT SHE ? - YES .

1393
01:13:51,824 --> 01:13:54,859
- Pam : AND CARMEL ? - SHE WAS EXCEPTIONAL , TOO .

1394
01:13:55,429 --> 01:13:58,229
I NEVER SAW SUCH INTENSITY OF EVIL .

1395
01:13:58,532 --> 01:14:01,433
SHE WAS A SPANISH GYPSY- - CRAFTY , CRUEL !

1396
01:14:03,135 --> 01:14:04,470
I 'M SORRY .

1397
01:14:04,570 --> 01:14:06,172
WHY DID MRS. MEREDITH PUT UP WITH IT ?

1398
01:14:06,272 --> 01:14:09,308
SHE THOUGHT MEREDITH SHOULD BE THE ONE TO END THE WRETCHED AFFAIR .

1399
01:14:09,408 --> 01:14:11,577
- AND DID HE ? - OH , YES , IN TIME .

1400
01:14:11,677 --> 01:14:13,412
SHE AND MEREDITH TOOK THE GIRL TO PARIS ,

1401
01:14:13,512 --> 01:14:16,880
FOUND A POSITION FOR HER , LEFT HER WELL SUPPLIED WITH MONEY .

1402
01:14:17,083 --> 01:14:19,385
THEN THEY CAME BACK HERE WITH THEIR BABY .

1403
01:14:19,485 --> 01:14:21,553
FOR A TIME IT SEEMED AS IF

1404
01:14:21,653 --> 01:14:23,689
THERE WAS SOME POSSIBILITY OF HAPPINESS .

1405
01:14:23,789 --> 01:14:25,791
- AND THEN ? - CARMEL CAME BACK .

1406
01:14:25,891 --> 01:14:29,125
SHE STILL WANTED MARY 'S HUSBAND . YOU KNOW HOW IT ENDED .

1407
01:14:31,296 --> 01:14:34,600
A NEIGHBOR OF OURS SPOKE OF SOMETHING WE CAN 'T QUITE UNDERSTAND .

1408
01:14:34,700 --> 01:14:37,768
HE MENTIONS A CHILD CRYING ON THE CLIFF THAT NIGHT .

1409
01:14:38,003 --> 01:14:39,838
A TERRIFIED CHILD .

1410
01:14:39,938 --> 01:14:41,039
OH .

1411
01:14:41,139 --> 01:14:43,940
THAT 'S A PART OF THE STORY SO ...

1412
01:14:44,042 --> 01:14:46,909
UGLY I 'VE NEVER MENTIONED IT BEFORE .

1413
01:14:48,146 --> 01:14:50,182
WE 'RE SORRY TO DISTRESS YOU .

1414
01:14:50,282 --> 01:14:52,484
THAT NIGHT , THE GIRL CARMEL

1415
01:14:52,584 --> 01:14:54,251
HAD BEEN TOLD SHE MUST LEAVE WINDWARD .

1416
01:14:54,351 --> 01:14:57,287
IF SHE COULD HAVE KILLED BOTH MARY AND HER HUSBAND SHE WOULD HAVE DONE SO .

1417
01:14:57,387 --> 01:15:00,523
A BETTER PLAN FLASHED INTO HER WICKED LITTLE BRAIN .

1418
01:15:01,025 --> 01:15:02,393
SHE WENT INTO THE NURSERY ,

1419
01:15:02,493 --> 01:15:04,528
PICKED UP THEIR BABY , AND RACED TO THE CLIFF .

1420
01:15:04,628 --> 01:15:07,597
- Pam : GOOD HEAVENS ! - MARY WAS AFTER IT IN A SECOND ,

1421
01:15:07,697 --> 01:15:09,400
MEREDITH AND I CLOSE BEHIND .

1422
01:15:09,500 --> 01:15:11,969
CARMEL REACHED THE CLIFF BY THE DEAD TREE .

1423
01:15:12,069 --> 01:15:14,871
FOR A MOMENT , I SAW THEM STRUGGLING ,

1424
01:15:14,971 --> 01:15:18,106
THEN CARMEL RAISED HER ARM ... AND STRUCK MARY DOWN .

1425
01:15:20,344 --> 01:15:21,412
THEN IT WAS MURDER ?

1426
01:15:21,512 --> 01:15:24,280
THE WILL TO KILL HAD ALWAYS BEEN THERE , I THINK .

1427
01:15:24,380 --> 01:15:26,049
DIRECTED AGAINST STELLA .

1428
01:15:26,149 --> 01:15:27,484
CAN THAT BE WHAT SURVIVES ?

1429
01:15:27,584 --> 01:15:30,754
MAYBE THAT ACCOUNTS FOR STELLA 'S QUEER BUSINESS ON THE CLIFF .

1430
01:15:30,854 --> 01:15:31,588
WHAT WAS THAT ?

1431
01:15:31,688 --> 01:15:34,090
SOMETHING IN THAT HOUSE DROVE HER OUT TOWARD THE EDGE ,

1432
01:15:34,190 --> 01:15:37,227
AND IF I HADN 'T CAUGHT HER , SHE 'D HAVE GONE OVER .

1433
01:15:37,327 --> 01:15:39,760
WOULD SHE INDEED ?

1434
01:15:39,862 --> 01:15:42,296
HOW VERY CURIOUS .

1435
01:15:43,232 --> 01:15:45,966
PLEASE FINISH YOUR STORY .

1436
01:15:46,536 --> 01:15:47,970
IT WAS FINISHED .

1437
01:15:48,070 --> 01:15:49,872
EVERYTHING WAS FINISHED .

1438
01:15:49,972 --> 01:15:52,706
MEREDITH WENT DOWN THE CLIFF .

1439
01:15:54,009 --> 01:15:56,844
MARY WAS DEAD WHEN HE REACHED HER .

1440
01:15:56,945 --> 01:15:58,714
Rick : AND CARMEL ?

1441
01:15:58,814 --> 01:16:00,182
SHE RAN OUT INTO THE STORM .

1442
01:16:00,282 --> 01:16:03,750
NEXT MORNING SHE CRAWLED BACK IN THE EARLY STAGES OF PNEUMONIA .

1443
01:16:05,120 --> 01:16:07,756
I FOUGHT FOR CARMEL 'S LIFE , DAY AND NIGHT ,

1444
01:16:07,856 --> 01:16:10,523
HATING HER ALL THE TIME !

1445
01:16:11,426 --> 01:16:13,428
Pam : HOW AWFUL FOR YOU .

1446
01:16:13,528 --> 01:16:16,429
I 'M SORRY , I DISCIPLINE OTHERS ...

1447
01:16:18,199 --> 01:16:20,900
I CAN 'T DISCIPLINE MYSELF .

1448
01:16:22,436 --> 01:16:23,204
THERE .

1449
01:16:23,304 --> 01:16:25,907
HAVE I TOLD YOU EVERYTHING YOU WANT TO KNOW ?

1450
01:16:26,007 --> 01:16:27,776
ALL EXCEPT ONE THING .

1451
01:16:27,876 --> 01:16:30,810
THAT LAST NIGHT , WHO TOLD CARMEL SHE MUST GO ?

1452
01:16:31,745 --> 01:16:32,981
WHY , MARY- -

1453
01:16:33,081 --> 01:16:34,315
I SHOULD SAY MEREDITH .

1454
01:16:34,415 --> 01:16:37,516
IT 'S THE ONE DECENT THING I EVER KNEW HIM TO DO .

1455
01:16:38,619 --> 01:16:41,286
THIS IS ALL EXTREMELY- -

1456
01:16:42,623 --> 01:16:44,956
I 'M SORRY .

1457
01:16:45,426 --> 01:16:46,660
MAY I OFFER YOU TEA ?

1458
01:16:46,760 --> 01:16:50,061
THANK YOU , BUT WE MUST GET BACK BEFORE OUR MAID LEAVES .

1459
01:16:50,564 --> 01:16:52,198
SHE WON 'T STAY AT WINDWARD AFTER DARK .

1460
01:16:52,298 --> 01:16:55,168
I 'M AFRAID I HAVEN 'T BEEN MUCH HELP WITH YOUR PROBLEM .

1461
01:16:55,268 --> 01:16:57,969
THANK YOU ANYWAY , AND GOODBYE .

1462
01:16:58,105 --> 01:17:00,705
- GOODBYE . - GOODBYE .

1463
01:17:24,463 --> 01:17:27,164
GOOD AFTERNOON , MY DEAR .

1464
01:17:28,100 --> 01:17:29,635
DO YOU WANT TO SEE ME ?

1465
01:17:29,735 --> 01:17:31,537
I 'VE BEEN ASKING FOR YOU ALL DAY .

1466
01:17:31,637 --> 01:17:34,239
I 'M BEING TREATED AS THOUGH I WERE INSANE .

1467
01:17:34,339 --> 01:17:36,008
HAS ANYONE USED THAT WORD ?

1468
01:17:36,108 --> 01:17:37,809
I 'VE TOLD THEM A THOUSAND TIMES- -

1469
01:17:37,909 --> 01:17:39,345
IT ISN 'T A QUESTION OF A WORD .

1470
01:17:39,445 --> 01:17:42,681
MY DOOR 'S KEPT LOCKED AND THERE 'S A QUEER LOOK IN THEIR EYES .

1471
01:17:42,781 --> 01:17:45,415
OH . YOU FEEL PERSECUTED .

1472
01:17:46,084 --> 01:17:47,185
NO .

1473
01:17:47,285 --> 01:17:49,521
ABOUT THE CLIFF AT WINDWARD , STELLA- -

1474
01:17:49,621 --> 01:17:52,521
WHAT DID YOU FEEL AS YOU RAN TOWARD IT ?

1475
01:17:54,358 --> 01:17:56,427
I DIDN 'T FEEL ANYTHING .

1476
01:17:56,527 --> 01:17:58,496
I WAS SAD IN THE HOUSE- -

1477
01:17:58,596 --> 01:18:01,099
WAS IT AS THOUGH SOME WILL WERE DIRECTING YOU ,

1478
01:18:01,199 --> 01:18:03,267
A WILL STRONGER THAN YOURS ?

1479
01:18:03,367 --> 01:18:06,237
THE SEA SOUNDED LOUD AND BEAUTIFUL .

1480
01:18:06,337 --> 01:18:08,706
I JUST WENT IN THAT DIRECTION .

1481
01:18:08,806 --> 01:18:10,341
IN FACT , YOU DON 'T QUITE KNOW .

1482
01:18:10,441 --> 01:18:13,010
I WANT TO SEE MY GRANDFATHER , MISS HOLLOWAY .

1483
01:18:13,110 --> 01:18:14,111
YOU WILL , IN TIME .

1484
01:18:14,211 --> 01:18:17,212
DOES GRANDFATHER KNOW WHAT THIS PLACE IS LIKE ?

1485
01:18:19,016 --> 01:18:20,551
THAT WOMAN WHO LAUGHS .

1486
01:18:20,651 --> 01:18:22,620
I HEAR LAUGHING ALL NIGHT !

1487
01:18:22,720 --> 01:18:24,088
AND THAT OTHER WOMAN THAT- -

1488
01:18:24,188 --> 01:18:26,790
YOUR GRANDFATHER 'S SORRY THAT YOU HAVE TO BE HERE ,

1489
01:18:26,890 --> 01:18:29,259
BUT HE KNOWS YOU 'LL BE BETTER SOON .

1490
01:18:29,359 --> 01:18:30,727
BETTER ?

1491
01:18:30,827 --> 01:18:32,529
BUT I 'M PERFECTLY ALL RIGHT !

1492
01:18:32,629 --> 01:18:34,497
I WOULDN 'T SAY THAT , STELLA , DEAR .

1493
01:18:34,597 --> 01:18:37,499
AND PLEASE DON 'T KEEP ASKING TO SEE ME .

1494
01:18:37,834 --> 01:18:40,702
WHY DO YOU HATE ME , MISS HOLLOWAY ?

1495
01:18:41,170 --> 01:18:42,739
YOU SEE- -

1496
01:18:42,839 --> 01:18:45,573
YOU DO FEEL PERSECUTED .

1497
01:18:57,286 --> 01:18:59,255
RICK , IF I SHOULD EVER HAPPEN TO LOSE MY MIND- -

1498
01:18:59,355 --> 01:19:02,523
I DON 'T THINK YOU 'LL LOSE IT . IT MIGHT RATTLE TO ONE SIDE .

1499
01:19:02,691 --> 01:19:05,692
BUT IF I DO , NO MARY MEREDITH RETREAT FOR ME .

1500
01:19:05,894 --> 01:19:08,431
PLAIN , OLD-FASHIONED LUNATIC ASYLUM ,

1501
01:19:08,531 --> 01:19:09,765
NOT THAT CREEPY HORROR !

1502
01:19:09,865 --> 01:19:12,501
YOU 'LL HAVE A LOVELY TALK WITH MISS HOLLOWAY ONCE A WEEK .

1503
01:19:12,601 --> 01:19:14,870
- BRRR . - YOU THINK SHE WAS LYING TO US ?

1504
01:19:14,970 --> 01:19:16,471
ABOUT THE PAST ? WHY SHOULD SHE ?

1505
01:19:16,571 --> 01:19:20,206
SHE WASN 'T GOING TO TELL US ABOUT THE BABY . AND LATER , SHE MADE THAT ONE BREAK .

1506
01:19:20,342 --> 01:19:22,610
ADMITTING IT WAS MARY WHO TOLD CARMEL TO GO .

1507
01:19:22,710 --> 01:19:25,480
WHY TRY TO HIDE IT ? IT WAS A NORMAL HUMAN REACTION .

1508
01:19:25,580 --> 01:19:28,450
MADE ME LIKE MARY BETTER , AS A MATTER OF FACT .

1509
01:19:28,550 --> 01:19:30,452
I WAS GETTING AWFULLY BORED WITH HER PERFECTION .

1510
01:19:30,552 --> 01:19:33,986
WHY WOULD MISS HOLLOWAY WANT TO TURN HER INTO A PLASTER SAINT ?

1511
01:19:34,856 --> 01:19:36,924
MAYBE SHE LIKES PLASTER SAINTS .

1512
01:19:37,024 --> 01:19:39,026
SHE 'S ONE HERSELF .

1513
01:19:39,126 --> 01:19:40,194
THANK YOU , DOCTOR .

1514
01:19:40,294 --> 01:19:42,630
I ASSURE YOU THAT WHEN THAT HEALTHY YOUNG MAN LAUGHS ,

1515
01:19:42,730 --> 01:19:45,798
- HE ISN 'T BEING DELIRIOUS . - GOODBYE , DOCTOR .

1516
01:19:46,734 --> 01:19:48,636
OH , HELLO ! COME IN .

1517
01:19:48,736 --> 01:19:50,204
HELLO .

1518
01:19:50,304 --> 01:19:53,671
- WHAT NEWS WI TH STELLA ? - NONE , AND I WON 'T BE HAVING ANY .

1519
01:19:54,241 --> 01:19:56,010
HER GRANDFATHER 'S KICKED ME OUT .

1520
01:19:56,110 --> 01:19:57,511
WHERE HAVE YOU BEEN ALL DAY ?

1521
01:19:57,611 --> 01:19:59,213
TO THE MIDDLE OF BODMIN MOOR AND BACK .

1522
01:19:59,313 --> 01:20:01,482
- SEEING A MISS HOLLOWAY . - WHAT ? HOLY HOLLOWAY

1523
01:20:01,582 --> 01:20:02,983
OF " WEALTH THROUGH HARMONY " ?

1524
01:20:03,083 --> 01:20:04,818
- WHAT DO YOU KNOW ABOUT HER ? - NOTHING REALLY ,

1525
01:20:04,918 --> 01:20:06,653
EXCEPT THAT DR. RUDD , MY PREDECESSOR ,

1526
01:20:06,753 --> 01:20:08,689
HAD SOME SORT OF PREJUDICE AGAINST HER .

1527
01:20:08,789 --> 01:20:10,356
SHE SAYS CARMEL KILLED MARY MEREDITH .

1528
01:20:10,456 --> 01:20:12,659
YES , SHE WAS THERE . NURSED CARMEL AFTERWARDS .

1529
01:20:12,759 --> 01:20:14,761
COULD WE TALK TO DR. RUDD ABOUT HER ?

1530
01:20:14,861 --> 01:20:17,163
ONLY IF WE HAVE ANOTHER SEANCE .

1531
01:20:17,263 --> 01:20:19,032
- I WONDER- - - WHAT ?

1532
01:20:19,132 --> 01:20:21,067
IT 'S ONLY THE VERY FAINTEST CHANCE ,

1533
01:20:21,167 --> 01:20:24,001
OF COURSE , BUT COME ON UPSTAIRS .

1534
01:20:26,772 --> 01:20:29,008
1908 TO ' 11 , '12 TO ' 15 ,

1535
01:20:29,108 --> 01:20:31,244
'16 TO ' 19 . HERE WE ARE .

1536
01:20:31,344 --> 01:20:32,678
IT HAPPENED IN THE WINTER .

1537
01:20:32,778 --> 01:20:35,047
Scott : YES , LET 'S START WITH NOVEMBER .

1538
01:20:35,147 --> 01:20:36,516
Pam : FROM HIS HANDWRITING ,

1539
01:20:36,616 --> 01:20:38,684
DR. RUDD MUST HAVE BEEN 200 YEARS OLD .

1540
01:20:38,784 --> 01:20:40,720
MEASLES , MEASLES , MEASLES ,

1541
01:20:40,820 --> 01:20:42,988
WHOOPING COUGH , MEASLES , APPENDICITIS .

1542
01:20:43,088 --> 01:20:45,725
PLEASANT CHANGE FOR THE OLD BOY .

1543
01:20:45,825 --> 01:20:47,026
HERE WE ARE .

1544
01:20:47,126 --> 01:20:48,260
CALLED TO WINDWARD HOUSE .

1545
01:20:48,360 --> 01:20:51,428
MEREDITH 'S MODEL , CARMEL QUESADA , DOUBLE PNEUMONIA .

1546
01:20:51,997 --> 01:20:53,532
QUESADA GIRL MUCH WORSE .

1547
01:20:53,632 --> 01:20:55,300
NO ATTEMPT TO WARM THE BEDROOM .

1548
01:20:55,400 --> 01:20:57,102
FOUND TRACES OF SNOW ON THE FLOOR .

1549
01:20:57,202 --> 01:20:59,404
SNOW ? THEN THE WINDOW WAS LEFT OPEN .

1550
01:20:59,504 --> 01:21:01,039
SPOKE SEVERELY TO NURSE .

1551
01:21:01,139 --> 01:21:03,408
RETURNED TO WINDWARD THIS EVENING .

1552
01:21:03,508 --> 01:21:04,609
PATIENT DEAD .

1553
01:21:04,709 --> 01:21:06,110
NURSE HOLLOWAY THREATENED ME

1554
01:21:06,210 --> 01:21:08,713
WITH LEGAL ACTION WHEN I USED THE WORDS ,

1555
01:21:08,813 --> 01:21:09,881
" CRIMINAL NEGLIGENCE . "

1556
01:21:09,981 --> 01:21:12,550
- BUT THAT MEANS- - - TO A DOCTOR OF RUDD 'S GENERATION ,

1557
01:21:12,650 --> 01:21:14,185
IT WAS VERY APT TO MEAN MURDER .

1558
01:21:14,285 --> 01:21:15,720
MISS HOLLOWAY MURDERED CARMEL ?

1559
01:21:15,820 --> 01:21:18,556
- Servant : DOCTOR . - IN A QUIET , LADYLIKE WAY .

1560
01:21:18,656 --> 01:21:20,391
- DOCTOR ! - YES , EDITH ?

1561
01:21:20,491 --> 01:21:22,693
THE COMMANDER 'S MAID 'S ON THE PHONE .

1562
01:21:22,793 --> 01:21:23,794
YOU 'RE TO COME AT ONCE .

1563
01:21:23,894 --> 01:21:26,797
- IS IT MISS MEREDITH ? - IT 'S THE COMMANDER .

1564
01:21:26,897 --> 01:21:28,732
TOOK AWFUL BAD , THE MAID SAYS .

1565
01:21:28,832 --> 01:21:30,501
ALL RIGHT , EDITH . YOU TAKE THIS HOME .

1566
01:21:30,601 --> 01:21:33,869
THERE MAY BE SOME OTHER DETAILS . I 'LL BE ALONG LATER .

1567
01:21:36,306 --> 01:21:38,874
HE 'S IN HERE , DOCTOR .

1568
01:21:40,510 --> 01:21:43,544
I UNDID HIS SHOES . IT WAS ALL I KNEW HOW TO DO .

1569
01:21:44,882 --> 01:21:47,883
- BAD ONE THIS TIME , SCOTT . - YES , I KNOW .

1570
01:21:48,518 --> 01:21:51,219
HOLD THAT UNDER HIS NOSE .

1571
01:21:54,524 --> 01:21:56,891
( coughs )

1572
01:21:59,161 --> 01:22:01,729
WANT AN APOLOGY , SCOTT ?

1573
01:22:02,331 --> 01:22:03,566
YOU 'D GET IT ,

1574
01:22:03,666 --> 01:22:05,935
- IF YOU STUCK OUT FOR IT . - NO , THANKS .

1575
01:22:06,035 --> 01:22:08,836
I 'LL HAVE YOU RIGHT IN A JIFFY .

1576
01:22:12,541 --> 01:22:13,409
WHO 'S THERE ? !

1577
01:22:13,509 --> 01:22:16,576
Rick : NOW WHO DO YOU SUPPOSE IS THERE ?

1578
01:22:21,049 --> 01:22:21,983
HELLO , LIZZIE .

1579
01:22:22,083 --> 01:22:24,353
I 'M SITTING IN YOUR MOTHER 'S CHAIR ,

1580
01:22:24,453 --> 01:22:25,754
AND IF ANY GHOST COMES ALONG ,

1581
01:22:25,854 --> 01:22:28,757
I 'LL LET OUT A SCREAM THAT WOULD FRIGHTEN THE LIFE OUT OF IT .

1582
01:22:28,857 --> 01:22:29,591
WHAT 'S HAPPENED ?

1583
01:22:29,691 --> 01:22:32,859
I FEEL THE WICKEDNESS OF THIS HOUSE GATHERING AROUND .

1584
01:22:33,562 --> 01:22:35,296
COME ON , NOW . HOP OFF TO THE JESSUPS .

1585
01:22:35,396 --> 01:22:38,032
I 'M NOT GOING . I 'LL BE FOUND DEAD IN ME BED IN THE MORNING ,

1586
01:22:38,132 --> 01:22:41,200
STIFF WITH FRIGHT , AND ME DEATH WILL BE ON YOU .

1587
01:22:41,469 --> 01:22:43,471
- ME ? ! - HOW DO I KNOW WHAT DEVILMENT

1588
01:22:43,571 --> 01:22:45,506
YOU 'LL BE UP TO WHEN ME BACK IS TURNED ?

1589
01:22:45,606 --> 01:22:47,541
I PROMISE YOU WE 'LL DO NOTHING TONIGHT

1590
01:22:47,641 --> 01:22:49,277
THAT THE PRIEST WOULDN 'T APPROVE OF .

1591
01:22:49,377 --> 01:22:51,346
LORD BLESS YOU , MR. RICK .

1592
01:22:51,446 --> 01:22:52,980
I WAS HOPING YOU 'D SAY THAT .

1593
01:22:53,080 --> 01:22:55,881
I 'LL GO AND GET ME HAT AND COAT .

1594
01:22:59,086 --> 01:23:00,220
FIND ANYTHING NEW ?

1595
01:23:00,320 --> 01:23:01,722
NOTHING AFTER THAT ENTRY .

1596
01:23:01,822 --> 01:23:03,223
HOW ABOUT A WHISKEY AND SODA ?

1597
01:23:03,323 --> 01:23:06,091
LESS SODA THAN USUAL , THANKS .

1598
01:23:09,296 --> 01:23:11,465
Pam : AWFUL IF WE TOOK TO DRINK , BOTH OF US .

1599
01:23:11,565 --> 01:23:14,834
Rick : WELL , IT 'S AN IDEAL HOUSE FOR DELIRIUM TREMENS .

1600
01:23:14,934 --> 01:23:16,836
BEFORE YOU TAKE A SIP ,

1601
01:23:16,936 --> 01:23:19,604
DON 'T YOU SMELL MIMOSA ?

1602
01:23:20,139 --> 01:23:21,574
YES .

1603
01:23:21,674 --> 01:23:23,142
ARE YOU SCARED ?

1604
01:23:23,242 --> 01:23:25,144
I WISH I 'D WAKE UP .

1605
01:23:25,244 --> 01:23:28,079
IT CAME FROM THE NURSERY LAST NIGHT .

1606
01:23:36,055 --> 01:23:38,758
YOU HAVE THE GREAT NOSE OF THE FAMILY .

1607
01:23:38,858 --> 01:23:41,525
NOT A TRACE OF IT NOW .

1608
01:23:49,435 --> 01:23:52,536
- IT 'S STRONGEST HERE . - IT 'S ALMOST OVERPOWERING .

1609
01:23:53,171 --> 01:23:56,272
I WISH YOU 'D TELL US WHAT YOU WANT , MARY MEREDITH !

1610
01:23:56,609 --> 01:23:58,711
- Lizzie : MR. RICK ? - YES ?

1611
01:23:58,811 --> 01:23:59,878
I FORGOT TO ASK .

1612
01:23:59,978 --> 01:24:01,880
DID YOU FIND OUT ANYTHING TODAY ?

1613
01:24:01,980 --> 01:24:03,949
JUST TURNED UP A COUPLE OF MURDERS .

1614
01:24:04,049 --> 01:24:05,784
HOLY SAINTS PRESERVE US .

1615
01:24:05,884 --> 01:24:08,720
- ( doorbell rings ) - ANSWER THE DOOR .

1616
01:24:08,820 --> 01:24:11,420
IT 'S PROBABLY DR. SCOTT .

1617
01:24:12,324 --> 01:24:14,759
- GOOD EVENING , DR. SCOTT . - EVENING , LIZZIE .

1618
01:24:14,859 --> 01:24:17,229
- IN HERE . - GOOD NIGHT , MISS PAM .

1619
01:24:17,329 --> 01:24:18,730
- GOOD NIGHT . - GOOD NIGHT .

1620
01:24:18,830 --> 01:24:20,932
- I 'M GLAD TO FIND YOU HERE . - HOW 'S THE COMMANDER ?

1621
01:24:21,032 --> 01:24:23,100
IT 'S NOT HIM I 'M WORRIED ABOUT . IT 'S STELLA .

1622
01:24:23,200 --> 01:24:25,135
- WHAT 'S THE MATTER WITH HER ? - SHE 'S AT MISS HOLLOWAY 'S .

1623
01:24:25,235 --> 01:24:28,138
- NO ! - WE CAN 'T LET HER STAY THERE . WE 'VE GOT TO GET HER TONIGHT .

1624
01:24:28,238 --> 01:24:31,141
THAT 'S THE WAY I FEEL , BUT DON 'T LET 'S GET HYSTERICAL .

1625
01:24:31,241 --> 01:24:33,277
MISS HOLLOWAY WAS HER MOTHER 'S BEST FRIEND .

1626
01:24:33,377 --> 01:24:36,380
THE IDEA OF HER SPENDING AN HOUR IN THAT PLACE IS HORRIBLE .

1627
01:24:36,480 --> 01:24:38,115
CAN YOU GET THE OLD BOY 'S PERMISSION ?

1628
01:24:38,215 --> 01:24:39,750
HE 'S FAR TOO ILL . WE 'VE NO AUTHORITY WHATEVER .

1629
01:24:39,850 --> 01:24:42,253
- THEN WE 'LL DO IT WITHOUT . - SHALL WE TAKE THE CASEBOOK ?

1630
01:24:42,353 --> 01:24:44,555
WE MIGHT BE ABLE TO FRIGHTEN HER WITH IT .

1631
01:24:44,655 --> 01:24:45,456
YES . NO , WAIT- -

1632
01:24:45,556 --> 01:24:48,259
WE 'LL DESCRIBE WHAT WE FOUND AND THEN PILE IT ON A BIT , HUH ?

1633
01:24:48,359 --> 01:24:50,992
LET 'S GO TO A TELEPHONE .

1634
01:24:58,267 --> 01:25:00,203
YES ?

1635
01:25:00,303 --> 01:25:01,738
YES .

1636
01:25:01,838 --> 01:25:04,307
IT 'S NO BOTHER AT ALL , MISS FITZGERALD .

1637
01:25:04,407 --> 01:25:06,309
I 'LL BE GLAD TO SEE YOU AGAIN .

1638
01:25:06,409 --> 01:25:08,711
ARE YOU MOTORING ?

1639
01:25:08,811 --> 01:25:11,212
IN TWO HOURS .

1640
01:25:11,414 --> 01:25:13,714
GOODBYE .

1641
01:25:19,287 --> 01:25:21,889
BRING IN MISS MEREDITH .

1642
01:25:24,727 --> 01:25:27,560
I MAY NEED THE CAR THIS EVENING .

1643
01:25:44,646 --> 01:25:46,881
GOOD EVENING , MY DEAR .

1644
01:25:46,981 --> 01:25:49,348
COME IN .

1645
01:25:51,853 --> 01:25:54,186
SIT DOWN .

1646
01:25:54,488 --> 01:25:57,158
I THOUGHT YOU 'D FEEL MORE AT HOME HERE .

1647
01:25:57,258 --> 01:25:58,693
I DO , MISS HOLLOWAY .

1648
01:25:58,793 --> 01:26:00,161
I 'VE BEEN GIVING YOUR PROBLEM

1649
01:26:00,261 --> 01:26:01,863
THE MOST SERIOUS CONSIDERATION .

1650
01:26:01,963 --> 01:26:04,032
IT 'S NOT MUCH OF A PROBLEM .

1651
01:26:04,132 --> 01:26:05,666
I JUST WANT TO GO HOME .

1652
01:26:05,766 --> 01:26:07,901
TO YOUR GRANDFATHER 'S ?

1653
01:26:08,001 --> 01:26:09,703
I COULDN 'T PERMIT THAT .

1654
01:26:09,803 --> 01:26:11,672
YOU 'VE NEVER BEEN VERY HAPPY THERE .

1655
01:26:11,772 --> 01:26:14,606
WHERE WOULD YOU REALLY LIKE TO BE ?

1656
01:26:15,108 --> 01:26:16,977
YOU MEAN WINDWARD ?

1657
01:26:17,077 --> 01:26:19,179
THAT 'S THE BASIS OF ALL YOUR TROUBLE ,

1658
01:26:19,279 --> 01:26:22,013
BEING KEPT AWAY FROM THERE .

1659
01:26:23,650 --> 01:26:25,952
DO YOU THINK SHE WANTS YOU THERE ?

1660
01:26:26,052 --> 01:26:28,552
YES , I THINK SHE DOES .

1661
01:26:29,522 --> 01:26:32,257
AND WHAT SHE WANTS , I WANT .

1662
01:26:33,693 --> 01:26:35,528
I 'VE TALKED WITH THE FITZGERALDS .

1663
01:26:35,628 --> 01:26:36,962
THEY 'RE VERY FOND OF YOU .

1664
01:26:37,062 --> 01:26:38,698
THEY 'LL LET ME STAY THERE WITH THEM ?

1665
01:26:38,798 --> 01:26:40,433
FOR THE PRESENT , YOUR GRANDFATHER 'S

1666
01:26:40,533 --> 01:26:42,569
NOT TO KNOW THAT YOU 'VE LEFT HERE .

1667
01:26:42,669 --> 01:26:44,269
IT WOULD WORRY HIM .

1668
01:26:44,369 --> 01:26:47,171
YOU MUST GO STRAIGHT TO WINDWARD .

1669
01:26:48,941 --> 01:26:50,677
IS THAT CLEAR ?

1670
01:26:50,777 --> 01:26:51,744
MISS HOLLOWAY ,

1671
01:26:51,844 --> 01:26:54,712
I 'M THE HAPPIEST PERSON IN THE WORLD .

1672
01:26:56,048 --> 01:26:58,849
THERE 'S A TRAIN IN 40 MINUTES .

1673
01:26:59,018 --> 01:27:01,918
MY CAR WILL TAKE YOU TO THE STATION .

1674
01:27:14,566 --> 01:27:17,366
GOOD EVENING . WON 'T YOU COME IN ?

1675
01:27:18,970 --> 01:27:20,371
OH , BUT I MUST ANNOUNCE YOU !

1676
01:27:20,471 --> 01:27:23,372
DON 'T BOTHER . WE 'LL ANNOUNCE OURSELVES .

1677
01:27:28,546 --> 01:27:29,247
GOOD EVENING .

1678
01:27:29,347 --> 01:27:31,149
SO YOU 'VE THOUGHT OF SOME MORE QUESTIONS ?

1679
01:27:31,249 --> 01:27:32,917
WHY DIDN 'T YOU TELL US STELLA WAS HERE ?

1680
01:27:33,017 --> 01:27:34,919
THE PRESENCE OF MY GUESTS IS CONFIDENTIAL .

1681
01:27:35,019 --> 01:27:37,722
- WE 'VE COME TO TAKE HER . - THIS IS STELLA 'S DOCTOR .

1682
01:27:37,822 --> 01:27:39,890
OH , I BEGIN TO UNDERSTAND .

1683
01:27:39,990 --> 01:27:41,058
THIS IS A RESCUE PARTY .

1684
01:27:41,158 --> 01:27:43,260
I MUST ASK YOU TO TAKE ME TO STELLA AT ONCE .

1685
01:27:43,360 --> 01:27:45,162
THERE WAS A TIME WHEN I WOULD HAVE RESENTED

1686
01:27:45,262 --> 01:27:47,397
SUCH IMPERTINENCE , PARTICULARLY FROM A DOCTOR

1687
01:27:47,497 --> 01:27:49,532
WHOSE CONDUCT LEAVES SO MUCH TO BE DESIRED .

1688
01:27:49,632 --> 01:27:51,301
PLEASE STOP BEATING ABOUT THE BUSH .

1689
01:27:51,401 --> 01:27:53,237
I COULDN 'T BE ANGRY WITH ANYONE TONIGHT .

1690
01:27:53,337 --> 01:27:56,373
YOU KNOW THOSE MOMENTS WHEN THE LIGHT IS VERY CLEAR ,

1691
01:27:56,473 --> 01:27:58,976
WHEN THE SCALES AT LAST SWING

1692
01:27:59,076 --> 01:28:00,343
INTO PERFECT BALANCE .

1693
01:28:00,443 --> 01:28:03,444
- WHERE IS STELLA ? ! - TELL THEM , MISS ELLIS .

1694
01:28:03,847 --> 01:28:06,848
SHE 'S ON THE TRAIN FOR BIDDLECOMBE . THE 9 : 20 .

1695
01:28:07,083 --> 01:28:08,985
ON HER WAY HOME .

1696
01:28:09,085 --> 01:28:12,121
- IS THAT TRUE ? - SHE 'LL BE THERE LONG BEFORE YOU .

1697
01:28:12,221 --> 01:28:14,323
- WHAT HAPPENED ? - NOTHING HAPPENED .

1698
01:28:14,423 --> 01:28:15,692
SHE WASN 'T VERY HAPPY HERE .

1699
01:28:15,792 --> 01:28:18,427
I CAN 'T BE OF ANY HELP TO PEOPLE WHO ARE UNHAPPY .

1700
01:28:18,527 --> 01:28:19,963
SHE WENT TO HER GRANDFATHER 'S ?

1701
01:28:20,063 --> 01:28:22,265
- NO . - NOT TO WINDWARD HOUSE .

1702
01:28:22,365 --> 01:28:23,466
BETTER THAN THAT .

1703
01:28:23,566 --> 01:28:24,600
TO THE CLIFF ...

1704
01:28:24,700 --> 01:28:26,202
AND THE ROCKS BELOW THE CLIFF .

1705
01:28:26,302 --> 01:28:29,203
- YOU LET HER ? ! - THAT 'S WERE MARY WENT .

1706
01:28:29,705 --> 01:28:31,207
THAT 'S WHERE SHE DIED .

1707
01:28:31,307 --> 01:28:33,842
SHE 'S OUT OF HER MIND . COME ON !

1708
01:28:33,942 --> 01:28:35,311
STELLA HAS A 20-MINUTE START !

1709
01:28:35,411 --> 01:28:38,013
Holloway : SHE HAD SUCH A LONELY SOUND .

1710
01:28:38,113 --> 01:28:39,047
EVERY SEVENTH WAVE .

1711
01:28:39,147 --> 01:28:41,617
- YOU 'D BETTER LOOK AFTER HER . - MISS HOLLOWAY !

1712
01:28:41,717 --> 01:28:43,719
WHAT 'S THE MATTER , MISS HOLLOWAY ?

1713
01:28:43,819 --> 01:28:46,485
GET OUT OF THIS ROOM !

1714
01:28:48,189 --> 01:28:50,826
I 'VE DONE WHAT SHE WANTED AT LAST .

1715
01:28:50,926 --> 01:28:52,760
HAVEN 'T I , MARY ?

1716
01:28:52,860 --> 01:28:55,395
IT 'S ALL STRAIGHT NOW .

1717
01:28:56,197 --> 01:28:58,633
THERE ARE NO FRAYED EDGES .

1718
01:28:58,733 --> 01:29:00,468
NO LOOSE ENDS .

1719
01:29:00,568 --> 01:29:02,470
ALL STRAIGHT .

1720
01:29:02,570 --> 01:29:04,937
ALL SMOOTH .

1721
01:29:09,911 --> 01:29:12,013
THESE LOCAL TRAINS ARE VERY SLOW , YOU KNOW .

1722
01:29:12,113 --> 01:29:13,681
BUT THIS ONE HAD A HEAD START .

1723
01:29:13,781 --> 01:29:16,250
YOU NEEDN 'T WORRY . SHE CAN 'T GET INTO THE HOUSE .

1724
01:29:16,350 --> 01:29:18,719
YOU DID LOCK THE DOOR , DIDN 'T YOU , PAM ?

1725
01:29:18,819 --> 01:29:21,386
NO , I THOUGHT YOU DID .

1726
01:29:31,598 --> 01:29:33,667
- WILL YOU BE ALL RIGHT ? - OH , YES .

1727
01:29:33,767 --> 01:29:36,768
I 'LL BE ALL RIGHT , NOW . I 'LL BE WITH MY FRIENDS .

1728
01:29:45,345 --> 01:29:47,812
( bells jingle )

1729
01:30:09,768 --> 01:30:11,370
PAMELA !

1730
01:30:11,470 --> 01:30:13,737
RICK !

1731
01:30:17,376 --> 01:30:19,909
PAMELA , ARE YOU THERE ?

1732
01:30:22,647 --> 01:30:24,914
RICK !

1733
01:30:30,321 --> 01:30:32,855
WHERE ARE YOU , PLEASE ?

1734
01:30:47,005 --> 01:30:49,405
( groaning )

1735
01:30:50,874 --> 01:30:52,743
LIZZIE ?

1736
01:30:52,843 --> 01:30:55,211
IS THAT YOU ?

1737
01:31:07,657 --> 01:31:10,225
Commander : STELLA .

1738
01:31:14,264 --> 01:31:16,597
STELLA .

1739
01:31:22,539 --> 01:31:24,274
GRANDFATHER !

1740
01:31:24,374 --> 01:31:25,975
GRANDFATHER !

1741
01:31:26,075 --> 01:31:27,209
STELLA , MY CHILD .

1742
01:31:27,309 --> 01:31:27,644
WHAT 'S THE MATTER ?

1743
01:31:27,744 --> 01:31:30,244
WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE ?

1744
01:31:30,446 --> 01:31:32,548
SOMEONE TELEPHONED

1745
01:31:32,648 --> 01:31:33,650
FROM MISS HOLLOWAY 'S .

1746
01:31:33,750 --> 01:31:36,218
AND YOU WALKED ALL THAT WAY ?

1747
01:31:36,318 --> 01:31:38,354
WELL , I HAD TO GET HERE .

1748
01:31:38,454 --> 01:31:41,488
DON 'T TRY AND TALK , DARLING . I 'LL GET DR. SCOTT .

1749
01:31:41,924 --> 01:31:44,857
OH , DEAR THERE 'S NO TELEPHONE IN THIS HOUSE .

1750
01:31:45,294 --> 01:31:46,462
GO . GO !

1751
01:31:46,562 --> 01:31:48,297
YOU CAN 'T BE LEFT ALONE .

1752
01:31:48,397 --> 01:31:50,166
BUT THE DANGER IS FOR YOU .

1753
01:31:50,266 --> 01:31:52,701
PLEASE GET OUT OF THIS HOUSE , NOW .

1754
01:31:52,801 --> 01:31:54,303
NOW LIE BACK QUIETLY .

1755
01:31:54,403 --> 01:31:57,203
I 'M NOT AFRAID OF ANYTHING HERE .

1756
01:31:58,006 --> 01:31:59,340
THEN BE AFRAID !

1757
01:31:59,440 --> 01:32:01,877
BE AFRAID , FOR HEAVEN 'S SAKE .

1758
01:32:01,977 --> 01:32:04,179
WHEN YOU WERE A LITTLE CHILD ,

1759
01:32:04,279 --> 01:32:05,546
AFTER HER DEATH ,

1760
01:32:05,646 --> 01:32:08,680
THE EVILS OF THIS HOUSE REACHED OUT FOR YOU .

1761
01:32:09,417 --> 01:32:11,419
I TOOK YOU AWAY THEN .

1762
01:32:11,519 --> 01:32:14,022
IF I COULD ONLY TAKE YOU NOW .

1763
01:32:14,122 --> 01:32:16,855
IT 'S ALL RIGHT , WE 'RE TOGETHER .

1764
01:32:28,135 --> 01:32:30,536
STELLA ! GO !

1765
01:32:32,139 --> 01:32:34,506
GRANDFATHER !

1766
01:32:43,983 --> 01:32:46,684
I WON 'T BE AFRAID , MOTHER .

1767
01:32:49,122 --> 01:32:51,489
( screams )

1768
01:32:57,530 --> 01:32:59,864
STELLA !

1769
01:33:01,534 --> 01:33:03,868
STELLA !

1770
01:33:05,138 --> 01:33:07,571
STELLA , STOP !

1771
01:33:13,011 --> 01:33:15,479
HOLD ON , DARLING .

1772
01:33:17,683 --> 01:33:18,016
WE 'VE GOT YOU NOW .

1773
01:33:18,116 --> 01:33:20,384
HANG ON .

1774
01:33:27,059 --> 01:33:28,426
ARE YOU ALL RIGHT ?

1775
01:33:28,526 --> 01:33:29,595
- YES . - SURE ?

1776
01:33:29,695 --> 01:33:32,562
DR. SCOTT , GRANDFATHER 'S IN THE STUDIO .

1777
01:33:32,865 --> 01:33:33,932
HE 'S TERRIBLY ILL .

1778
01:33:34,032 --> 01:33:36,832
WE 'D BETTER GET TO HIM AT ONCE .

1779
01:33:45,176 --> 01:33:47,745
THERE 'S NOTHING I CAN DO , MY DEAR .

1780
01:33:47,845 --> 01:33:49,947
I KNEW .

1781
01:33:50,047 --> 01:33:53,015
SHE KILLED HIM JUST AS SHE TRIED TO KILL ME .

1782
01:33:53,685 --> 01:33:56,153
- MY OWN MOTHER ! - NO , STELLA .

1783
01:33:56,253 --> 01:33:57,922
BUT I TELL YOU I SAW MY MOTHER

1784
01:33:58,022 --> 01:33:59,423
JUST AS MY FATHER PAINTED HER .

1785
01:33:59,523 --> 01:34:02,326
- IT MUST HAVE BEEN CARMEL . - IT WASN 'T .

1786
01:34:02,426 --> 01:34:03,961
STEADY , STELLA .

1787
01:34:04,061 --> 01:34:06,030
UNLESS- -

1788
01:34:06,130 --> 01:34:08,665
UNLESS PERHAPS MISS HOLLOWAY WAS RIGHT .

1789
01:34:08,765 --> 01:34:11,333
PERHAPS IT 'S MY MIND .

1790
01:34:12,369 --> 01:34:15,136
- OH , RICK ! - NO , DARLING , NO .

1791
01:34:18,074 --> 01:34:20,444
THE MIMOSA SCENT , IT 'S FLOODING THE ROOM .

1792
01:34:20,544 --> 01:34:23,179
IT 'S ALL RIGHT , DARLING . NOTHING WILL HURT YOU .

1793
01:34:23,279 --> 01:34:24,347
BUT I 'M NOT FRIGHTENED .

1794
01:34:24,447 --> 01:34:27,514
THIS IS WHAT I FELT IN THE NURSERY THAT NIGHT .

1795
01:34:28,218 --> 01:34:30,053
THE BOOK !

1796
01:34:30,153 --> 01:34:31,354
WHAT 'S DOING IT ?

1797
01:34:31,454 --> 01:34:32,721
Dr. Scott : THE WIND .

1798
01:34:32,821 --> 01:34:34,824
Pam : BUT WHAT ABOUT THE MIMOSA ?

1799
01:34:34,924 --> 01:34:36,792
WE 'RE LETTING OUR IMAGINATIONS

1800
01:34:36,892 --> 01:34:38,794
PLAY HOB WITH OUR SENSES .

1801
01:34:38,894 --> 01:34:41,629
11 : 15 A.M. MARY ANN HARDY .

1802
01:34:42,131 --> 01:34:44,500
BROKEN ARM . SECOND THIS YEAR .

1803
01:34:44,600 --> 01:34:47,267
IT 'S IMAGINATION , ALL RIGHT .

1804
01:34:49,271 --> 01:34:51,173
WHAT DID I EXPECT ?

1805
01:34:51,273 --> 01:34:52,240
WAIT A MINUTE .

1806
01:34:52,340 --> 01:34:54,844
3 : 20 P.M. , CALLED TO WINDWARD HOUSE

1807
01:34:54,944 --> 01:34:56,912
TO ATTEND MEREDITH 'S MODEL WHO HAD FAINTED .

1808
01:34:57,012 --> 01:35:00,013
IT DIDN 'T TAKE MUCH SKILL TO FIND THE REASON .

1809
01:35:01,150 --> 01:35:02,551
GIRL IN POOR PHYSICAL CONDITION ,

1810
01:35:02,651 --> 01:35:05,885
BUT I 'M SURE HER GREAT HAPPINESS WILL CARRY HER THROUGH .

1811
01:35:05,987 --> 01:35:07,656
THEN CARMEL HAD A BABY , TOO ?

1812
01:35:07,756 --> 01:35:10,657
5 : 10 P.M. MRS. MEREDITH CAME TO SEE ME .

1813
01:35:10,759 --> 01:35:11,993
EXPECTED TEARS , HYSTERIA .

1814
01:35:12,093 --> 01:35:15,027
INSTEAD , ICY CONTROL AND A DOMINATING DESIRE

1815
01:35:15,163 --> 01:35:17,198
THAT THE GIRL 'S CONDITION BE KEPT SECRET .

1816
01:35:17,298 --> 01:35:19,200
I SHOULD HAVE MORE SYMPATHY WITH THE LADY

1817
01:35:19,300 --> 01:35:22,036
IF I DID NOT KNOW HOW SHE HERSELF HAS FEARED

1818
01:35:22,136 --> 01:35:24,072
AND REFUSED MOTHERHOOD .

1819
01:35:24,172 --> 01:35:25,907
WHAT CAN IT ALL MEAN ?

1820
01:35:26,007 --> 01:35:27,408
WHERE WERE YOU BORN , STELLA ?

1821
01:35:27,508 --> 01:35:29,210
- IN PARIS . - WHERE THEY TOOK CARMEL

1822
01:35:29,310 --> 01:35:31,312
BEFORE THEY CAME BACK WITH THEIR BABY .

1823
01:35:31,412 --> 01:35:33,314
Pam : BUT SURELY YOU DON 'T THINK- -

1824
01:35:33,414 --> 01:35:35,083
I THINK MARY ADOPTED CARMEL 'S CHILD ,

1825
01:35:35,183 --> 01:35:37,385
GAVE HER A HOME AND A NAME ON THE CONDITION

1826
01:35:37,485 --> 01:35:38,719
CARMEL NEVER CAME BACK HERE .

1827
01:35:38,819 --> 01:35:41,622
SHE COULDN 'T LIVE UP TO IT . SHE HAD TO BE NEAR HER BABY .

1828
01:35:41,722 --> 01:35:42,923
BUT RICK , IT DOESN 'T FIT .

1829
01:35:43,023 --> 01:35:45,158
THE MIMOSA SCENT THAT COMES WITH THE GENTLE GHOST ,

1830
01:35:45,258 --> 01:35:48,259
THAT WAS MARY 'S SCENT . STELLA 'S FATHER TOLD HER .

1831
01:35:48,595 --> 01:35:49,029
NO .

1832
01:35:49,129 --> 01:35:52,230
NO , MY FATHER ONLY WROTE IT WAS MY MOTHER 'S SCENT .

1833
01:35:53,000 --> 01:35:54,735
I 'M CARMEL 'S CHILD .

1834
01:35:54,835 --> 01:35:57,535
STELLA , DON 'T MIND TOO MUCH .

1835
01:35:58,338 --> 01:35:58,872
MIND ?

1836
01:35:58,972 --> 01:36:00,974
CAN 'T YOU SEE WHAT IT 'S DONE FOR ME ?

1837
01:36:01,074 --> 01:36:03,676
ALWAYS THERE 'S BEEN SOMETHING FIGHTING IN ME ,

1838
01:36:03,776 --> 01:36:05,712
SOMETHING THAT COULDN 'T BE CALM

1839
01:36:05,812 --> 01:36:07,714
AND COLD LIKE MARY .

1840
01:36:07,814 --> 01:36:09,282
I CAN BE MYSELF NOW .

1841
01:36:09,382 --> 01:36:12,483
THAT 'S WHAT SHE 'S WAITED ALL THESE YEARS TO TELL YOU .

1842
01:36:13,118 --> 01:36:15,686
OH , MOTHER , NOW I KNOW !

1843
01:36:16,989 --> 01:36:19,523
( Carmel laughing )

1844
01:36:26,398 --> 01:36:28,267
SHE 'S HAPPY NOW .

1845
01:36:28,367 --> 01:36:30,169
THE SCENT 'S GONE .

1846
01:36:30,269 --> 01:36:32,802
SHE WON 'T CRY ANYMORE .

1847
01:36:33,104 --> 01:36:34,839
SHE 'S GONE FOREVER .

1848
01:36:34,939 --> 01:36:36,742
WILL YOU COME BACK TO MY HOUSE NOW ?

1849
01:36:36,842 --> 01:36:39,344
- PLEASE , STELLA . - COME ALONG , DARLING .

1850
01:36:39,444 --> 01:36:41,811
ALL RIGHT .

1851
01:36:45,383 --> 01:36:47,786
GET HER OUT THROUGH THE NURSERY , QUICK !

1852
01:36:47,886 --> 01:36:49,620
- WHAT IS IT , THE COLD ? - GO ON , PAM !

1853
01:36:49,720 --> 01:36:52,856
- WHAT ARE YOU GOING TO DO ? ! - HELP STELLA , PLEASE .

1854
01:37:04,735 --> 01:37:06,637
MARY MEREDITH ,

1855
01:37:06,737 --> 01:37:09,170
WHERE ARE YOU ?

1856
01:37:13,110 --> 01:37:16,177
IT 'S TIME SOMEBODY FACED THAT ICY RAGE OF YOURS .

1857
01:37:17,981 --> 01:37:19,516
WHAT DO YOU WANT ?

1858
01:37:19,616 --> 01:37:22,183
IT 'S STELLA , ISN 'T IT ?

1859
01:37:31,595 --> 01:37:33,363
IT 'S TOO LATE , MARY .

1860
01:37:33,463 --> 01:37:33,596
YOU SEE ,

1861
01:37:33,696 --> 01:37:35,131
WE 'RE ON TO YOU NOW .

1862
01:37:35,231 --> 01:37:37,634
YOU TOLD CARMEL TO CLEAR OUT AND LEAVE HER BABY ,

1863
01:37:37,734 --> 01:37:39,368
BUT MEREDITH WOULDN 'T STAND FOR IT .

1864
01:37:39,468 --> 01:37:41,471
AND TO SPITE THEM , YOU TRIED TO KILL THEIR CHILD ,

1865
01:37:41,571 --> 01:37:44,540
AND INSTEAD WENT HURTLING OVER THE CLIFF YOURSELF .

1866
01:37:44,640 --> 01:37:47,909
GIVES YOUR SAINTLY LEGEND RATHER A BLACK EYE , DOESN 'T IT ?

1867
01:37:49,645 --> 01:37:52,848
OH , SO YOU DON 'T LIKE THE SOUND OF LAUGHTER , DO YOU ?

1868
01:37:52,948 --> 01:37:55,849
BUT THAT 'S ALL YOU 'LL GET FROM NOW ON .

1869
01:37:59,455 --> 01:38:02,356
I SHOULD THINK YOU 'D BE ON YOUR WAY NOW .

1870
01:38:02,524 --> 01:38:03,659
WE 'VE HAD ENOUGH .

1871
01:38:03,759 --> 01:38:05,528
WE 'RE NOT FRIGHTENED OF YOU ANYMORE .

1872
01:38:05,628 --> 01:38:08,595
FROM NOW ON THIS HOUSE IS FOR THE LIVING !

1873
01:38:21,443 --> 01:38:23,011
( knocking )

1874
01:38:23,111 --> 01:38:25,845
Pam : RICK , ARE YOU ALL RIGHT ?

1875
01:38:27,182 --> 01:38:29,849
Stella : LET ME IN , RICK !

1876
01:38:30,718 --> 01:38:32,720
- OH , RICK ! - YOU ALL RIGHT , FITZGERALD ?

1877
01:38:32,820 --> 01:38:35,423
YES , FINE . SHE 'S GONE , STELLA .

1878
01:38:35,523 --> 01:38:36,290
LOOK !

1879
01:38:36,390 --> 01:38:39,391
HE 'D NEVER GO NEAR THOSE STAIRS BEFORE .

1880
01:38:40,761 --> 01:38:41,929
BOBBY 'LL BE BACK TOMORROW .

1881
01:38:42,029 --> 01:38:45,097
I THINK WE 'LL BE HAVING OTHER PLANS FOR BOBBY .

1882
01:38:46,333 --> 01:38:48,102
YOU 'RE STILL SHAKING , RICK .

1883
01:38:48,202 --> 01:38:49,669
WELL , I 'VE HAD A NARROW ESCAPE .

1884
01:38:49,769 --> 01:38:52,671
SHE MIGHT HAVE BEEN MY MOTHER-IN-LAW .

